{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist","id":1560488,"title":"How Did The Sabbat Exist?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-09T11:57:20-07:00","id":1560488,"title":"How Did The Sabbat Exist?","content":"A thought has just occurred to me regarding the Sabbat's actions, and how they synergize with the Paths of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Upon retrospect, I realize that nearly all PoE's forbid the act casual murder, while the ones who actually do permit it demand that you must have a higher purpose beyond simple desire.<br /> <br /> So, how is it that the sect of blood crazed, vampiric berserkers, who bury people in mass graves and commit every sort of atrocity you can imagine are able to get away with these kinds of acts?<br /> <br /> Even among those who have adopted a PoE, shouldn't the whole sect consist of Wights by this point?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T13:22:41-07:00","id":1560492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist#post1560488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A thought has just occurred to me regarding the Sabbat's actions, and how they synergize with the Paths of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> Upon retrospect, I realize that nearly all PoE's forbid the act casual murder, while the ones who actually do permit it demand that you must have a higher purpose beyond simple desire.<br /> <br /> So, how is it that the sect of blood crazed, vampiric berserkers, who bury people in mass graves and commit every sort of atrocity you can imagine are able to get away with these kinds of acts?<br /> <br /> Even among those who have adopted a PoE, shouldn't the whole sect consist of Wights by this point?</div> </div> </div> </div>So the thing is, most Sabbat vampires were just very low humanity. In a given pack, in fact probably less than 25% of Sabbat members were on a Path. Some clans were more likely to have members on Paths, for example Tzimisce, Lasombra, Followers of Skulls, were more likely to be on Paths, but then other clans like the Brujah, Gangrel, Nosferatu, Malkavians, etc, most of those members were just low humanity. Giving up your humanity and embracing a Path is actually really difficult.<br /> <br /> Still compared to the number of Camarilla members on Paths of Enlightenment, the Sabbat absolutely had a heck of a lot more. Ultimately though the Paths were notable but they weren't a defining aspect of Sabbat existence until 5E where it seems that most (all?) Sabbat vampires are now on a Path. It's also worth noting that for many Paths, killing is perfectly okay. The Path member may need a reason to do so, but for most Sabbat, killing as social activity to increase the bonds with their pact mates or sect would be reason enough. <br /> <br /> Still though, yeah, most Sabbat vampires were fairly low humanity or low Path rating and hovering close to wrightdom. It's just what happens when you have a sect whose members choose to frequently feed the Beast.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T14:47:19-07:00","id":1560495,"title":"","content":"There probably is a lot of sabbat who goes wight but it's not like they'd have any trouble just embracing someone else. Keeping themselves stocked with kindred is their deal. Sabbat is quantity Camarilla is quality. Camarilla would never understand it, they spend years handpicking the most likely candidate to succeed, spend a few more years sucking up to the prince to please please let me embrace, then spend several more years teaching their pick everything he needs to know and hope he works out.<br /> <br /> Sabbat meanwhile: 'that guy looks free get 'im'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T16:11:16-07:00","id":1560497,"title":"","content":"Let's look at some of the more popular Sabbat Paths and see where they'd be. I'll be using the Revised era Paths of The Guide to the Sabbat. I know other editions have different Hierarchy of Sins.<br /> <br /> Path of Caine - I don't see any mention about not killing mortals. So that's an easy Path for the routine mass murdering Sabbat, and we know this is a popular Path for the sect.<br /> <br /> Path of Cathari - Prohibitions on &quot;arbitrary killing&quot; at level 2 (quite serious) and &quot;impassioned killing&quot; at level 6. If we excuse the killings done as part of the Auctoritas Ritae (like Blood Bath, Blood Beast, and Palla Grande) as not arbitrary, most followers can probably be at normal Path levels as Camarilla vampires on Humanity. They'd just need to avoid routine &quot;needless&quot; killing of mortals the rest of the time.<br /> <br /> Path of Death and the Soul - &quot;<i>Failing</i> to kill when useful&quot; (Useful meaning useful to one's study of death) is a level 6 sin. &quot;Showing compassion&quot; is a level 3 sin. &quot;Killing <i>without studying death afterward</i>&quot; is a level 2 sin. This is probably where the difficulty comes from as someone attempting to &quot;study&quot; at a Blood Feast or during a Sabbat murder hobo crusade is probably hard to do. &quot;Needlessly preventing a death&quot; is a level 1 sin. This path doesn't have a problem with killing mortals. The real complication is the need to &quot;study&quot; it afterwards. This will create some odd behavior, but should not present too much a trouble. It's just more likely a Path adherent will prefer isolated &quot;intimate&quot; murders where she can study the effects rather than killing sprees.<br /> <br /> Path of Evil Revelations - There's no conflicts here at all.<br /> <br /> Path of the Feral Heart - This Path is one that will have some trouble. Being &quot;overly cruel&quot; is a level 7 sin. &quot;Killing without need&quot; is a level 4 sin. &quot;Killing a creature other than for survival&quot; is a level 2 sin. Cainites on this Path will definitely have problems. This is the meaner version of the Path of Harmony of first edition. That edition made clear most Path adherents were Country Gangrel, many of whom were of Native American stock, who were Loyalists and nomad packs. These Sabbat were probably politically important in early Sabbat history when first arriving in North America, but were probably the big losers of the Sabbat Civil Wars as the Lasombra and Tzimisce (and others) became coven based packs in cities. In a Sabbat chronicle, the followers of this Path probably have little to do with most of the sect except for some old vestigial loyalties (probably due to the vaulderie). Instead, they probably just hang out with other members of their Path and interpret ritae like the Blood Feast very loosely. They are the Sabbat one could most easily justifying defecting from the Sabbat en masse, perhaps joining the anarchs or even the Camarilla. There's a reason Revised edition purged most of these when they eliminated much of the diversity within the sect in order to turn it into the Sword of Caine masturbatory fantasy of the Ultra-conservatives.<br /> <br /> Path of Honorable Accord - &quot;Killing without reason&quot; is a level 2 sin. Again, the Auctoritas Ritae probably provide a &quot;reason&quot; for killing so the knights can participate without lowering their Path ratings, but they are probably the least murderous Path outside of Feral Heart/Harmony. As long as they mostly hang out in their own packs, they can probably get by. Being in packs with the muder hobos would probably hurt their path ratings immensely.<br /> <br /> Path of Lilith - I'll note this is not actually a Sabbat path. The original version comes from Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand which is about the Tal'mahe'Ra. Lilith worshippers won't do well in a sect devoted to Caine as the followers of the Dark Mother despise Caine. &quot;Killing a living or unliving being&quot; is a level 4 sin. The Bahari will do well outside the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> Path of Power and the Inner Voice - A classic Sabbat path, and one that many (most?) of its leaders follow. No prohibitions against murder here. &quot;<i>Failing</i> to kill when it's in your interests&quot; is a level 5 sin. While individual unifiers may not kill a lot, there's not much problem if they do. They're just more likely to kill for a reason.<br /> <br /> Path of Metamorphosis - This is pulled from the Revised Vampire: the Masquerade Corebook. This is another dark Path. No prohibitions against killing. Instead &quot;<i>Refusing</i> to kill when knowledge may be gained from it&quot; is a level 6 sin. &quot;Considering the needs of others&quot; is a level 4 sin. &quot;Exhibiying compassion for others&quot; is a level 1 sin. These vampires are sick.<br /> <br /> So there's actually not much problem here.<br /> <br /> The Paths of the Feral Heart and Honorable Accord are the only ones who likely would a problem with most stereotypical Sabbat behavior. Followers of these paths probably do their best to stay away from most other Sabbat. If we assume Feral Heart/Harmony followers are those Native American Country Gangrel in wilderness nomad packs, they are effectively their own sect with limited ties to other Sabbat. Honorable Accord presents much more of a challenge. They'd probably have been destroyed long ago except for their fanatical loyalty to the Code of Milan. I imagine they mostly hang out with themselves and avoid other Sabbat except as part of the auctoritas ritae or their duties as paladins/templars, inquisitors, or their own packs. I imagine they recruit other newly Sabbat whenever they see a new one with potential and quickly try to recruit one.<br /> <br /> The Paths of Cathari and Power and the Inner Voice are probably only so-so as murder hobos. They likely won't engage in routine murder, but have plentiful of meaningful homicides. They probably work well with the above paths as they know they may need help at some time from the real sickos. However, they can usually fit in well with them.<br /> <br /> The Paths of Caine, Death and the Soul, Evil Revelation, and Metamorphosis are probably where most of the murder hobos come from. Nothing really stops them from killing at any time, and many will justify killing just in order to not sin against their Paths.<br /> <br /> I imagine early on, Sabbat who were on Paths were mostly those on more humane paths. But as the sect grew to identify themselves with radical notions of freedom, it encouraged the morally worst shitbags to justify their awful behavior in the guise of twisted Paths, and they gradually took over the sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T16:42:50-07:00","id":1560498,"title":"","content":"I don't think you can seriously look at the Sabbat and it's functional viability and ignore the Viniculum's impact on its members. While the Sabbat likes to claim the Vaulderie frees its members from the tyranny of Blood Bonds... it does so simply by replacing the power of one vampire to exert radical control on another by forcing a weaker level of influence spread out among the rest of the local Sabbat. Unless a pack falls apart very quickly, holding a Vaulderie as often as the book indicates most packs do means the majority of members of a pack are going to be at 7+ Viniculum ratings towards the other pack members. So there is a lot of supernatural peer pressure to interpret Paths in a fashion that lets Sabbat members cooperate.<br /> <br /> Since Feral Heart and Honorable Accord got singled out above me, Feral Heart doesn't negate the idea of &quot;survival&quot; being added by working with your pack and thus killing for survival can mean killing for the good of the pack instead of just for immediate sustenance. &quot;For the good of my pack&quot; is as viable as a reason for a Knight to do pretty much anything that might otherwise cause problems for their Path rating.<br /> <br /> This is also a reason I don't like just looking at the sin lists. The Paths have deeper write-ups - and especially the Ethics lists - that help put those charts in context so STs and players can judge what should and shouldn't count. Feral Heart and Honorable Accord both heavily stress the importance of group cohesion (Feral Heart is more pack focused, Honorable Accord more institution focused) in how they're actually written. Adding that context in addition to the Viniculum means they're not nearly as hard to have in packs as they can seem if you just look at the sin lists. Both Paths also have a pretty big leeway between &quot;You as a Path follower shouldn't do this,&quot; and, &quot;You as a Path follower need to stop others from doing this.&quot; Beyond those two Paths, the Paths most associated with the Sabbat tend towards personal actions over demands on the group. There's very little that can't be solved by, &quot;whatever floats your boat as long as you don't force me to participate,&quot; when it comes to balancing group dynamics when the Paths are involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-09T18:54:04-07:00","id":1560502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560497#post1560497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So there's actually not much problem here.<br /> <br /> The Paths of the Feral Heart and Honorable Accord are the only ones who likely would a problem with most stereotypical Sabbat behavior. Followers of these paths probably do their best to stay away from most other Sabbat. If we assume Feral Heart/Harmony followers are those Native American Country Gangrel in wilderness nomad packs, they are effectively their own sect with limited ties to other Sabbat. Honorable Accord presents much more of a challenge. They'd probably have been destroyed long ago except for their fanatical loyalty to the Code of Milan. I imagine they mostly hang out with themselves and avoid other Sabbat except as part of the auctoritas ritae or their duties as paladins/templars, inquisitors, or their own packs. I imagine they recruit other newly Sabbat whenever they see a new one with potential and quickly try to recruit one.<br /> <br /> The Paths of Cathari and Power and the Inner Voice are probably only so-so as murder hobos. They likely won't engage in routine murder, but have plentiful of meaningful homicides. They probably work well with the above paths as they know they may need help at some time from the real sickos. However, they can usually fit in well with them.<br /> <br /> The Paths of Caine, Death and the Soul, Evil Revelation, and Metamorphosis are probably where most of the murder hobos come from. Nothing really stops them from killing at any time, and many will justify killing just in order to not sin against their Paths.<br /> <br /> I imagine early on, Sabbat who were on Paths were mostly those on more humane paths. But as the sect grew to identify themselves with radical notions of freedom, it encouraged the morally worst shitbags to justify their awful behavior in the guise of twisted Paths, and they gradually took over the sect.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I believe the Gentleman Gamer brought up the idea that the rest of the pack would be coerced into adopting the same Path as the pack priest. If for no other reason than to make their job of acting as the spiritual guide easier to fulfill. If you've got 4 members in the pack who all follow a different moral philosophy, that's going to make administering to their spiritual education nearly impossible.<br /> <br /> So if the whole pack is following the Path of Death and the Soul, then studying opportunities become a lot easier to manage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560497#post1560497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Path of Evil Revelations - There's no conflicts here at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but this path involves demon worship, which even the Sabbat agree is a no-no. They'll sick the inquisitors on you if they find out you follow it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560497#post1560497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Path of Lilith - I'll note this is not actually a Sabbat path. The original version comes from Dirty Secrets of the Black Hand which is about the Tal'mahe'Ra. Lilith worshippers won't do well in a sect devoted to Caine as the followers of the Dark Mother despise Caine. &quot;Killing a living or unliving being&quot; is a level 4 sin. The Bahari will do well outside the Sabbat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>While I know the &quot;True&quot; Black Hand are the ones pulling the strings, I don't consider them Sabbat; in large part due to their true intention of selling out their own kind to curry favor with the Antedeluvians.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-10T08:26:11-07:00","id":1560522,"title":"","content":"The interesting question is just how accurate you want perceptions of the Sabbat as mass murderers on a regular basis to be: I tend to run with the notion that the Sabbat are those vampires committed to an idea of themselves as proudly inhuman and casual killers in consequence, but as being less often caught in a situation where the lunatics are in charge of the asylum than quite a lot of the World of Darkness might think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-10T11:27:02-07:00","id":1560530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Atticus Cleanclaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560522#post1560522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The interesting question is just how accurate you want perceptions of the Sabbat as mass murderers on a regular basis to be: I tend to run with the notion that the Sabbat are those vampires committed to an idea of themselves as proudly inhuman and casual killers in consequence, but as being less often caught in a situation where the lunatics are in charge of the asylum than quite a lot of the World of Darkness might think.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, they're modeled after the catholic church, and the term <i>&quot;Sabbath&quot;</i> makes me think of witches having blood soaked orgies with animals in the woods at night.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I like envisioning the Sabbat as an utterly monstrous horror show. Unfortunately, the mechanics surrounding one's Beast make that kind of hard to pull off, without hand waving it as you just being very low on the Path / Humanity rating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T07:49:05-07:00","id":1560545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560530#post1560530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, they're modeled after the catholic church, and the term <i>&quot;Sabbath&quot;</i> makes me think of witches having blood soaked orgies with animals in the woods at night.<br /> <br /> So yeah, I like envisioning the Sabbat as an utterly monstrous horror show. Unfortunately, the mechanics surrounding one's Beast make that kind of hard to pull off, without hand waving it as you just being very low on the Path / Humanity rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clanbook Lasombra Revised explains the reason for all of this in its narrative. Pg 25 explains why the sect is called the Sabbat, and pgs 28-29 explains why the Sect is modeled after the church. The summary is that the first was using human superstition to flaunt themselves, and the latter was because Cainites get bored, so bureaucracy is a fun way to keep them engaged, while also enacting a bit of heresy and pomp.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T10:03:01-07:00","id":1560548,"title":"","content":"Part of the problem is that the Sabbat has never really been consistent in what it is. By Revised and thus in V20 it's taken on what's probably its most common iterating in use (because it's actually a functional organization at that point, even if still limited by avoiding too many additional retcons), but even in 1e the Sabbat was being adjusted in what it's purpose in the setting really was: from ultra-evil vampires who were both psychotic killers and somehow a functional group, to champions of the inhumane but still driven by a coherent and understandable if alien ideology. The later part of 1e, throughout the entire runs of both 2e and Rev, there was an ongoing process in trying to explain why the ultra-evil version of them could exist at least in some areas and times, but the organization was something that could rationally exist in the larger setting. Leading to contradictions and retcons to address them.<br /> <br /> You can see the influence of that development process on how Requiem instituted it's three many antagonists to its vampires: Belial's Brood (groups of seemingly young vampires punching way above their weight class doing lots of crazy evil things while somehow being cockroaches that keep coming back no matter how many you kill off and how little sense it makes for them to function beyond a small group level), the VII (purposefully vague ideological fanatics that have it in for the normal vampires for some reason), and the Strix (something deeply connected to vampires, but not truly vampires themselves, that represent a constant boogeyman to the kindred). One group becomes unwieldy when trying to embody so many setting functions at once, so Requiem went with the approach of dividing the narrative rules up between more antagonist factions.<br /> <br /> But VtM (well at least pre-V5) worked to keep all three concepts in one group. That's why trying to treat the Sabbat as a whole as filling one of those roles doesn't really work out; even if you're keeping to the early material. The Sabbat was iterated over time to be an institution that could have individual groups within it to be the specific Sabbat you want encountered in your game, even if they're not the whole group; letting the institution be more functional and coherent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\u2615","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T10:19:38-07:00","id":1560549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560548#post1560548\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can see the influence of that development process on how Requiem instituted it's three many antagonists to its vampires: Belial's Brood (groups of seemingly young vampires punching way above their weight class doing lots of crazy evil things while somehow being cockroaches that keep coming back no matter how many you kill off and how little sense it makes for them to function beyond a small group level),</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> From what I understand of it, Belial's Brood is not some mundane faction as we typically understand it. They don't hold recruitment drives or pass out fliers to people.<br /> <br /> They are a spiritual phenomenon that occurs when a vampire finally gets sick of pretending to be human, and actively wishes to embrace their monstrosity in all its glory.<br /> <br /> Once that happens, they may begin to hear the psychic Call, guiding them to seek out like minded individuals.<br /> <br /> This is why the Brood continues to resurface again and again, no matter how thorough the other covenants are in eradicating their numbers. So long as there are vampires who chafe under the restrictions of Humanity, there will always be new converts to reform the sect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T12:06:04-07:00","id":1560554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560530#post1560530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the term <i>&quot;Sabbath&quot;</i> makes me think of witches having blood soaked orgies with animals in the woods at night.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you talking about that specifically in this kind of context, or are you unfamiliar with the fact that the Sabbath is the mandated day of rest in Judaism, Christianity, and Islam?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T13:50:24-07:00","id":1560555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560497#post1560497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">L<br /> Honorable Accord presents much more of a challenge. They'd probably have been destroyed long ago except for their fanatical loyalty to the Code of Milan. I imagine they mostly hang out with themselves and avoid other Sabbat except as part of the auctoritas ritae or their duties as paladins/templars, inquisitors, or their own packs. I imagine they recruit other newly Sabbat whenever they see a new one with potential and quickly try to recruit one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I dont think thats really true, nothing in their code prohibits a broad variety of truly vile actions and thats assuming a high path rating.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T13:59:51-07:00","id":1560556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560554#post1560554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Are you talking about that specifically in this kind of context, or are you unfamiliar with the fact that the Sabbath is the mandated day of rest in Judaism, Christianity, and Islam?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Family's catholic on my dad's side. I'm aware that 'the sabbath' is the holy weekend of rest and prayer. When doing any sort of work is punishable by death.<br /> <br /> But that sounds boring, so I'll stick with my satanic, goat fucking witches.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","user":"DarkKing","date":". 06-11-2026, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T14:01:35-07:00","id":1560557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560549#post1560549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I understand of it, Belial's Brood is not some mundane faction as we typically understand it. They don't hold recruitment drives or pass out fliers to people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda? They're difficult to understand because they were heavily reworked twice (once with their initial source book that added a lot of what you're saying, and again in VtR 2e to adjust all of that into the changes made in that edition).<br /> <br /> The reason why it's impossible to fully get rid of them is largely irrelevant to my point though. Most vampires have no idea, they just know that the Brood keep coming back in new iterations no matter how much they're put down. My point is that the Brood serve as the &quot;murder hobo&quot; antagonists for VtR. They're there to roll into town, flaunt their inhumanity, cause chaos, and get killed by the PCs; one of the narrative roles the Sabbat is meant to play for Camarilla and Anarch based games. My point was to illustrate how the VtR creators (who were largely VtM Revised creators) opted to split out the narrative roles the Sabbat was meant to accomplish so it was easier to give each role its own breathing room (and also the playable aspect getting put into the Covenants as well). Which is all to make the larger point that the Sabbat is messy in its development history which leads to a lot of the issues with how they function (or don't) based on your needs for your own games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T14:05:36-07:00","id":1560558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560557#post1560557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kinda? They're difficult to understand because they were heavily reworked twice (once with their initial source book that added a lot of what you're saying, and again in VtR 2e to adjust all of that into the changes made in that edition).<br /> <br /> The reason why it's impossible to fully get rid of them is largely irrelevant to my point though. Most vampires have no idea, they just know that the Brood keep coming back in new iterations no matter how much they're put down. My point is that the Brood serve as the &quot;murder hobo&quot; antagonists for VtR. They're there to roll into town, flaunt their inhumanity, cause chaos, and get killed by the PCs; one of the narrative roles the Sabbat is meant to play for Camarilla and Anarch based games. My point was to illustrate how the VtR creators (who were largely VtM Revised creators) opted to split out the narrative roles the Sabbat was meant to accomplish so it was easier to give each role its own breathing room (and also the playable aspect getting put into the Covenants as well). Which is all to make the larger point that the Sabbat is messy in its development history which leads to a lot of the issues with how they function (or don't) based on your needs for your own games.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes sense. The Sabbat did seem to be a walking contradiction of itself, where they tried to be multiple, conflicting things simultaneously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T21:16:28-07:00","id":1560564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560502#post1560502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the Gentleman Gamer brought up the idea that the rest of the pack would be coerced into adopting the same Path as the pack priest. If for no other reason than to make their job of acting as the spiritual guide easier to fulfill. If you've got 4 members in the pack who all follow a different moral philosophy, that's going to make administering to their spiritual education nearly impossible.</div> </div> </div> </div>As an ST, that's how I usually organize Sabbat packs in chronicles because it makes things coherent. Some packs do have other purposes as an organizing principle, but its members tend to have compatible paths that don't present problems for other members. The only time there are packs with wildly different paths are when the survivors of war parties and the like have to temporarily pack together simply to have a pack, and they usually disperse quickly once they are back to safety and can find more compatible packs.<br /> <br /> I think packs whose members have wildly different Paths of Enlightenment are PC packs because players want to play wildly different characters and are relying on real life camaraderie oft he players and ST indulgence to smooth over the difficulties. From a game perspective, that's not a problem. You want all the players to have fun. However, it is poor precedent when designing NPC packs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T21:27:01-07:00","id":1560565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560555#post1560555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dont think thats really true, nothing in their code prohibits a broad variety of truly vile actions and thats assuming a high path rating.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can do lots of things and not violate the Paths as written, but the no killing without reason could create problems if the pack is lax about it. Associating with the dishonorable might also cause problems, but at least that is a level 8 sin, so only those truly devoted to the Path have to worry about it. I might be reading too much into them having Conscience instead of Conviction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T21:51:16-07:00","id":1560568,"title":"","content":"There are also fairly function Path &quot;clusters&quot; that are simple to have in the same pack because they tend to engender some level of shared tactics or philosophy. Power and the Inner Voice and Honorable Accord pair fairly well in the tactics regard (enough that they were effectively retconned by DAV Rev to have come from the same original Road of Kings) with a ductus and priest on PatIV and the other members as their loyal knights is a very functional approach as they compliment each other fairly well. Similarly &quot;scholarly&quot; Paths like Metamorphosis and Death and the Soul can work well together as both Paths are going to share a lot of common practical necessities to facilitate their studies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T22:20:01-07:00","id":1560569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560565#post1560565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can do lots of things and not violate the Paths as written, but the no killing without reason could create problems if the pack is lax about it. Associating with the dishonorable might also cause problems, but at least that is a level 8 sin, so only those truly devoted to the Path have to worry about it. I might be reading too much into them having Conscience instead of Conviction.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sabbat typically has a reason to kill, its notable how loose that statement is. As long as their is a reason, not is it one we'd find acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-11T22:44:32-07:00","id":1560571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560568#post1560568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are also fairly function Path &quot;clusters&quot; that are simple to have in the same pack because they tend to engender some level of shared tactics or philosophy. Power and the Inner Voice and Honorable Accord pair fairly well in the tactics regard (enough that they were effectively retconned by DAV Rev to have come from the same original Road of Kings) with a ductus and priest on PatIV and the other members as their loyal knights is a very functional approach as they compliment each other fairly well. Similarly &quot;scholarly&quot; Paths like Metamorphosis and Death and the Soul can work well together as both Paths are going to share a lot of common practical necessities to facilitate their studies.</div> </div> </div> </div>I remain skeptical. Since the <b>Path of Honorable Accord</b> believes that it is their moral duty as superior beings to take on the role of stewards of humanity. They see humans as being too weak and foolish to be entrusted with self governance, so they must take up the reigns of leadership. <br /> <br /> While the <b>Path of Power and Inner Voice</b> control their Beast through becoming absolute tyrants. Everyone and everything must submit to their iron fisted authority, or be destroyed. They are guided purely by self interest, and have zero regard for the suffering of those around them, so long as they get what they want out of (un)life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T00:00:46-07:00","id":1560572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560571#post1560571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the <b>Path of Honorable Accord</b> believes that it is their moral duty as superior beings to take on the role of stewards of humanity. They see humans as being too weak and foolish to be entrusted with self governance, so they must take up the reigns of leadership.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where are you getting this? It's not a core ethic or tenet of the Path. It might be how Camarilla and Independent vampires on it (as of V20 it's considered one of the more common Paths outside of the Sabbat that isn't linked to specific Clans/Bloodlines) justify their actions, but the Sabbat followers are consistently seen as not caring in the slightest about what humans do with themselves. Humans only matter to them as far as it matters to them fulfilling their duties, obligations, and ensuring they don't sully their honor. If a Knight makes a promise to a human, they'll keep it, but that's because they don't break their promises, not because humans are a concern to them. V20's write up of the Path directly compares the Path's view on humans is that of a knight to their horse or hounds <i>at best</i>. Humans are tools... and knights keep their tools in good condition sword or beast... not beings of value to guide into proper governance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While the <b>Path of Power and Inner Voice</b> control their Beast through becoming absolute tyrants. Everyone and everything must submit to their iron fisted authority, or be destroyed. They are guided purely by self interest, and have zero regard for the suffering of those around them, so long as they get what they want out of (un)life. </div> </div> </div>And they have the nickname of &quot;Unifiers&quot; for a reason... they need to be very smart and charismatic to be successful. It's important to note that Power and the Inner Voice is explicit in not tolerating adherents that try to deflect blame for their mistakes onto others; if they can't do things well they will fail to follow the Path. Their self-interest creates stability and order in their domains, and the Knights fight specifically for the order that well run domains entail. Knights don't care if their leader is a complete egoist as long as the Unifiers understand that the best way to keep the Knights happy is to do their job as a leader to create functional systems of control over the local areas.<br /> <br /> Sure, if there was no room for conflict there would be no reason for distinct Paths. The point is that these are Paths with complimentary structures: Unifiers lead with ruthless efficiency, and Knights are loyal to successful leaders in the brutal world of vampire existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T00:19:54-07:00","id":1560573,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560572#post1560572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where are you getting this? It's not a core ethic or tenet of the Path. It might be how Camarilla and Independent vampires on it (as of V20 it's considered one of the more common Paths outside of the Sabbat that isn't linked to specific Clans/Bloodlines) justify their actions, but the Sabbat followers are consistently seen as not caring in the slightest about what humans do with themselves. Humans only matter to them as far as it matters to them fulfilling their duties, obligations, and ensuring they don't sully their honor. If a Knight makes a promise to a human, they'll keep it, but that's because they don't break their promises, not because humans are a concern to them. V20's write up of the Path directly compares the Path's view on humans is that of a knight to their horse or hounds <i>at best</i>. Humans are tools... and knights keep their tools in good condition sword or beast... not beings of value to guide into proper governance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems you're right, I misremembered it.<br /> <br /> But that's weird; I could have sworn there was a path that worked along the line of humans being too stupid to govern themselves. If it wasn't Honorable Accord, then I don't know which one it could have been.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-12T00:33:51-07:00","id":1560574,"title":"","content":"That view is present in the DA Road of Kings... not necessarily in terms of humans being inept, but simply lesser. Scions of the Road are required to ensure that the humans within their domains see them as fair and just (even if potentially dangerous and forceful) rulers that make sure everything is safe and prosperous. Humans should want to live in the domains of the Scions because they're well run and successful, rather then being slaves to vampires in the guises of blood-gods (something Noddist lore says is a command from Caine himself on how vampires are to use their superior natures to humans, and failure to abide this order is supposedly why Caine destroyed Enoch).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-15T22:51:17-07:00","id":1560649,"title":"","content":"For me it all sums up to the idea that the Sabbat is many things not just out of design inconsistencies, but as a result of being a big organization.<br /> <br /> Anything that's said about the Sabbat is true with a lot of caveats, which means it's also not true if taken to extremes:<br /> <br /> They are *not* murder hobos. Or numerous. Or evil. Or inhuman. Or on Paths. Or functional. Or dysfunctional. Or what-have-you. They *can*.<br /> <br /> Most depictions add the problem of unreliable authors. The original depiction itself was ostensibly a rumor running on a Camarilla city with no real contact with the sect whatsoever. The more the author of a given text has actual contact with the Sabbat, and reason to not be just messing with the reader, the more nuanced they get.<br /> <br /> So the main reasons it all works is:<br /> <br /> 1. The Sabbat doesn't nearly kill all that many mortals in a daily basis, the existence of *Lost Boys* style murder hobo packs notwithstanding.<br /> <br /> 2. Most of the actual killings do meet the Paths of those involved.<br /> <br /> 3. There is room for errors, from members that don't attend to Ritae as frequently as they should to Path Followers that aren't exactly a pristine success example.<br /> <br /> 4. Everything is context-adapted. Of all the things the Sabbat can be, what it will actually be depends mostly on what's feasible at a given place and time.<br /> <br /> If you want to conciliate the idea of frequent blood-soaked orgies at night with a functional Sabbat, all you need is for the local Sabbat to exist in a context where it's feasible, which includes that those orgies fit the PoE actually present.<br /> <br /> But if you really want to keep the headcanon of the Sabbat being universally like that, then truth is that your headcanon doesn't work with many PoE.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-16T03:45:11-07:00","id":1560653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560649#post1560649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most depictions add the problem of unreliable authors. The original depiction itself was ostensibly a rumor running on a Camarilla city with no real contact with the sect whatsoever. The more the author of a given text has actual contact with the Sabbat, and reason to not be just messing with the reader, the more nuanced they get.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, I forgot about the unreliable narrator aspect of the books.<br /> <br /> It makes a lot more sense now, if we consider that stories of the Sabbat's behavior are greatly exaggerated, or being used as propaganda.<br /> <br /> These days, people usually aren't in the habit of showing respect to one's enemies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T22:05:10-07:00","id":1560742,"title":"","content":"To be fair, the morality system up to including the version presented in V20 always required a character to find new levels of evil to sink to in order to risk degeneration. The NPC's who you'd hear about going into Wassail always seemed to be elders who had been ground down by age, because once your Morality gets low enough, feeling anything when you kill stops making sense or being a factor.<br /> <br /> Vampire: the Requiem did a really good job in its second edition of making a game mechanic out of ennui being the vampire's biggest enemy, with breaking points coming from siring a child, outliving the last person you knew from your mortal days, seeing decade and century anniversaries from the night of your embrace, all stuff that aren't necessarily crimes against God and man, but that rub a character's nose in how far from human they've become in other aspects of their existence. V5's touchstone system draws inspiration from that, whether it succeeds or not, with the additional and appropriate (imo) risk of stains from using the Oblivion discipline to draw power from a force that's darker and hungrier than death itself.<br /> <br /> To get back to the point I meant to make, very few Sabbat probably have long enough unlives to fall to wassail. An elder who doesn't find a purpose to lock in on to give their immortality meaning is going to end up getting cannibalized by someone younger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T22:21:48-07:00","id":1560745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560742#post1560742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the morality system up to including the version presented in V20 always required a character to find new levels of evil to sink to in order to risk degeneration. The NPC's who you'd hear about going into Wassail always seemed to be elders who had been ground down by age, because once your Morality gets low enough, feeling anything when you kill stops making sense or being a factor.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Aye, it requires more extreme acts, but it also implies that you become more prone to committing those acts as well.<br /> <br /> If vampires can just reach a stopping point where they're like <i>&quot;no thanks, I'm good&quot;</i> with their Beast, then that cheapens the threat it poses. Makes it sound more like a vampire is only at risk of becoming a Wight if they actively pursue that fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T01:29:53-07:00","id":1560747,"title":"","content":"The Sabbat gained a lot of detail and lore late in Revised that made it more compelling but also more realistic. <i>Guide to the Sabbat</i> filled in a lot of gaps, but <i>Caine's Chosen</i> and <i>Archons and Templars</i> provided a lot of information about the Black Hand and Sabbat Inquisition, and institutions such as the templars and paladins.<br /> <br /> When you add in the lore from <i>New York by Night</i> and <i>Mexico City by Night</i>, you get a lot of details about their history and the three civil wars which makes them so much more interesting as a group. They also help explain how everything hung together like it did.<br /> <br /> <i>Chaining the Beast</i> did a lot to make paths more plausible. Even as early as <i>Montreal by Night</i> (1996), though, you had things like the Path of Cathari becoming more spiritual and less &quot;LOL you're a sadist torturer&quot;. All of this stuff helped make the Sabbat more nuanced.<br /> <br /> <i>Montreal by Night </i>has some very iffy stuff now, in part because it was written at a time when White Wolf and Black Dog were still reacting to the whole Satanic panic thing, but it's also a fantastically evocative book and one of the best By Night books out there (probably my favourite, at least). It singlehandedly showed what the spiritual side of the Sabbat could be. <i>Mexico City by Night</i> really complements it, and i love the diversity of packs it includes. It shows how the packs are the heart of the Sword, and the Vaulderie is the thing that binds them together (that and the might of the Black Hand).<br /> <br /> <i>Caine's Chosen</i> hammers home how the Sabbat really is just an assortment of groups that came together at the end of the Anarch Revolt for various purposes (pp. 15\u201316, &quot;Roots &amp; Branches&quot;, <i>Caine's Chosen: The Black Hand</i>). This actually makes it resemble the large political parties in the US or UK, which are also broad coalitions. Some Conservatives are closer to Labour Party members than to each other, but they huddle together in big blocs for convenience, power, and tribalism. Sometimes politicians side with things they don't really believe in because they oppose the other side even more.<br /> <br /> Basically, I think there are plenty of reasons why the Sabbat survived, and its competing, diverse factions are actually a big part of that. It makes it adaptable, but it also gives Cainites the drive to go on\u2014even when they're not fighting the Camarilla, the fact they want to beat out the other factions keep them determined and driven in a way that prevents them from becoming complacent in the same the Camarilla does. They hang together not just out of the loyalty of the Vinculi, but also through sheer spite and perversity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Typo 06-19-2026, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T05:38:36-07:00","id":1560753,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560742#post1560742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, the morality system</div> </div> </div> </div>The important part is to understand what each of those systems do, that they're not trying to achieve the same goal or state the same thing, and if you think the problem is Wassail not being reachable, then you greatly missed the point.<br /> <br /> First of all, none of those are hard to balance, not really. And that's important because they're a tool for worldbuilding first. For a Vampire society of any kind to even work in the first place, you need a stable default, no matter if it is 3, 5 or 8. There is a point where most chars will fluctuate at, otherwise those who don't wouldn't stand out, and society itself would crumble anyway.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Up to V20, VtM Humanity is about the price of power and your willingness to pay it. It's the easier one to keep at any point you want and that's a design feature, not a failure.<br /> <br /> Here the unreliable narrator matters a lot, because the text repeats the spiel about degeneration being an inevitable curse as a deliberate red herring. Actually believing this is a staple of Kindred Society just because it help them to live with their choices. It's defensive hypocrisy.<br /> <br /> For the game, the point is to present the PCs with situations where risking degeneration is convenient, not to find excuses to make them roll. It's imperative that in the end every check for degeneration come from a deliberate decision the character can rationalize however they want, but they truly could have done different.<br /> <br /> And if that never risks Wassail, no prob either. In this context your level of Humanity is above all a character statement. It's you saying where, at least for now, you feel comfortable drawing the line. That stability helps grounding a char Humanity score in their characterization rather than luck.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Requiem 2nd ed Humanity is about connection, not morality. This is a nuance that shouldn't be lost, and is the reason you can get extra Bans to buy some Free Out of Prison cards in your Humanity track.<br /> <br /> A low Humanity Kindred has an easier time being an asshole without mechanical consequences, but this is not what's important to measure. A high Humanity vampire can be a Nazi, a low Humanity one can still believe in the sanctity of life, even if it doesn't have an emotional engagement anymore.<br /> <br /> Humanity here is under attack from your reality as nonhuman, and the risk is disconnection, to lose your ability to feel like you're a part of the crowd, regardless if you believe it or not, if it is an identity marker or merely an ambush tactic.<br /> <br /> The crux of it is the Touchstone system as it works in Requiem, because the key dynamic isn't what causes a Degeneration Roll, but how you manage your Touchstones and bonuses they provide. How your character reacts to the attacks on your sense of belonging and which strategies they chose to deal with it.<br /> <br /> Which again involves deciding at which rung they feel more comfortable at staying, just now being a slightly more fluctuating thing, but between the strategies you can employ and the cost of buying a dot back, it isn't really hard to find a stable footing at any level you want.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> V5 commits to the red herring, which isn't a bad thing, but is an entirely distinct approach. And that's one of the reasons it is divisive, it is a subtle but fundamental difference in what the game loop will be.<br /> <br /> Degeneration is truly expected to be almost inevitable, a real slippery slope where staying moral is an uphill battle.<br /> <br /> This is staple of current horror trends. Previous editions follow the Naturalistic Moral of classic Gothic literature, where the horror is in the choices people are willing to make. In V5 the horror is in the intermittent loss of autonomy, the idea that the Beast doesn't simply makes it harder to stay moral, but actively forces you to be immoral no matter how hard you want to avoid it.<br /> <br /> It is the crushing system that really gives you no choice in the matter, or any matter, and you ultimately can't really step outside of it or beat it for good, only try to do the best you can between crisis, between failures, between cleaning after your last catastrophic depravity and the next, while depravity is the cost of existing in this world.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Three takes on horror, tragedy and how the Curse opposes identity, each exploring distinct themes and logic. I personally find V5's take cheap, but that's on me.<br /> <br /> I only have one actual criticism about the rules: I actually find Oblivion's stains a deeply stupid idea that misses the point royally to capitalize on cheap signaling.<br /> <br /> All Disciplines come from a place darker and hungrier than death itself, it's the Curse of the Beast. The thing that moves you to prey on the living, threaten the innocent and abuse those around you physically, emotionally, spiritually.<br /> <br /> More importantly, they're all means to abuse and victimization in some form, usually quite direct. Oblivion is, if anything, in the lower end of the spectrum.<br /> <br /> What it does is to cash in cool factor by using the edgy description of the Abyss in lieu of actually arguing anything. And the effect is the opposite of what it should, because any user of Oblivion that isn't a moron would notice A.S.A.P. that their best bet is to be conservative with its use and otherwise be a decent person, as they mechanically need their soul in a good shape to keep fueling/risking it in Oblivion.<br /> <br /> Oblivion is precisely for two clans known for being reliant on spamming their signature powers and being openly more imoral than other kindred, but works as a reverse incentive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T06:04:34-07:00","id":1560754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560753#post1560753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Three takes on horror, tragedy and how the Curse opposes identity, each exploring distinct themes and logic. I personally find V5's take cheap, but that's on me.</div> </div> </div> </div>On one hand, vampirism is explicitly supposed to be a CURSE, or a divine PUNISHMENT. So making degeneration of one's Humanity an inevitable process does reinforce that idea.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it also legitimizes the Sabbat's PoE system as being the only rational form of morality.<br /> <br /> Maintaining one's Humanity is an exercise in futility. It is doomed to failure, so you should begin looking for alternatives as soon as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T07:20:13-07:00","id":1560755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560754#post1560754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On one hand, vampirism is explicitly supposed to be a CURSE, or a divine PUNISHMENT. So making degeneration of one's Humanity an inevitable process does reinforce that idea.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, it also legitimizes the Sabbat's PoE system as being the only rational form of morality.<br /> <br /> Maintaining one's Humanity is an exercise in futility. It is doomed to failure, so you should begin looking for alternatives as soon as possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's kind of the funny thing about the Sabbat. While their methods may be flawed, their is a sense of logic to their beliefs.<br /> <br /> If clinging to one's humanity is not sustainable in the long term, and vampires have the capacity to live forever, then why bother fighting? There are other options which will be far less stressful on your mental and spiritual health.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T07:41:06-07:00","id":1560756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560754#post1560754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> On one hand, vampirism is explicitly supposed to be a CURSE, or a divine PUNISHMENT. So making degeneration of one's Humanity an inevitable process does reinforce that idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you buy the argument rather than question it. Every single word here is up to debate in more than one way.<br /> <br /> Is it a curse? What kind of curse? Punishment for what? From what kind of divinity?<br /> <br /> More importantly, why does inevitable degeneration reinforce this? What's the point of punishment if degeneration is a fate, not a choice? That's completely backwards.<br /> <br /> This logic being backwards is one of the points of 1st edition: the Book of Nod sells a story where ultimately vampirism is a cyclical falacy: you're cursed with degeneration for the sin of becoming degenerate once put on a curse of degeneration.<br /> <br /> What solves the falacy there is that there is no curse of degeneration, really: you're just as free to decide your path as before. The horror is not that your downfall is inevitable, but that it is totally avoidable, yet most will still fall because it is convenient.<br /> <br /> And what if a character don't buy the premises to begin with? All the usual vampire spiel is strictly based on European Roman Catholic premises. Followers of Protestant churches like to say those things are closer to universal ideas, but that's because they don't notice how much they're still locked in Roman Catholic theological priors.<br /> <br /> Many cultures out there don't have many of the premises needed for that reasoning to hold. Take for example that Islam assumes every intelligent entity has the basic free will to join the Faithful, no exceptions. There is no concept in it of a class of beings being inherently corrupt or damned. Many don't have the notion of damnation at all.<br /> <br /> For me the proposal of V5 has merit as a reflex of the horror of a society that build a idealized moral for you, then constrain you to a life where breaking morality becomes a survival need, and finally punishes you for doing the evil you had no choice about. But that's precisely a recognition that this is a setup, you're given a context where you can't win.<br /> <br /> Those are not the premises of traditional Gothic or Punk literature, which are the standards for previous editions. V5 follows &quot;Gothic-Punk&quot; only as aesthetics, which isn't a bad thing, but its literary tradition is Grimdark Satire.<br /> <br /> Valid, but not more valid.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-19T10:49:54-07:00","id":1560760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560756#post1560756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Only if you buy the argument rather than question it. Every single word here is up to debate in more than one way.<br /> <br /> Is it a curse? What kind of curse? Punishment for what? From what kind of divinity?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Originally, the curse was to be forever separated from human society, hiding from the sun, and feeding on the blood of the living. The super powers were never part of the package, until Lilith came along and taught Caine the secret of disciplines.<br /> <br /> Prior to that, his punishment from God was to live like a wild animal. I don't know if this exists in World of Darkness, but the bible also says that if anybody tried to kill Caine, they would have his curse inflicted upon them 7 times over. God wanted Caine to suffer, and anybody who tries to end that suffering will receive an even harsher sentence.<br /> <br /> As for degeneration being a choice, I believe that the constant backstabbing and tyrannical oppression that permeates vampire society is another part of Caine's punishment. Just as he murdered his own brother out of jealousy, he must now watch as all his progeny reenact the same sin over and over again. Generations of vampires enslaving, killing and devouring each other for petty power plays, that's the true <i>Mark of Caine.</i><br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> The European roman catholic premise being unreliable would be plausible, IF Caine was confirmed to be just a mythical figure who never shows up outside of stories. But that's not the case. Caine is a real figure, who's been wandering the planet for the last 300 something thousand years. You can theoretically meet the guy in person and have interactions with him.<br /> <br /> Other gods such as Odin, Set, Samedi, est. are all confirmed to be vampires that merely used their powers to trick mortals into worshiping them.<br /> <br /> <br /> I don't know what version of Islam you read, but I'm not touching that subject on these forums with a 20 foot pole.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T02:06:28-07:00","id":1560809,"title":"","content":"One thing I would like a potential V6 to do is reduce the centrality of the Caine myth somewhat, so it's just one of several options. Yes, it's the one most Western and Abrahamic Kindred believe (and it's pretty much an essential belief in the Sabbat), but presenting a few different options would help open the game up.<br /> <br /> If the Caine myth is always presented as basically true, not only are you chump for thinking the First Vampire was someone else, but it also limits Kindred history to a small period of time from the Middle East to the present day. Every Antediluvian essentially has to come from somewhere between Syria and Iran.<br /> <br /> But if there's scope for Caine to have been something else, the First City might have been in Ethiopia, or Mohenjo-Daro, or whatever. This also opens us up to moving away from the centrality of Abrahamic faith in Kindred morality.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be a big retcon. Just provide options and refer back to those options later on, instead of saying &quot;it might be these other things&quot; in the CRB and then never really mentioning those other origins again (which is what Revised did).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T05:24:50-07:00","id":1560814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560809#post1560809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I would like a potential V6 to do is reduce the centrality of the Caine myth somewhat, so it's just one of several options.</div> </div> </div> </div>So much that.<br /> <br /> But nowadays I notice why they don't, and even other Abrahamic beliefs are sidestepped. Because let's be clear here, the Book of Nod is Christian. It is not Jewish and it is not Muslim, it is unapologetically and unavoidably Christian as it tell everything from interpretations that are in proto forms in post-exilic Israel at best, or are straight up post-Agostinian at worse.<br /> <br /> The problem, though, is that in all versions the game cycles back to the theme of Damnation and objective Good and Evil. It builds horror over the premise that the taint of sin and evil can condemn your immortal soul by bringing it away from the love of YHWH and its redemption.<br /> <br /> Most other belief systems don't engage with such priors. Not that they offer other answers, they see the very question as nonsensical.<br /> <br /> We already have this experiment in the Ashirra and the Revised (and exiled) Banu Haqim: in the Quran every intelligent being has free will and can chose to join the faithful. The notion of a condition that intrinsically condemns you is straight up shut down by the Book itself. The demons aren't defined by what they are, but by their work on straying the Faithful from the Path.<br /> <br /> Minor, and works as a group within the game. But part of the difficulty of using them as PCs is that they immediately throw half the personal horror through the window. Being a decent person is still hard, but not desperately so, and you have your shot at Paradise like any other person.<br /> <br /> For most, nonhuman creatures are just that. They are ontologically distinct, which means distinct cosmological roles, but otherwise are there to be themselves. An Hindu vampire will ask their relationship with the classes of gods within Maya. A Japanese one accepts it turned y\u014dkai and moves on. Even the ancient Greek would find the transformation the destiny in itself: the will of the gods caused this, but this has no inherent weight on your later destiny in Erebus if you ever get there. The life you forge out of your new condition is the punishment in itself.<br /> <br /> Look to the half a dozen religious constructs of the Setites. At least 2 or 3 are actually pretty decent: they give positive drive to the vampire, propose community good, and reconcile this with the predatory nature. You won't be lovable, innocent and harmless, but won't be denied a positive role in society either.<br /> <br /> Even removing religion: what's the ecological niche of a vampire? Why should a human predator that exists in a complex ecological system with the prey, and a micro-predator by the way, be just consigned to extinction?<br /> <br /> Do you know how vile something has to be for biologists to conclude the world is undeniably better without you? Most atheists still grew up surrounded by Christians, so they understand and buy the Damnation question easily. But one that doesn't already throws the whole premise to the ground.<br /> <br /> For us to see alternatives to Nod taken seriously and consistently in VtM, the game has to first grip with what being a vampire means in radically different spiritual frameworks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T07:08:28-07:00","id":1560816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560809#post1560809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I would like a potential V6 to do is reduce the centrality of the Caine myth somewhat, so it's just one of several options. Yes, it's the one most Western and Abrahamic Kindred believe (and it's pretty much an essential belief in the Sabbat), but presenting a few different options would help open the game up.<br /> <br /> If the Caine myth is always presented as basically true, not only are you chump for thinking the First Vampire was someone else, but it also limits Kindred history to a small period of time from the Middle East to the present day. Every Antediluvian essentially has to come from somewhere between Syria and Iran.<br /> <br /> But if there's scope for Caine to have been something else, the First City might have been in Ethiopia, or Mohenjo-Daro, or whatever. This also opens us up to moving away from the centrality of Abrahamic faith in Kindred morality.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be a big retcon. Just provide options and refer back to those options later on, instead of saying &quot;it might be these other things&quot; in the CRB and then never really mentioning those other origins again (which is what Revised did).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Since the system is taking its sweet, fucking time approving my last post, after I corrected a couple typos, I'll say this again.<br /> <br /> the 'Caine myth' would be more reasonable, if Caine and the Antedeluvians were not explicitly confirmed to be real. Caine's not some imaginary figure who only appears in stories told to fledglings at bed time. He's an actual character that's been wandering the earth for at minimum of 300,000 years. He predates the very concept of regional origins, because he's been around since before there were enough humans to establish them.<br /> <br /> You can theoretically run into the guy and have a personal conversation with him.<br /> <br /> Several clans know for a fact the antedeluvians existed at some point, such as Tzimisce, Lasombra, Tremere, Giovanni and Ravnos. Because they had to find them in order to secure their legitimacy, or kickstart their revolutions. Or because they were driving everyone in the entire hemisphere batshit insane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T09:39:37-07:00","id":1560818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560816#post1560816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Since the system is taking its sweet, fucking time approving my last post, after I corrected a couple typos, I'll say this again.<br /> <br /> the 'Caine myth' would be more reasonable, if Caine and the Antedeluvians were not explicitly confirmed to be real. Caine's not some imaginary figure who only appears in stories told to fledglings at bed time. He's an actual character that's been wandering the earth for at minimum of 300,000 years. He predates the very concept of regional origins, because he's been around since before there were enough humans to establish them.<br /> <br /> You can theoretically run into the guy and have a personal conversation with him.<br /> <br /> Several clans know for a fact the antedeluvians existed at some point, such as Tzimisce, Lasombra, Tremere, Giovanni and Ravnos. Because they had to find them in order to secure their legitimacy, or kickstart their revolutions. Or because they were driving everyone in the entire hemisphere batshit insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>It depends what you mean by &quot;not confirmed to exist&quot;. Do you mean they never existed, they did exist but don't exist now, or that they were simply something else?<br /> <br /> I think the first of those options is actually harder than just saying the First Generation is Something Else (TM). For starters, the fact we have generations as an in-character and out-of-character thing implies certain things about the setting.<br /> <br /> Now, we can handwave this by saying that every x millennia, the Ancients wake up and chow down, bringing us back to four or five generations, which means we can set that First Generation figure as far back in history as we like\u2014perhaps even millions of years. But there's still an implication that <i>something</i> was first. That's why I think it's easier to say the First Generation was not-Caine than to say there was no First Generation at all.<br /> <br /> Of course, the First Generation might also have been multiple entities, or perhaps each clan actually has its own First Generation entity, or perhaps the blood only started thinning after 500 generations instead of after 3, but the idea of blood thinning with generation still implies a primordial, undiluted origin somewhere down the line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T10:40:51-07:00","id":1560819,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560818#post1560818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, the First Generation might also have been multiple entities, or perhaps each clan actually has its own First Generation entity, or perhaps the blood only started thinning after 500 generations instead of after 3, but the idea of blood thinning with generation still implies a primordial, undiluted origin somewhere down the line.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I like how Requiem introduced the concept of spontaneous embraces (Longinus and Dracula in particular), so there could technically be multiple 'first generation' vampires.<br /> <br /> Followers of Set also claimed that Set was the first true vampire, and thus counted all their generations as being two steps lower in reflection of this. For example, a 9th generation Setite would be considered 7th generation by the rest of the clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T12:44:30-07:00","id":1560820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560816#post1560816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Since the system is taking its sweet, fucking time approving my last post, after I corrected a couple typos, I'll say this again.<br /> <br /> the 'Caine myth' would be more reasonable, if Caine and the Antedeluvians were not explicitly confirmed to be real. Caine's not some imaginary figure who only appears in stories told to fledglings at bed time. He's an actual character that's been wandering the earth for at minimum of 300,000 years. He predates the very concept of regional origins, because he's been around since before there were enough humans to establish them.<br /> <br /> You can theoretically run into the guy and have a personal conversation with him.<br /> <br /> Several clans know for a fact the antedeluvians existed at some point, such as Tzimisce, Lasombra, Tremere, Giovanni and Ravnos. Because they had to find them in order to secure their legitimacy, or kickstart their revolutions. Or because they were driving everyone in the entire hemisphere batshit insane.</div> </div> </div> </div>The game confirms a lot less than the fandom embraces as canon.<br /> <br /> Caine is not, by any means, confirmed to have existed. Not in the sense of being the 1st Gen, and not in the sense of being the person he's purported to be.<br /> <br /> The Second Generation, same thing, and their numbers and names aren't even something you can be sure of, IF you assume they existed. Their stories are legends from legends.<br /> <br /> Only the Third Generation is confirmed to have existed. Any confirmation of vampire society starts with them, and anything prior comes from archaeology or them, and they lie.<br /> <br /> Also, you know other things we don't really know?<br /> <br /> 1. We don't know if there was any Deluge, or how big.<br /> 2. We don't know if the 3rd Gen aren't really the 1st.<br /> 3. We don't know if they're human at all at any point in time. As far as we know even some 4th Gen may never have been human.<br /> 4. We don't know how real is the link between clans. Are Kindred the same species, or similar products of independent origins?<br /> 5. We don't know how many Antes existed, if there aren't others who originated rarer bloodlines or other things or nothing.<br /> 6. We don't know if the birth of new 3rd Gens outside diablerie really stopped at all.<br /> 7. We don't know what really caused vampires.<br /> <br /> We do know one thing:<br /> A Super powered bloody monster awoke in Bangladesh in 1999 and the clan Ravnos went berserker. Most people think it was their Ante.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T13:52:45-07:00","id":1560827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560820#post1560820\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game confirms a lot less than the fandom embraces as canon.<br /> <br /> Caine is not, by any means, confirmed to have existed. Not in the sense of being the 1st Gen, and not in the sense of being the person he's purported to be.<br /> <br /> The Second Generation, same thing, and their numbers and names aren't even something you can be sure of, IF you assume they existed. Their stories are legends from legends.<br /> <br /> Only the Third Generation is confirmed to have existed. Any confirmation of vampire society starts with them, and anything prior comes from archaeology or them, and they lie.<br /> <br /> Also, you know other things we don't really know?<br /> <br /> 1. We don't know if there was any Deluge, or how big.<br /> 2. We don't know if the 3rd Gen aren't really the 1st.<br /> 3. We don't know if they're human at all at any point in time. As far as we know even some 4th Gen may never have been human.<br /> 4. We don't know how real is the link between clans. Are Kindred the same species, or similar products of independent origins?<br /> 5. We don't know how many Antes existed, if there aren't others who originated rarer bloodlines or other things or nothing.<br /> 6. We don't know if the birth of new 3rd Gens outside diablerie really stopped at all.<br /> 7. We don't know what really caused vampires.<br /> <br /> We do know one thing:<br /> A Super powered bloody monster awoke in Bangladesh in 1999 and the clan Ravnos went berserker. Most people think it was their Ante.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The game sometimes throws doubt on these things, but then you have Caine pop up as a character in books and video games, and so on. They did try to be vague about it from time to time, but then the next writer would just add something else to confirm the original myth.<br /> <br /> V20DA does present more non-Cainite origins for the clans, though, so I think it's something successive writing teams have been aware of. Whether New nuWW carry that forward or not is anyone's guess, though.<br /> <br /> Bringing it back to the Sabbat, I think that's an organisation that would struggle to remove the Caine myth entirely. I mean, you can do it, but the whole premise is that it's the Sword of Caine, and the leader is his regent, so a lot of stuff loses its internal coherence if they just become a generic &quot;anti-Antediluvians&quot; faction (and the Caine myth is one of a small number of things holding the sect together).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T14:11:24-07:00","id":1560829,"title":"","content":"But the religious fanatic aspect of the Sabbat is a better narrative element in an unsure setting. <br /> <br /> When we look at the Garou, they're zealots... but zealots that can directly contact their deities which blunts their ability to satirize fanaticism as a narrative device.<br /> <br /> If the game treats Noddist lore as true, the Sabbat aren't really a satire of religious fanatics... because a lot of their philosophy would stem from justified truth claims not faith in legendary stories. You don't want to remove the Noddist mythology from the Sabbat... you want them to hold on to it despite there being no demonstrable evidence that any of it is actually true. The Sabbat are a lot scarier and a lot more effective narratively when they're driven by faith instead of facts. The difficulty for the writers is keeping Noddist mythology in the game believable enough that the Sabbat don't just come off as delusional for believing in it and then taking it to its logical extremes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T14:33:11-07:00","id":1560831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560829#post1560829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the religious fanatic aspect of the Sabbat is a better narrative element in an unsure setting.<br /> <br /> When we look at the Garou, they're zealots... but zealots that can directly contact their deities which blunts their ability to satirize fanaticism as a narrative device.<br /> <br /> If the game treats Noddist lore as true, the Sabbat aren't really a satire of religious fanatics... because a lot of their philosophy would stem from justified truth claims not faith in legendary stories. You don't want to remove the Noddist mythology from the Sabbat... you want them to hold on to it despite there being no demonstrable evidence that any of it is actually true. The Sabbat are a lot scarier and a lot more effective narratively when they're driven by faith instead of facts. The difficulty for the writers is keeping Noddist mythology in the game believable enough that the Sabbat don't just come off as delusional for believing in it and then taking it to its logical extremes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, I agree with that. I wasn't really arguing otherwise, so I must've been unclear.<br /> <br /> What I meant was that if the game dials back the &quot;Caine is real/the truth&quot; element, it would have to do so in all areas except those written from the POV of the Sabbat. So any future Sabbat sourcebook would necessarily be written from a similar mythological standpoint as older editions were. Depending on how much you write about the Sabbat, that could still outweigh other theories about the origin of vampires, just because that one theory might get 25% of the coverage while all the others only get 5\u201310%.<br /> <br /> You could present the Caine stuff purely as something believed IC, and question it OOC throughout the book, but WoD books don't always do that\u2014a lot of them are written as intensely IC for history and fluff sections. That was especially true in Revised and is somewhat true in V5 (but wasn't as true in V20, except in the &quot;Lore of&quot; books).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T15:00:32-07:00","id":1560832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560829#post1560829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the religious fanatic aspect of the Sabbat is a better narrative element in an unsure setting.<br /> <br /> When we look at the Garou, they're zealots... but zealots that can directly contact their deities which blunts their ability to satirize fanaticism as a narrative device.<br /> <br /> If the game treats Noddist lore as true, the Sabbat aren't really a satire of religious fanatics... because a lot of their philosophy would stem from justified truth claims not faith in legendary stories. You don't want to remove the Noddist mythology from the Sabbat... you want them to hold on to it despite there being no demonstrable evidence that any of it is actually true. The Sabbat are a lot scarier and a lot more effective narratively when they're driven by faith instead of facts. The difficulty for the writers is keeping Noddist mythology in the game believable enough that the Sabbat don't just come off as delusional for believing in it and then taking it to its logical extremes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is Noddhism actually religious though? I got the impression that it was more focused on trying to emulate Caine, rather than outright worship him. It also seems more scholastically driven, as opposed to theocratic. Followers of the path are expected to seek out and research vampiric lore, history, and explore the limits of their powers. Religious institutions tend to be of the mind of <i>&quot;this book has all the answers, so stop asking questions!&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T15:52:21-07:00","id":1560835,"title":"","content":"Noddism (which is not just the Path of Caine) is theological even if not a religion by itself. There's a reason why I only used &quot;religious&quot; when directly indexing the Sabbat itself, rather than Noddism lore broadly.<br /> <br /> Also keep in mind that there aren't some sort of objective criteria around what makes something religious or a religion. It's a very blurry line that sometimes gets defined in neater ways for utility's sake. Buddhism is a pretty text book example of something that doesn't really fit what most people think of as a religion on a surface level (including emulating Buddha, not worshiping him), while still filling the vast majority of the same cultural and social roles as a more &quot;standard&quot; religion does. Noddism still recognizes the Abrahamic supreme deity as the world's supreme deity even while centering Caine as it's most important mythological figure (Zoroaster is not the deity of Zoroastrianism for another real world parallel) that serves as more of a prophetic archetype that teaches how to relate to the divine instead of replacing the divine as the target of ritual practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T15:53:18-07:00","id":1560836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560827#post1560827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes and no. The game sometimes throws doubt on these things, but then you have Caine pop up as a character in books and video games, and so on. They did try to be vague about it from time to time, but then the next writer would just add something else to confirm the original myth.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is what we can really say to be confirmed?<br /> <br /> It throws references all over the place, some are 100% intended by that author to be real, but how much the setting really assumes &quot;this is canon and future books will assume you run like that&quot; is way less if anything.<br /> <br /> He said the game makes it explicit Noddism is real, Caine and the Antes exist. I'm saying the game toys with this idea, but not really confirm nothing.<br /> <br /> Above all, my 7 questions and many others remain unanswered by those cameos. The Book of Nod is packed with assumptions, one thing being true says nothing about all the rest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560829#post1560829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the religious fanatic aspect of the Sabbat is a better narrative element in an unsure setting.<br /> <br /> When we look at the Garou, they're zealots... but zealots that can directly contact their deities which blunts their ability to satirize fanaticism as a narrative device.</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the things I love in Ravenloft for 3rd ed in D&amp;D is that it strips religion of certainty, and the result is wonderful.<br /> <br /> Even if some author shoehorn nods to Caine and stuff, my favorite interpretations of the WoD have this fog of mystery over the past.<br /> <br /> There's no &quot;such and such happened&quot;. It's always according to someone, and there is no such a thing as neutrality.<br /> <br /> Werewolf ditches a lot of religious ambiguity to ease some other aspects (and shut down global warm deniers in their tracks), but is all the poorer for this, at least until you explore more the unreliable nature of spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560832#post1560832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is Noddhism actually religious though? I got the impression that it was more focused on trying to emulate Caine, rather than outright worship him. It also seems more scholastically driven, as opposed to theocratic. Followers of the path are expected to seek out and research vampiric lore, history, and explore the limits of their powers. Religious institutions tend to be of the mind of <i>&quot;this book has all the answers, so stop asking questions!&quot;</i></div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure about your exposure to other religions, but quite a lot of them have this same attitude, including some Christian and even Catholic schools of thought.<br /> <br /> No religion is free from dogmatism (and that includes the Sabbat), but scholastic, esoteric and similar studies abound on them all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T17:06:54-07:00","id":1560843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560836#post1560836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure about your exposure to other religions, but quite a lot of them have this same attitude, including some Christian and even Catholic schools of thought.<br /> <br /> No religion is free from dogmatism (and that includes the Sabbat), but scholastic, esoteric and similar studies abound on them all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on my observations over the years, it seems like trying to propose ideas or viewpoints that fall outside the established dogma gets you labeled as a heretic, or leads to you branching off to found a new sect. Of which, Christianity alone has 20,000 different options, and half the combined population all claim to be Catholic.<br /> <br /> I know that theological scholars do exist, but I always got the impression they were studying it for academic purposes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Yeah, Buddha was not a true deity in the way we might typically understand it. But he became the next best thing when he achieved enlightenment and subsequently became one with the universe. One story has him challenge Sun Wukong to see if he can leap out of Buddha's hand; but since Buddha is one with the universe as a whole, such a feat was thus impossible. Sun Wukong would have needed to jump outside the universe to win the challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-21T17:36:39-07:00","id":1560845,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29009_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29009\" data-vbnamecard=\"29009\">DarkKing</a> Religions mix a lot of attitudes, but overall there is an expectation that followers will study, and study hard. If this is to reach the same conclusions or what, doesn't change what's being asked is a scholarly approach.<br /> <br /> For this I'll conflate Noddism with the Sabbat religion for ease writing, they're not actually the same and the relationship is complicated.<br /> <br /> Think all Bible study groups and whatnot the average Christian church houses, even if to teach prescribed doctrine. Advanced classes frequently trade tips and stories on experiences during pray. This is a repeating motif.<br /> <br /> More dogmatic ones do the opposite to stop followers from &quot;wandering dangerously through the text&quot;, but most want people that at the very least learn apologetics, if they have no good reason.<br /> <br /> And the religious side of the Sabbat does a lot of that and other takes. Doctrine teaches the members should study Noddism and the vampiric condition. The reality:<br /> 1. From the beginning a lot of member pay only lip service to Noddism or Caine,<br /> 2. Most Paths are religions themselves distinct from Noddism, they use excuses and pay lip service,<br /> 3. A lot of members don't give a fuck, they're followers, not thinkers, and decidedly don't study as doctrine prescribes,<br /> 4. A minority, big but still minority, actually do as they're told, study, yet half end up religious zealots like the Black Hand, the Sabbat Inquisition, etc.<br /> <br /> Part of what makes the Sabbat interesting is that it is a political philosophy wrapped under a religion for morale. The religion is real, but the overall fanaticism is not, or at least is more nuanced.<br /> <br /> And as religious practices frequently are IRL, if you focus on doctrine you miss what most members actually live there. For most of them, being the Sword of Caine isn't about study, doctrine or whatever. It's about the Ritae and the experiences you have with your siblings in Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-22T08:43:15-07:00","id":1560860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560816#post1560816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Since the system is taking its sweet, fucking time approving my last post, after I corrected a couple typos, I'll say this again.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it takes longer than a week, I'd recommend trying to contact somebody about it.<br /> <br /> I don't think the mods are very active around here. It took them over a month to approve my account for forum activity, and even then it was only after I submitted a trouble ticket about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T07:09:52-07:00","id":1560883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560497#post1560497\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's look at some of the more popular Sabbat Paths and see where they'd be. I'll be using the Revised era Paths of The Guide to the Sabbat. I know other editions have different Hierarchy of Sins.<br /> <br /> Path of Caine - I don't see any mention about not killing mortals. So that's an easy Path for the routine mass murdering Sabbat, and we know this is a popular Path for the sect.<br /> <br /> Path of Cathari - Prohibitions on &quot;arbitrary killing&quot; at level 2 (quite serious) and &quot;impassioned killing&quot; at level 6. If we excuse the killings done as part of the Auctoritas Ritae (like Blood Bath, Blood Beast, and Palla Grande) as not arbitrary, most followers can probably be at normal Path levels as Camarilla vampires on Humanity. They'd just need to avoid routine &quot;needless&quot; killing of mortals the rest of the time.<br /> <br /> Path of Death and the Soul - &quot;<i>Failing</i> to kill when useful&quot; (Useful meaning useful to one's study of death) is a level 6 sin. &quot;Showing compassion&quot; is a level 3 sin. &quot;Killing <i>without studying death afterward</i>&quot; is a level 2 sin. This is probably where the difficulty comes from as someone attempting to &quot;study&quot; at a Blood Feast or during a Sabbat murder hobo crusade is probably hard to do. &quot;Needlessly preventing a death&quot; is a level 1 sin. This path doesn't have a problem with killing mortals. The real complication is the need to &quot;study&quot; it afterwards. This will create some odd behavior, but should not present too much a trouble. It's just more likely a Path adherent will prefer isolated &quot;intimate&quot; murders where she can study the effects rather than killing sprees.<br /> <br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> <br /> Path of Power and the Inner Voice - A classic Sabbat path, and one that many (most?) of its leaders follow. No prohibitions against murder here. &quot;<i>Failing</i> to kill when it's in your interests&quot; is a level 5 sin. While individual unifiers may not kill a lot, there's not much problem if they do. They're just more likely to kill for a reason.<br /> <br /> Path of Metamorphosis - This is pulled from the Revised Vampire: the Masquerade Corebook. This is another dark Path. No prohibitions against killing. Instead &quot;<i>Refusing</i> to kill when knowledge may be gained from it&quot; is a level 6 sin. &quot;Considering the needs of others&quot; is a level 4 sin. &quot;Exhibiying compassion for others&quot; is a level 1 sin. These vampires are sick.<br /> <br /> (...)<br /> <br /> The Paths of Cathari and Power and the Inner Voice are probably only so-so as murder hobos. They likely won't engage in routine murder, but have plentiful of meaningful homicides. They probably work well with the above paths as they know they may need help at some time from the real sickos. However, they can usually fit in well with them.<br /> <br /> The Paths of Caine, Death and the Soul, Evil Revelation, and Metamorphosis are probably where most of the murder hobos come from. Nothing really stops them from killing at any time, and many will justify killing just in order to not sin against their Paths.<br /> <br /> I imagine early on, Sabbat who were on Paths were mostly those on more humane paths. But as the sect grew to identify themselves with radical notions of freedom, it encouraged the morally worst shitbags to justify their awful behavior in the guise of twisted Paths, and they gradually took over the sect.</div> </div> </div> </div>And killing to create shovelheads isn't arbitrary or without purpose, it's right there on the tin. The purpose is creating shovelheads.<br /> <br /> Weren't the first Paths formulated things like Metamorphosis and Death and the Soul, since they were basically re-dos of medieval Roads and the Tzimisce founded the Path system?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T08:26:40-07:00","id":1560885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560836#post1560836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is what we can really say to be confirmed?<br /> <br /> It throws references all over the place, some are 100% intended by that author to be real, but how much the setting really assumes &quot;this is canon and future books will assume you run like that&quot; is way less if anything.<br /> <br /> He said the game makes it explicit Noddism is real, Caine and the Antes exist. I'm saying the game toys with this idea, but not really confirm nothing.</div> </div> </div> </div>While your interpretation is dear to my heart I will quibble a bit. As conceptualised and most often written Caine is real in VtM. He is a child of Adam and Eve who has been cursed by God and so became a first vampire. We can argue how fictionalised Book of Nod or Erciyes fragments are but this idea is pretty certain OOC even if many individuals and groups IC consider it bullshit (like Beckett does). <br /> <br /> The main problem, like with any long running universe, is that VtM has been written by hundreds of people over the decades so they were stressing, ignoring or deemphasizing different aspects of the world so there is no coherent description of the setting because it's actually many settings depending on the edition, lead developer and actual writers describing it. So much for nitpicking. <br /> <br /> As for the truth about vampire mythos in-world I agree that treating it as a legend that might or might not be based in historical facts is the best approach. That's when on the subreddits people ask about Caine, Second Generation or Antes I say that most of this stuff is debatable. Because what sources we have for Caine existence? Book of Nod, Erciyes Fragments, Book of Grave War or Revelations of the Dark Mother? Those are all books of religious mythology that are surely coloured by religious and political bias of their authors. <br /> <br /> Oh, and of course, Antediluvians. Who as far as we know, hate Caine utterly and are more prone to lie even than the average vampire. Hell, do they even remember what has happened thousands of years ago? Or is their recollection shaped by millenia of emotional reactions to the events in the First and Second City? <br /> <br /> The many point of view are a problem for coherent setting description but are also, in my mind, big part of VtM's, and WoD' as whole, success. Players and Storytellers love to quarrel and argue whether Saulot was Dark Plagius or a saint smeared by Tremere. And yes, it's much more interesting when in-world characters argue about it too. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T09:34:13-07:00","id":1560886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560883#post1560883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And killing to create shovelheads isn't arbitrary or without purpose, it's right there on the tin. The purpose is creating shovelheads.<br /> <br /> Weren't the first Paths formulated things like Metamorphosis and Death and the Soul, since they were basically re-dos of medieval Roads and the Tzimisce founded the Path system?</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, yes. The Lasombra and Tzimisce both claim credit for the paths in their Revised clanbooks (<i>Clanbook: Lasombra Revised</i>, p. 26; <i>Clanbook: Tzimisce Revised</i>, p. 23), but they're both unreliable narrators. I think they probably contributed in their own ways, and moreso than most clans, though each claims they were the biggest contributors for obvious reasons.<br /> <br /> <i>Giovanni Chronicles II: Blood &amp; Fire </i>attributes most of the paths to those at the Black Monastery, meaning Cainites from a wide range of clans, but four paths were developed directly or indirectly by Lasombra and Tzimisce there, too (two apiece). The full list is here: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Monastery\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Black_Monastery</a> (Lady Vadislava and Zara Slatikov are Tzimisce; Lord Alexandre and Lord Marcus are Lasombra.)<br /> <br /> That list fits the canon elsewhere, as Lady Vadislava worked on Death and the Soul, Slatikov (not in GC2, but added later in <i>Chaining the Beast</i>) worked on Metamorphosis (but contributed to others), and Lords Alexandre and Marcus contributed to Power and the Inner Voice. These three paths all derive from Dark Ages Roads (Bones, Metamorphosis, and Kings, IIRC), meaning they likely emerged early on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T09:56:01-07:00","id":1560887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560885#post1560885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While your interpretation is dear to my heart I will quibble a bit. As conceptualised and most often written Caine is real in VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Demonstrate.<br /> <br /> You literally just said that everything in the game that we have for Caine's existence are religious texts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T10:17:30-07:00","id":1560889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560885#post1560885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While your interpretation is dear to my heart I will quibble a bit. As conceptualised and most often written Caine is real in VtM. He is a child of Adam and Eve who has been cursed by God and so became a first vampire. We can argue how fictionalised Book of Nod or Erciyes fragments are but this idea is pretty certain OOC even if many individuals and groups IC consider it bullshit (like Beckett does).</div> </div> </div> </div>One of Beckket's friends (a Malkavian) even came across Tzimisce, and immediately proceeded to swan dive into its biomass when he realized what that meant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560885#post1560885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the truth about vampire mythos in-world I agree that treating it as a legend that might or might not be based in historical facts is the best approach. That's when on the subreddits people ask about Caine, Second Generation or Antes I say that most of this stuff is debatable. Because what sources we have for Caine existence? Book of Nod, Erciyes Fragments, Book of Grave War or Revelations of the Dark Mother? Those are all books of religious mythology that are surely coloured by religious and political bias of their authors.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I personally disagree with the notion that the Caine mythos is heavily rooted in Christian dogma, due to the fact they introduced figures like Lilith into the story. Lilith comes from the hebrew scripture, and is not mentioned within Christianity.<br /> <br /> Lilith's existence kind of throws the whole concept of Adam and Eve being responsible for original sin out the window, since she was the one who originally defied God by refusing to be submissive to Adam, and refusing a direct order to return to the Garden of Eden after she ran off. Caine also can't have been the one who originally taught Angels the concept of murder, when they threatened to kill 1,000 of Lilith's children every day as punishment for her defiance.<br /> <br /> Lilith, drawing upon giga chad energy, vowed that she would birth 2,000 children to counteract their efforts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560885#post1560885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, and of course, Antediluvians. Who as far as we know, hate Caine utterly and are more prone to lie even than the average vampire. Hell, do they even remember what has happened thousands of years ago? Or is their recollection shaped by millenia of emotional reactions to the events in the First and Second City?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Given that a recurring theme with the curse of vampirism seems to be you becoming mentally or culturally stagnant in whatever time period you were at the time of your embrace, I'd say they remember very well.<br /> <br /> Bare in mind, the Antedeluvians were originally sired during the earliest days of humanity's development. They are 10's of thousands of years old at the very least, with the possibility of being 100's. The degree of barbarism and cruelty they inflict upon the world was common place back when they were alive, so they probably don't think anything of it.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T10:55:53-07:00","id":1560891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560889#post1560889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally disagree with the notion that the Caine mythos is heavily rooted in Christian dogma, due to the fact they introduced figures like Lilith into the story. Lilith comes from the hebrew scripture, and is not mentioned within Christianity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lilith comes from medieval Jewish scripture. And means exactly nothing anyway.<br /> <br /> First of all, legends and myths are mixes of influences and previous stories from several origins. This rationale would be like saying the Old Testament itself isn't heavily rooted in Hebrew dogma because it has the Deluge, and that comes from Mesopotamyan scripture.<br /> <br /> Second, the text is ultimately an ooc creation heavily based on the Bible and Christian doctrine, and that's that. Not that you can't declare it is something else in the setting, but that will still be the author presenting us with a story heavily rooted in Christian dogma.<br /> <br /> Which in this particular case is what matters, because if it is truth in the game, then in the game it isn't based in any doctrine, it's just truth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T11:44:29-07:00","id":1560892,"title":"","content":"To nitpick a bit:<br /> <br /> Lilith isn't part of any Abrahamic scriptures. She's part of apocrypha; which is a very important distinction if we're talking about doctrines and dogmas. When Lilith becomes part of apocrypha based mythology depends which version of her (or if she's a proper noun instead of a class of being) we're talking about (there are many, and her being part of the Eden narrative is the Medieval version).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T13:02:56-07:00","id":1560896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560891#post1560891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> First of all, legends and myths are mixes of influences and previous stories from several origins. This rationale would be like saying the Old Testament itself isn't heavily rooted in Hebrew dogma because it has the Deluge, and that comes from Mesopotamyan scripture.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thing about that, the story of Jesus is plagiarized from the mythology of a previously established Sun God, who was themselves a plagiarism, who was also a plagiarism, who was also a plagiarism, est.<br /> <br /> Saying that anything is rooted in Christian dogma is kind of funny, when they're not even the ones who originally came up with it. They're just the most recent in a long line of copycats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T13:12:09-07:00","id":1560897,"title":"","content":"Heck, if you want to get into Christian mythology, was Caine cursed by El or Yahweh? Because they weren't originally the same being. Yahweh was originally the local version of basically Thor. El was the king of the pantheon. It was only much later that the pantheon was retconned out of existence, and Yahweh and El got merged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T13:26:08-07:00","id":1560898,"title":"","content":"Let's not get into a deep talk of real world theology maybe? It doesn't seem like this is going to go well.<br /> <br /> That said... dogma doesn't care about how original or derivative a belief system is. Dogmas are just core/central belief claims of a belief system. The things that need to be true for the rest of it to make sense.<br /> <br /> Whether you want to analyze the Noddist mythology in a Watsonian or Doylist fashion, the claim of it being rooted in Christian dogma comes from Noddist myth relying on post-Greco-Roman Judaism dogmatic developments that are unique to Christianity. Most specifically the Temptation of Caine is a Christian dogma derived aspect of the story; Christianity has a dogmatic requirement of intercessory divine mercy that isn't found in other related faiths or possible sources of myths that aren't original to the Abrahamic faiths in the first place..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T13:39:20-07:00","id":1560899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560897#post1560897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Heck, if you want to get into Christian mythology, was Caine cursed by El or Yahweh? Because they weren't originally the same being. Yahweh was originally the local version of basically Thor. El was the king of the pantheon. It was only much later that the pantheon was retconned out of existence, and Yahweh and El got merged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, once you realize that they used to be polytheistic, it suddenly makes a lot more sense as to why God seems to contradict himself so much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T14:26:14-07:00","id":1560902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560892#post1560892\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To nitpick a bit:<br /> <br /> Lilith isn't part of any Abrahamic scriptures. She's part of apocrypha; which is a very important distinction if we're talking about doctrines and dogmas. When Lilith becomes part of apocrypha based mythology depends which version of her (or if she's a proper noun instead of a class of being) we're talking about (there are many, and her being part of the Eden narrative is the Medieval version).</div> </div> </div> </div>To be the nitpickiest, Lilith is mentioned in the Hebrew Bible (Isaiah, IIRC), although most translators translate the mention to her as &quot;the night-owl,&quot; &quot;owl-demon,&quot; or &quot;night-demon,&quot; rather than keeping the Hebrew intact. And the Lilith being part of the Eden narrative is late ancient, not medieval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T14:27:21-07:00","id":1560903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560898#post1560898\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's not get into a deep talk of real world theology maybe? It doesn't seem like this is going to go well.<br /> <br /> That said... dogma doesn't care about how original or derivative a belief system is. Dogmas are just core/central belief claims of a belief system. The things that need to be true for the rest of it to make sense.<br /> <br /> Whether you want to analyze the Noddist mythology in a Watsonian or Doylist fashion, the claim of it being rooted in Christian dogma comes from Noddist myth relying on post-Greco-Roman Judaism dogmatic developments that are unique to Christianity. Most specifically the Temptation of Caine is a Christian dogma derived aspect of the story; Christianity has a dogmatic requirement of intercessory divine mercy that isn't found in other related faiths or possible sources of myths that aren't original to the Abrahamic faiths in the first place..</div> </div> </div> </div>Caine sits down with a couple of Sabbat neonates and tries to explain the Age of Sorrows and how he's really the last surviving abyssal exalt.<br /> <br /> They zone out when he starts rambling about how Cybertron is actually real and still around, hidden behind the sun. And he needs them to go there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T14:39:22-07:00","id":1560907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560887#post1560887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demonstrate.<br /> <br /> You literally just said that everything in the game that we have for Caine's existence are religious texts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not the user you replied to, but the Kuei-Jin are proof that different strains of vampirism exist, making the likelihood that 13 individuals would develop the same strain approach zero. And things lile Caitiff and Baali are proof that it is the same strain. <br /> <br /> That said, none of this proves the Book of Nod. The Antedeluvians could be the Second Generation, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T14:44:44-07:00","id":1560909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560907#post1560907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, not the user you replied to, but the Kuei-Jin are proof that different strains of vampirism exist, making the likelihood that 13 individuals would develop the same strain approach zero. And things lile Caitiff and Baali are proof that it is the same strain.<br /> <br /> That said, none of this proves the Book of Nod. The Antedeluvians could be the Second Generation, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kuei-Jin are a completely different species of parasitic undead. Like Ming Xiao once said, calling them &quot;eastern vampires&quot; is a &quot;grave misnomer.&quot;<br /> <br /> Their dietary habits and manner of procreation are completely different. They start off eating human flesh, then evolve to drinking blood, and finally gain the power to consume chi.<br /> <br /> Not only that, but they are the souls of people who managed to escape the pits of Hell and came back to life by possessing whatever corpse they were able to grab.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T14:52:22-07:00","id":1560910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560909#post1560909\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Kuei-Jin are a completely different species of parasitic undead. Like Ming Xiao once said, calling them &quot;eastern vampires&quot; is a &quot;grave misnomer.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>They are not Kindred, but they are vampires. That is my point. Besides, Ming Xiao lies almost as often as LaCroix. <br /> <br /> Alright, how about the Jiang-Shi? They get a mention in &quot;Gods &amp; Monsters.&quot; Completely different vampire type. There is no law of reality that says that all vampires must come from the same curse, or manifest the same core weaknesses, or spread their curse the same way, but all Kindred do, even Caitiff. Thus, logically speaking, all Kindred have a common source, whether that's Caine, or Lilith, or even Abel if you want to get Hyronist, or something else. <br /> <br /> There's also the issue of the Path of Blood spell which determines Generation. If the Generation determined by the spell lines up with the Generation that they should be according to the Book of Nod, that evidences the Book of Nod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T15:04:15-07:00","id":1560913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560910#post1560910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They are not Kindred, but they are vampires. That is my point. Besides, Ming Xiao lies almost as often as LaCroix.<br /> <br /> Alright, how about the Jiang-Shi? They get a mention in &quot;Gods &amp; Monsters.&quot; Completely different vampire type. There is no law of reality that says that all vampires must come from the same curse, or manifest the same core weaknesses, or spread their curse the same way, but all Kindred do, even Caitiff. Thus, logically speaking, all Kindred have a common source, whether that's Caine, or Lilith, or even Abel if you want to get Hyronist, or something else.<br /> <br /> There's also the issue of the Path of Blood spell which determines Generation. If the Generation determined by the spell lines up with the Generation that they should be according to the Book of Nod, that evidences the Book of Nod.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The way I see it, it's kind of like comparing a mosquito, to a vampire bat. Yes, they both drink blood, and yes they both fly around, but that doesn't make them the same thing.<br /> <br /> Kuei-Jin even have the ability to consume mortal foods, as stated by Ming Xiao herself, and is further demonstrated by the existence of the Thrashing Dragons.<br /> <br /> <br /> ----------------------<br /> <br /> For another comparison, we could look at the Hengeyokai. Which is just what people in the east call their Fera population. The only difference separating Hengeyokai from Fera is their cultural behavior. But in terms of functionality, they're one in the same.<br /> <br /> That can not be said for Kuei Jin and Cainites. They are noticeably and heavily divergent from each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T16:49:32-07:00","id":1560916,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560913#post1560913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That can not be said for Kuei Jin and Cainites. They are noticeably and heavily divergent from each other.</div> </div> </div> </div>That. Was. My. Point. The 13 Clans of Caine very clearly have a common origin that they do not share with the Kuei-Jin. That is evidence pointing towards Caine's existence. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T20:01:36-07:00","id":1560918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560916#post1560916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That. Was. My. Point. The 13 Clans of Caine very clearly have a common origin that they do not share with the Kuei-Jin. That is evidence pointing towards Caine's existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, you could have a scenario where the 13 Antedeluvians were the first vampires, or the Second Generation were the first vampires and there was no Caine or first vampire. Instead you had a group of vampires get together, they maybe performed some sort of ritual and were all transformed into kindred at the same time. It's not impossible to come up with an alternative that bypasses the idea of a first vampire entirely.<br /> <br /> The thing is though, White Wolf never really took things in that direction and pretty much always presented the setting as having a singular first vampire. Even in non-noddist traditions like the Settites or the African vampires, there was always the idea of a singular individual who was the first vampire and spread the curse to others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T20:14:09-07:00","id":1560920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560918#post1560918\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean, you could have a scenario where the 13 Antedeluvians were the first vampires, or the Second Generation were the first vampires and there was no Caine or first vampire. Instead you had a group of vampires get together, they maybe performed some sort of ritual and were all transformed into kindred at the same time. It's not impossible to come up with an alternative that bypasses the idea of a first vampire entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much what the Tremere did, but they needed to use some previously existing vampire blood to pull it off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-23T20:36:35-07:00","id":1560921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560902#post1560902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be the nitpickiest, Lilith is mentioned in the Hebrew Bible (Isaiah, IIRC), although most translators translate the mention to her as &quot;the night-owl,&quot; &quot;owl-demon,&quot; or &quot;night-demon,&quot; rather than keeping the Hebrew intact. And the Lilith being part of the Eden narrative is late ancient, not medieval.</div> </div> </div> </div>OK, since I need to break this out every once and awhile:<br /> <br /> I have four years of training in Biblical Hebrew. This is something that happens a lot when people that don't know Hebrew make claims about what's in the texts. &quot;Lilith&quot; as a proper noun never appears in the Hebrew Bible, the lines in Isaiah (34:13-15) is a list of animalistic plagues that befall Edom. In the Masoretic text lilit is presented in the singular, but in the Dead Sea Scrolls its in the plural (in line with the wild cats, and jackals presented in both versions). This context is why no serious scholars of the text consider this a reference to Lilith as a character, and thus the translation is rendered as either a nocturnal bird (to keep with everything else in the list being an animal), or a type of night demon (in keeping with the messy etymology of the root L-L-T in the early Semitic languages and a possible conflation with a type of Babylonian spirit with a similar phonetic structure). There's nothing in the base structure of the noun (esp. with the Dead Sea Scroll findings), it's context within the wider verse, or the context of the larger verses around it to indicate that the word is meant to be a proper noun name of a specific character &quot;Lilith,&quot; and is instead meant to be part of a list of creatures that render Edom uninhabitable to human life. Whatever you want to translate lilit as, it has to make sense as a group of otherwise normal animals that have come to feast on the carrion and gore of the slaughter of the Edomites and their livestock.<br /> <br /> The Wisdom of Sirach - the book from antiquity - does not contain Lilith in any of the preserved traditions or manuscripts. Though the text is primarily preserved in Greek translation and the Greek translations of Isaiah didn't keep lilit either and that passage is kinda of a jumble of minor Greek supernatural creatures, and we only have fragments of Hebrew versions of the text. So it is, in theory, possible the original text in Hebrew did use L-L-T in some way, but we have nothing to indicate that's the case. The Alphabet of Ben Sirach is a medieval text that is attributed to the son of the guy the wrote the text from antiquity but there's not evidence of this being a true connection. That's where we see the early evidence of the Lilith of Eden.<br /> <br /> So, no, nitpick not accepted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T01:04:19-07:00","id":1560928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560920#post1560920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's pretty much what the Tremere did, but they needed to use some previously existing vampire blood to pull it off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nagarajah as well. In the older editions they were presented as a weird group of mages that became vampires by mimicking the curse of Caine, but in V20 they were officially classified as an off-branch of the Setites. So yeah, it seems like the designers never wanted to have an actual Kindred line that didn't descend from Caine. Even the clans that 'self embraced' still used the vitae from actual vampires. But at the same time, if someone wanted to, they could easily run a game without Caine or a first vampire without ever actually breaking canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T05:32:49-07:00","id":1560933,"title":"","content":"Caine is not a vampire. He is a cursed immortal Mage (of the awakened variety) with a corrupted viral avatar that spreads itself through his blood. The first known &quot;vampire&quot; would be Enoch/Enosh. Caine was cursed by Adam. The God entity (Yahweh, El, Personage of Jade, the Gift Bringer, the One, Prime, take your pick) was gone from the world/shattered by the time of Caine. Caine being cast out to wander, meets Lilith and she bleeds in a bowl for him to awaken him. She warns him that since he is cursed already the awakening my have consequences. Its during his awakening that the &quot;curses&quot; of vampirism appear: Weakness to Fire, Weakness to Sunlight, Need to feed on Blood, Anything you build turns to Ash. During his awakening his avatar takes on the form of the angels, and after he has his disciplines. He immediately leaves Lilith after gaining power, and wanders for millennia, till he gets lonely and decides to take over what would become the first city/Enoch.<br /> <br /> Adam, Eve, and Lilith all ate from the Tree of Knowledge, Lilith also ate from the Tree of Life. They have the equivilant of Awakened Avatars due to the Fruit of Knowledge. Adam's fate is a mystery. Eve shows up in time as the Lady of Fate in the underworld, where she is not a Wraith. Lilith exists as basically an Incarna in her own pocket dimension garden. Abel is the first wraith, and being kept in a Memory Tower.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T11:24:26-07:00","id":1560938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560887#post1560887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Demonstrate.<br /> <br /> You literally just said that everything in the game that we have for Caine's existence are religious texts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I literally never said that, c'mon. <br /> <br /> Gehenna is the official ending of the VtM. It discusses official information on Antediluvians and, yes, Caine. To quote:<br /> <br /> &quot; As the end of the world approaches <b>the founder of the feast</b>(highlight mine) deserves a special mention. Were if not for Caine, vampires would (probably) never exist&quot;. <br /> <br /> So that is that. Yes, Caine was sometimes presented as a myth and there were alternate vampire origins presented here and there but as Mark Rein-Hagen imagined it, Caine was always the father of vampire race. Again, I understand the desire to keep it vague or even make it a lie in your games but this is one of the few things that is pretty certain. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T11:34:39-07:00","id":1560939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560889#post1560889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of Beckket's friends (a Malkavian) even came across Tzimisce, and immediately proceeded to swan dive into its biomass when he realized what that meant.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I personally disagree with the notion that the Caine mythos is heavily rooted in Christian dogma, due to the fact they introduced figures like Lilith into the story. Lilith comes from the hebrew scripture, and is not mentioned within Christianity.<br /> <br /> Lilith's existence kind of throws the whole concept of Adam and Eve being responsible for original sin out the window, since she was the one who originally defied God by refusing to be submissive to Adam, and refusing a direct order to return to the Garden of Eden after she ran off. Caine also can't have been the one who originally taught Angels the concept of murder, when they threatened to kill 1,000 of Lilith's children every day as punishment for her defiance.<br /> <br /> Lilith, drawing upon giga chad energy, vowed that she would birth 2,000 children to counteract their efforts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Given that a recurring theme with the curse of vampirism seems to be you becoming mentally or culturally stagnant in whatever time period you were at the time of your embrace, I'd say they remember very well.<br /> <br /> Bare in mind, the Antedeluvians were originally sired during the earliest days of humanity's development. They are 10's of thousands of years old at the very least, with the possibility of being 100's. The degree of barbarism and cruelty they inflict upon the world was common place back when they were alive, so they probably don't think anything of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's funny that you quoted me and disagreed with me... on thing I never mentioned. I said nothing about Christian dogma. When I mentioned religious bias I meant noddism. <br /> <br /> Also, just because VtM mythos draws from myths different than Christian does not mean that Christian myths are not heavily used. <br /> <br /> Also being mentally stagnant and remembering what has happened over 10 millenia ago are wildly different things. Especially if you had emotional reaction about those things. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T11:57:56-07:00","id":1560940,"title":"","content":"[QUOTE=sathriel;n1560938]&quot; Were if not for Caine, vampires would (<i><u><b>probably</b></u></i>) never exist&quot;.<br /> <br /> Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> Your own choice of quote undermines your claim. MR*H also didn't write for the book you quoted, nor is he the sole authority on the original intentions of VtM. There were other people that created the first WoD material with him.<br /> <br /> Even beyond that, the ToJ books are all present as possible scenarios. Some of them outright contradict each other on answers to deep lore mysteries in the game(s).<br /> <br /> So.... not really a solid choice to back up your position. The games want the truth of the matter to be optional, not just fans. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T12:07:45-07:00","id":1560941,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560939#post1560939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny that you quoted me and disagreed with me... on thing I never mentioned. I said nothing about Christian dogma. When I mentioned religious bias I meant noddism.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I misunderstood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560939#post1560939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also being mentally stagnant and remembering what has happened over 10 millenia ago are wildly different things. Especially if you had emotional reaction about those things.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do vampires still get emotional reactions, or is that just a tool they use for manipulation? Because if it's the former, that kind of spits in the face of the Brujah.<br /> <br /> Absimiliard seems pretty dead set on regaining his lost beauty, even though it was precisely because he was so obsessed over it, that lead to him being cursed in the first place.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T12:13:27-07:00","id":1560942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560940#post1560940\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Even beyond that, the ToJ books are all present as possible scenarios. Some of them outright contradict each other on answers to deep lore mysteries in the game(s).<br /> <br /> So.... not really a solid choice to back up your position. The games want the truth of the matter to be optional, not just fans.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which makes discussing the game frustrating, because I am constantly met with arguments to the contrary, whenever I bring up anything regarding the setting or lore.<br /> <br /> Like, I get them wanting to give players a sense of freedom, but there has to be some form of established cannon when it comes to this shit. Otherwise, your just wasting your ink when you spend several pages of the book writing a story, instead of telling us how to play the game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T13:54:27-07:00","id":1560943,"title":"","content":"Why do you think Exalted, Scion, Trinity, the CofD, and Curseborne have all moved away from the WoD style of metaplot and lore presentation?<br /> <br /> The WoD is a 35 year old game. It is full of old decisions that haven't aged well from mechanics to lore. There doesn't have to be an established lore, it would just be much nicer for these sorts of discussion if there was. Text in the books is only wasted if people never use it. If nobody ever uses it? That's bad. If a dozen groups use the setting two dozen different ways... then it's not a waste because the variety and lore inconsistencies still resulted in people playing and having fun; which is the primary goal of a game, not people debating stuff online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T14:11:36-07:00","id":1560946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560943#post1560943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do you think Exalted, Scion, Trinity, the CofD, and Curseborne have all moved away from the WoD style of metaplot and lore presentation?<br /> <br /> The WoD is a 35 year old game. It is full of old decisions that haven't aged well from mechanics to lore. There doesn't have to be an established lore, it would just be much nicer for these sorts of discussion if there was. Text in the books is only wasted if people never use it. If nobody ever uses it? That's bad. If a dozen groups use the setting two dozen different ways... then it's not a waste because the variety and lore inconsistencies still resulted in people playing and having fun; which is the primary goal of a game, not people debating stuff online.</div> </div> </div> </div>Chronicles got it right, by rebooting the franchise from scratch, and presenting each chronicle as their own self contained stories. None of the 'unreliable narrator' gimmick making a mess of things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T14:57:24-07:00","id":1560947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560896#post1560896\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thing about that, the story of Jesus is plagiarized from the mythology of a previously established Sun God, who was themselves a plagiarism, who was also a plagiarism, who was also a plagiarism, est.<br /> <br /> Saying that anything is rooted in Christian dogma is kind of funny, when they're not even the ones who originally came up with it. They're just the most recent in a long line of copycats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Adding to what Heavy Arms said earlier, on a broader stroke:<br /> <br /> This is not about the origin of the stories. It's about systems of thought and belief, about culture. About a Christian story not telling the same message as a Jewish or Muslim story even when they're literally telling their versions of the same story.<br /> <br /> It's about anthropology, not comic book copyright laws.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JagneStormskull</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560907#post1560907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, not the user you replied to, but the Kuei-Jin are proof that different strains of vampirism exist, making the likelihood that 13 individuals would develop the same strain approach zero.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, while the first conclusion is true, the second does not follow.<br /> <br /> We don't know the nature of the Kindred condition, and without that we can't infer anything about their links beyond the mere fact there's something.<br /> <br /> The very Kuei-Jin demonstrate this problem: as independently escaped souls with no process for procreation, they're each and all the first of their line, they are not a continuous species.<br /> <br /> Yet, they share traits because those derive not from each specific undead, but the process that spawned them.<br /> <br /> So we can, indeed, say something for sure: the Antes were created either by the same process or with some crucial common element to their origins. That's absolutely true. But it can be as far apart still as just some form of convergent evolution plus survival bias.<br /> <br /> Let's propose a wild thesis: Kindred lineages are independent events of Awakened Immortality attempts. Such attempts can cause a lot of distinct effects, though. But the result doesn't depend only on the paradigm, but other hitherto unknown circumstances.<br /> <br /> In this thesis, Immortal Mages can take a variety of forms and effects, but some clusters are statistically favored. The Avatar breaks in such and such ways, Quintessence must be processed from certain classes of sources. The Magick can't continue for some reason, or it spoils true immortality.<br /> <br /> Even then, only about 4% of the processes generate a Kindred. This is not a single species but rather a likely configuration. What if from the other 96% a majority simply doesn't work so well after a few centuries? Some wander to other realms, some are too fragile or have even worse weaknesses. Some even survive, just are not as numerous and regarded as Bygones.<br /> <br /> Given the span of time we're potentially talking, this could be the whole of the Antediluvian origin. They're exactly like the Tremere and the original version of the Nagaraja. It's even possible that they didn't held the power of the 3rd Generation at first, but as firsts they were not normal vampires, working through an actual Blood Potency rule.<br /> <br /> Do I think this is the best explanation? Not by far. But it is 100% compatible with the canon. And methods to identify Generation? The number is just a label. You get the strength of the Blood, and Generation is the language you're provided to explain your results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560938#post1560938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I literally never said that, c'mon.<br /> <br /> Gehenna is the official ending of the VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reread your previous post. You did.<br /> <br /> And the book Gehenna is divided in three parts: the Withering that's actual canon, a discussion on what the authors held as headcanon but deliberately kept open-ended, and the four scenarios that, by the way, not only contradict each other, they also contradict the second part, where your quote comes from.<br /> <br /> The key point: deliberately kept open-ended. It's how almost every book was written in the game outside novels, kept open-ended on purpose because this is a mystery setting by default, the author can give all the smart nods and winks they want as long as they keep enough ambiguity.\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560942#post1560942\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which makes discussing the game frustrating, because I am constantly met with arguments to the contrary, whenever I bring up anything regarding the setting or lore.<br /> <br /> Like, I get them wanting to give players a sense of freedom, but there has to be some form of established cannon when it comes to this shit. Otherwise, your just wasting your ink when you spend several pages of the book writing a story, instead of telling us how to play the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>There <b><i>is </i></b>a canon.<br /> <br /> It's in the narration itself.<br /> <br /> What makes the unreliable narrator approach tick is that it shows you the now and how the narrative affects it.<br /> <br /> Caine being real isn't important. Thin-Bloods being hunted because of old stories is. Undead monsters risking their existence for old paper fragment is. What a Prince is wiling to sacrifice and risk for a big box with a mummy (or bomb) is.<br /> <br /> All By Nights are canon iirc, adventures, several events within the many books. But is a canon made of perspective and stories, not of out-of-character facts.<br /> <br /> Most important, though, the unreliability itself is canon, and the most important one. The fact no one can say for sure. The uncertainty if what you're told is sincere or a lie. The game of interests.<br /> <br /> You misunderstood in one point: it is not about giving players a sense of freedom. Other games give far more. It's about keeping the mystery and paranoia that's foundational to the kind of horror and drama being played. Giving the ST a baseline story that is meant to be twisted. To tell a lie in the book in preparation for a reveal in the table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-24T21:31:01-07:00","id":1560955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560947#post1560947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There <b><i>is </i></b>a canon.<br /> <br /> It's in the narration itself.<br /> <br /> What makes the unreliable narrator approach tick is that it shows you the now and how the narrative affects it.<br /> <br /> Caine being real isn't important. Thin-Bloods being hunted because of old stories is. Undead monsters risking their existence for old paper fragment is. What a Prince is wiling to sacrifice and risk for a big box with a mummy (or bomb) is.<br /> <br /> All By Nights are canon iirc, adventures, several events within the many books. But is a canon made of perspective and stories, not of out-of-character facts.<br /> <br /> Most important, though, the unreliability itself is canon, and the most important one. The fact no one can say for sure. The uncertainty if what you're told is sincere or a lie. The game of interests.<br /> <br /> You misunderstood in one point: it is not about giving players a sense of freedom. Other games give far more. It's about keeping the mystery and paranoia that's foundational to the kind of horror and drama being played. Giving the ST a baseline story that is meant to be twisted. To tell a lie in the book in preparation for a reveal in the table.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't like it. Given my neurological condition, I don't like when things are left up to interpretation, or surrounded by nuance. My brain always comes away with a radically different conclusion than what the original creator was going for, and then it makes me feel lesser for not understanding it.<br /> <br /> I need things to be spelled out, clear cut, no room for misinterpretation. When the story fails to provide that, it leaves me confused and frustrated.<br /> <br /> I do love the World of Darkness franchise, don't get me wrong. But the metaplot was a mistake, and getting rid of it was the right call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T01:44:41-07:00","id":1560957,"title":"","content":"While I appreciate this is not solely a matter of personal choice, I think you're letting your flavor of neuro-spicy cause friction that you don't need to struggle with.<br /> <br /> TTRPG books are not written to tell you a story. They're written to facilitate you and your group telling your own stories. Premade settings are a tool for your group to use. The intent of a premade setting, metaplot, and so on is to inspire you to have fun. The creators' intent isn't to communicate an explicit &quot;truth&quot; you have to follow, their intent is to plant seeds that you'll tend to and grow as you see fit. Having a radically different head-canon for your games than what the devs and authors were thinking is not a lack of understanding... it's part of their intention for the setting. They know perfectly well people are going to have different interpretations and they intended to encourage it with enough structure that the game doesn't fall apart as long as a given interpretation does get too far from the base conceits of the game(s).<br /> <br /> It feels strange to me for you to point to the CofD as it's a far less spelled out setting than the WoD. The CofD might not lean as hard on unreliable narrators, but the authorial voices of the games are still bent heavily towards &quot;here's three to five different possible ideas of why this might be the case, none of them are officially The Reason, and you're free to make up your own.&quot; So the setting is just as open to personal takes as the WoD is. At best what the CofD accomplishes is communicate that intent better.<br /> <br /> To repeat myself a bit, the CofD was created by WoD creators. Yes, that does means they got to make improvements based on their previous experiences, but broadly if you get it when the CofD does something... the odds are you get it when the WoD does it too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T01:48:11-07:00","id":1560958,"title":"","content":"For hatever reasom Quote function does not work for me so here we go: <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> Excuse me what? Yes, maybe if Caine wasn't cursed someone else would be the First Murderer and became the First Vampire but it's a hypothetical matter because he was and he became. So no, it doesn't undermine my argument.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> No, I didn't.<br /> <br /> And there is also fourth part, about Caine which the quote comes from. And it states pretty clearly that Caine is/was a First Vampire even if it presents other options. Again, the possibility of different options does not mean that there is not one that is considered &quot;canon&quot; FWIW. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29009_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29009\" data-vbnamecard=\"29009\">DarkKing</a> Your hang ups aside you are wrong. Metaplot is part of why VtM and WoD as a whole became so popular. Anyone who was there in the 90s/early 2000s remember the constant arguments about the history and canon of the world (kinda like this one). I might disagree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> but she is right, WoD is a mystery and it's success was built on the ambiguity and enigmas built-in. <br /> <br /> It's the same thing that made Lost, Severance or Pluribus so popular: people rushing to the forums and subreddits, discussing the revelations and their meanings with their friends and getting emotionally invested in wanting to see a continuation.<br /> <br /> Also nWoD and WoD5 might point to you being wrong as well but it's safe to say that there were other problems there other than &quot;do away with the metaplot&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T02:23:38-07:00","id":1560959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560958#post1560958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29009_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29009\" data-vbnamecard=\"29009\">DarkKing</a> Your hang ups aside you are wrong. Metaplot is part of why VtM and WoD as a whole became so popular. Anyone who was there in the 90s/early 2000s remember the constant arguments about the history and canon of the world (kinda like this one). I might disagree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> but she is right, WoD is a mystery and it's success was built on the ambiguity and enigmas built-in.<br /> <br /> It's the same thing that made Lost, Severance or Pluribus so popular: people rushing to the forums and subreddits, discussing the revelations and their meanings with their friends and getting emotionally invested in wanting to see a continuation.<br /> <br /> Also nWoD and WoD5 might point to you being wrong as well but it's safe to say that there were other problems there other than &quot;do away with the metaplot&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's strange, because I was lead to believe the ToJ scenarios were created specifically because the metaplot had become nearly impossible for new players to wrap their heads around.<br /> <br /> So they introduced a climactic finale to the setting, and then rebooted it with Chronicles.<br /> <br /> Only for them to resurrect the game 20 years later, with a new metaplot that most people seem to collectively agree is shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T02:34:39-07:00","id":1560960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560957#post1560957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I appreciate this is not solely a matter of personal choice, I think you're letting your flavor of neuro-spicy cause friction that you don't need to struggle with.<br /> <br /> TTRPG books are not written to tell you a story. They're written to facilitate you and your group telling your own stories. Premade settings are a tool for your group to use. The intent of a premade setting, metaplot, and so on is to inspire you to have fun. The creators' intent isn't to communicate an explicit &quot;truth&quot; you have to follow, their intent is to plant seeds that you'll tend to and grow as you see fit. Having a radically different head-canon for your games than what the devs and authors were thinking is not a lack of understanding... it's part of their intention for the setting. They know perfectly well people are going to have different interpretations and they intended to encourage it with enough structure that the game doesn't fall apart as long as a given interpretation does get too far from the base conceits of the game(s).</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand that, but I try to remain true to established lore and canon as much as possible.<br /> <br /> It's my way of showing my passion for the franchise, and respect for the creator's vision.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560957#post1560957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It feels strange to me for you to point to the CofD as it's a far less spelled out setting than the WoD. The CofD might not lean as hard on unreliable narrators, but the authorial voices of the games are still bent heavily towards &quot;here's three to five different possible ideas of why this might be the case, none of them are officially The Reason, and you're free to make up your own.&quot; So the setting is just as open to personal takes as the WoD is. At best what the CofD accomplishes is communicate that intent better.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why it gets a pass, is because it never claimed to have a metaplot in the first place. Straight from the get-go, it's been introduced as a sandbox narrative, where ST's are free to make up whatever setting they want. I don't need to consult the lore, because I decide what the lore is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T02:51:05-07:00","id":1560963,"title":"","content":"I think it's fair to say what WW said and what it did weren't always the same thing, while it's human nature to spot patterns and try to find answers. Therefore, I think it's perfectly fine to say the WoD often (but not always) wanted things to be ambiguous, while at the same time sticking very closely to one core &quot;mythos&quot; for each game (Noddism in VTM, Gaia in WTA, the Purple Paradigm in MTAs, etc.).<br /> <br /> That's why one player can honestly see one mythos as truer than another in practice, while another honestly sees the truth in the ambiguity instead. Both are and were true at different times and under different authors. And that's one of the things I like about the WoD\u2014two people who enjoy it can be enjoying entirely different parts of the game.<br /> <br /> With that said, is it perhaps worth bringing it back to the topic of the Sabbat so we don't get too off-track? For instance, I think that subjective dimension is also why the Sabbat is relatively popular both IC and OOC. It also has that element of &quot;people see what they want to see&quot;.<br /> <br /> Vasantasena likely has no doubt she's fighting for freedom from the elders and sees that as the sect's aim. She was joined by those Malkavians who refused to give up Dementation, seeing it as a useful oracular tool as well as a part of themselves. For those Cainites, it's a check against the abuses of the elders and a commitment to being who or what you truly are.<br /> <br /> But a member of the <i>Amici Noctis </i>might see the sect's aim as providing them with power and allowing them to pursue their interests without interference from meddling Ventrue. Many elder Tzimisce see it in the same way. In fact, the elders of both clans only really joined the sect because a) they couldn't bare bending the knee to their ancient rivals and b) because, after the supposed diablerie of their Antediluvians, they knew the anarchs would come after them if they didn't pick the right side in the Anarch Revolt. Gratiani and Lugoj basically committed acts of terrorism, providing perfect propaganda to motivate the anarchs in their clans.<br /> <br /> The Black Hand (or Lost Tribe) likely sees the sect as a weapon of vengeance against the Antediluvians. The Knights of the Blood, before they became a pillar of the Ventrue <i>antitribu</i> and the Path of Honourable Accord, saw it as a way to fight the Daeva and wage holy war. They're still fighting the same holy war today, with the Antediluvians as the Daeva and the Camarilla as their agents.<br /> <br /> The orthodox Albigensians likely see the sect as the means through which to serve the Demiurge as mankind's jailers. The heretical Cathars likely think they're mankind's liberators through almost identical means. These two groups descend from the Road of Sin, with elements from the individualist, antiheroic Path of the Devil (<i>Via Adversarius</i>), the sadistic Path of Cruelty (<i>Via Crudelitas</i>), and the decadent Path of Pleasure (<i>Via Voluptarius</i>). The Path of Screams (<i>Via Quiritare</i>) obviously gave way to the infernalists who follow the Path of (Evil) Revelations. All of these groups find shelter in the Sabbat as a vehicle for the paths and as a place where their actions won't necessarily be considered grounds for destruction.<br /> <br /> The Black Angels and Nihilists have yet another slight variant on dualist/gnostic beliefs that aren't really all that different from the Path of Cathari and the Path of Redemption, and which essentially boil down to them being instruments of Satan (the former) or of divine punishment (the latter), with a bunch of Abyss Mysticism thrown into the mix. The Black Angels' philosophy specifically derives from the Road of the Devil, although the modern Path of Night seems to also borrow from the Road of Heaven and parts of the Road of Sin. The Sabbat gives them ample cover for their actions, especially as they blend in so well with the rest of the Lasombra and members of other paths.<br /> <br /> The Shepherds of Caine and the Redeemers are also inheritors of the Road of Heaven, which included the anti-infernalist Order of the Chanticleer (possibly a template for the later Sabbat Inquisition). They seek to understand evil so they can master it and find redemption, and the Sabbat is the only suitable vehicle for that. (There's a common theme of the Sabbat's religious elements being a perfect cover for Gnostic, radical, and even infernalist leanings.)<br /> <br /> This means the Sabbat is never without a purpose to <i>someone</i>. And that's probably what helps keep it going. The sect leans so much on the pack mentality that it's designed to keep people riled up. You only need one person in a pack to care about the cause, and they can rile everyone else up. So many of these groups are bound through doctrine (paths, eschatology, Noddism in general), ritual (ritae, the religious practices of paths and the sect as a whole) and blood (Vinculi, rejection of a parent clan, unity as Clanless, banding together for safety) that it causes a chain reaction.<br /> <br /> They're also always fighting something (the Camarilla, the Ancients, ideology), so they don't have time to stop and think too hard about all their differences. When they run out of enemies, that tends to be when they turn on each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T03:08:23-07:00","id":1560965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560960#post1560960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Straight from the get-go, it's been introduced as a sandbox narrative, where ST's are free to make up whatever setting they want. I don't need to consult the lore, because I decide what the lore is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that is more common wisdom that is not actually correct. Like, the latter 2e CofD books lean into explicit sandbox stuff more, but even then, there are still large parts of the setting that are presented as hard fact. (Hell, given Dark Eras, there are potentially many more hard facts in CofD than in WoD.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T03:14:51-07:00","id":1560966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560965#post1560965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that is more common wisdom that is not actually correct. Like, the latter 2e CofD books lean into explicit sandbox stuff more, but even then, there are still large parts of the setting that are presented as hard fact. (Hell, given Dark Eras, there are potentially many more hard facts in CofD than in WoD.)</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I've never so much as even looked at any of the Dark Ages books, for either version of the game. Not for lack of curiosity, mind you, but more a case of being nowhere near as much of a history buff as the setting might require.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T03:22:49-07:00","id":1560967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560963#post1560963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's fair to say what WW said and what it did weren't always the same thing, while it's human nature to spot patterns and try to find answers. Therefore, I think it's perfectly fine to say the WoD often (but not always) wanted things to be ambiguous, while at the same time sticking very closely to one core &quot;mythos&quot; for each game (Noddism in VTM, Gaia in WTA, the Purple Paradigm in MTAs, etc.).<br /> <br /> That's why one player can honestly see one mythos as truer than another in practice, while another honestly sees the truth in the ambiguity instead. Both are and were true at different times and under different authors. And that's one of the things I like about the WoD\u2014two people who enjoy it can be enjoying entirely different parts of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I might need a bit of clarification on this subject, because it seems like I have misinterpreted what exactly the metaplot is supposed to be?<br /> <br /> As of the time of me writing this, my belief is that the metaplot attempts to join all the different splats together under one unified cosmology. Which causes it to immediately begin shooting sparks and emitting strange odors the second you try to cross examine them.<br /> <br /> But from the way people are talking about it on these forums, it sounds like each of the different splats has their own version of a metaplot, which applies specifically to their gameline?<br /> <br /> If that is the case, then it greatly reduces the amount of frustration I have with trying to piece the story together. But there are still tidbits which have to be dealt with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T03:49:05-07:00","id":1560968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560958#post1560958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Excuse me what? Yes, maybe if Caine wasn't cursed someone else would be the First Murderer and became the First Vampire but it's a hypothetical matter because he was and he became. So no, it doesn't undermine my argument.</div> </div> </div> </div>By what logic exactly?<br /> <br /> Your claim is that Caine is 100% absolutely the first vampire and the Noddist lore of Caine is 100% correct.<br /> <br /> Your evidence is the book saying that Caine is possibly such.<br /> <br /> That evidence does not support that claim. That's the what from my end. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And it states pretty clearly that Caine is/was a First Vampire even if it presents other options. Again, the possibility of different options does not mean that there is not one that is considered &quot;canon&quot; FWIW. </div> </div> </div>You're confusing &quot;default&quot; and &quot;canon.&quot; Canon is whatever the developers say it is. Canon is canon even if it's incomplete or contradictory. Canon literally comes from the result of a process by which some texts are considered official and some aren't; not the specifics of the contents within them. A bible is a religious canon where a bunch of theologians decided some texts got in, and others got excluded. A literary canon is when a bunch of academics get together and make an &quot;official&quot; list of books that are exemplars of a given culture/era/etc. A TTRPG canon are the official books according to the devs.<br /> <br /> The Gehenna book treats the Noddist Caine as the default for its scenarios. That's not the same as declaring it the official stance that only that take one Caine and the first vampire story are the absolute truth in the game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Your hang ups aside you are wrong. </div> </div> </div>No, DarkKing is not wrong. Opinions on the metaplot are a matter of taste. Some people love the WoD for the metaplot, and others think the metaplot is a detriment to it. I don't have the same hangups about it as our fellow poster, but I have a very similar conclusion regarding the metaplot after many decades of playing WoD games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560959#post1560959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's strange, because I was lead to believe the ToJ scenarios were created specifically because the metaplot had become nearly impossible for new players to wrap their heads around.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ToJ scenarios were created to provided endings to the games after the decision to end the WoD was made. That decision was multifaceted. A big reason was that multiple developers felt overly confined by a decade of retcons piling up and wanted a reset to make their lives easier. Opting for a hard reset in the CofD over a softer reset more akin to how WoD5 was intended is complicated and we only ever got a partial story of what happened behind the scenes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Only for them to resurrect the game 20 years later, with a new metaplot that most people seem to collectively agree is shit. </div> </div> </div>That is skipping the 2011 revival of the WoD that was kicked off by V20. V20 was not meant to be a true new edition. It was made as a one-off special idea... but it gained huge amounts of support because a lot of WoD fans didn't mesh with the direction the CofD took, and plenty of us are fans of both and appreciated having a newer version of the old games with some patches and fresh paint.<br /> <br /> Ignoring how successful the 20th books were (and were during and after Paradox's acquisition of the IP) doesn't make a lot of sense when judging Paradox's choice to revive the WoD over focus on the CofD. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560960#post1560960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that, but I try to remain true to established lore and canon as much as possible.<br /> <br /> It's my way of showing my passion for the franchise, and respect for the creator's vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why though? It's causing mental friction that's dampening your enjoyment of the game, and it's not really that respectful of the creators' vision if their vision was for you to modify the canon and lore to your tastes. If you want to focus on MR*H specifically... VtM 1e, much like the CofD, was very upfront about being more of a sandbox meant for STs to make up whatever. It was later as the game grew and grew (even just the setting, ignore the metaplot) that the tone of the franchise changed to have more things spelled out with unreliable narrators being the cover to avoid making anything too set in stone.<br /> <br /> I can't force anything here, but how you channel your passion is a choice. Surely you can understand how weird it is to see you defend picking a harder path that less enjoyable for you according to your own posts. You can make this easier on yourself, and then make these discussions more productive because you can just dissect topics for what you want to use rather what you've decided you're obligated to use.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason why it gets a pass, is because it never claimed to have a metaplot in the first place. Straight from the get-go, it's been introduced as a sandbox narrative, where ST's are free to make up whatever setting they want. I don't need to consult the lore, because I decide what the lore is. </div> </div> </div>The WoD didn't claim to have one in the first place either. Both developed metaplots over time. The CofD was just more aware of the consequences of letting the metaplot get too larger and avoided letting that happen more successfully before becoming defunct anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T03:54:08-07:00","id":1560969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560967#post1560967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I might need a bit of clarification on this subject, because it seems like I have misinterpreted what exactly the metaplot is supposed to be?</div> </div> </div> </div>A metaplot is simply a narrative that extends through multiple gaming supplements that aren't designated as being part of a specific ongoing story (so the Transylvania Chronicles don't count as having a metaplot as it's one story explicitly split up over a few books). Metaplot can be internal to the gamelines, or include multiple, or all of them. Most of the WoD metaplot is internal to the gamelines, though the end of 2e and through Revised tended to lean more into the &quot;unify the setting&quot; stuff to setup major changes from 2e to Revised, and then to help facilitate the ToJ; that is, it wasn't one concerted effort but an accumulation of different design goals moving the same direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T04:17:52-07:00","id":1560971,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560968#post1560968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why though? It's causing mental friction that's dampening your enjoyment of the game, and it's not really that respectful of the creators' vision if their vision was for you to modify the canon and lore to your tastes. If you want to focus on MR*H specifically... VtM 1e, much like the CofD, was very upfront about being more of a sandbox meant for STs to make up whatever. It was later as the game grew and grew (even just the setting, ignore the metaplot) that the tone of the franchise changed to have more things spelled out with unreliable narrators being the cover to avoid making anything too set in stone.</div> </div> </div> </div>The mental friction and dampening of enjoyment stems from the game trying to simultaneously tell me that stuff is going on in the background, while also telling me that none of that stuff is confirmed, and that I should draw my own conclusions about it.<br /> <br /> Like, if it's not confirmed one way or the other, then why even bring up the subject in the first place? It sounds like they want me to write my own story, while also trying to present their own narrative at the same time.<br /> <br /> The two settings can not coexist within the same space, due to a conflict of creative differences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T04:47:06-07:00","id":1560972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560968#post1560968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By what logic exactly?<br /> <br /> Your claim is that Caine is 100% absolutely the first vampire and the Noddist lore of Caine is 100% correct.<br /> <br /> Your evidence is the book saying that Caine is possibly such.<br /> <br /> That evidence does not support that claim. That's the what from my end.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> You're confusing &quot;default&quot; and &quot;canon.&quot; Canon is whatever the developers say it is. Canon is canon even if it's incomplete or contradictory. Canon literally comes from the result of a process by which some texts are considered official and some aren't; not the specifics of the contents within them. A bible is a religious canon where a bunch of theologians decided some texts got in, and others got excluded. A literary canon is when a bunch of academics get together and make an &quot;official&quot; list of books that are exemplars of a given culture/era/etc. A TTRPG canon are the official books according to the devs.<br /> <br /> The Gehenna book treats the Noddist Caine as the default for its scenarios. That's not the same as declaring it the official stance that only that take one Caine and the first vampire story are the absolute truth in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, DarkKing is not wrong. Opinions on the metaplot are a matter of taste. Some people love the WoD for the metaplot, and others think the metaplot is a detriment to it. I don't have the same hangups about it as our fellow poster, but I have a very similar conclusion regarding the metaplot after many decades of playing WoD games.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The ToJ scenarios were created to provided endings to the games after the decision to end the WoD was made. That decision was multifaceted. A big reason was that multiple developers felt overly confined by a decade of retcons piling up and wanted a reset to make their lives easier. Opting for a hard reset in the CofD over a softer reset more akin to how WoD5 was intended is complicated and we only ever got a partial story of what happened behind the scenes.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>All I said that Caine is the First Vampire. The rest is your projection. And as for the Noddists' lore I even specifically said that their texts are clearly biased due to religious and or political bias. <br /> <br /> I don't even know what 100% true means. All I said was that as how the world was conceptualised by Hagen and different line developers over the years Caine was always considered the First Vampire. Gehenna does not say that Caine is possibly a First Vampire. You read the quote, right? <br /> <br /> Oh no, I thought we were supposed to refrain from discussing religion because it does not end up well? And comparing Bible to VtM is silly in reference to canon anyway. Despite to what some crazy VtM fans might think, vampires are not real, and VtM was created as an entertainment. Mark Rein-Hagen and most of it's writers are still alive and we can talk with them about their ideas. <br /> <br /> He is fine with having whatever preference about the way VtM/WoD are written but he is in minority. So there you go, not wrong just in minority. Metaplot is/was an important part of the setting for many players and as I said, a big part of the reason Vampire became so popular in the 90s. <br /> <br /> Agreed about the Time of Judgment, the reasons were many. Computers and consoles started to be more popular and TTRPGs started to falter so the higher-ups at White Wolf decided to make a shake up that is going to bring them more money. It worked only for the initial Requiem corebook. And the rest is history. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T05:02:23-07:00","id":1560973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560971#post1560971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The mental friction and dampening of enjoyment stems from the game trying to simultaneously tell me that stuff is going on in the background, while also telling me that none of that stuff is confirmed, and that I should draw my own conclusions about it.<br /> <br /> Like, if it's not confirmed one way or the other, then why even bring up the subject in the first place? It sounds like they want me to write my own story, while also trying to present their own narrative at the same time.<br /> <br /> The two settings can not coexist within the same space, due to a conflict of creative differences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because they do, that's why it's a storytelling system and why the golden rule exist in RPGs.<br /> <br /> But I get where you are coming from because as much as I love the ambiguity and open options I am a bit annoyed that Keith Baker refuses to give any concrete information what's caused the Mourning in Eberron.<br /> <br /> So that is the issue with metaplot, RPGs are not novels. When you are reading Lord of the Rings you are following the story that the writer put his merry gang of hobbits, humans and assorted miscreants in. But in RPGs you are creating your own stories and you're using as much or as little of what the writers conceived of the world. And hence metaplot is a &quot;damned if you do, damned if you don't&quot; kinda thing. If you make the metaplot too rigid some people will be annoyed that it's hamstringing their play (kinda what happened with WoD5 what with blowing up Sabbat, making them a bunch of homicidal hobos or making a nazi cult out of Get of Fenris). On the other hand if you make the story to vague and open-ended you risk of angering players like you, that prefer to have the answers spelled out. Ultimately the vagueness is understandable when you consider one of Rein-Hagen's answers about the concept for Caine and VtM as a whole<br /> <br /> &quot;Actually, Steward Wieck had a comic book where Caine was a Vampire and I asked him if I could borrow it... and since he was my business partner, he said hell yes. That was the big turning point actually. Until then I was trying to shy away from religion. After that... I went all in. The game and the world became about religion and belief.<br /> <br /> My father was a Lutheran minister, and I think that played a huge role in not only Vampire but the whole WoD series. I was always fascinated by what made people believe so strongly when I didn't seem to believe at all. Talking about that theme, the power of belief, fueled the second half of Vampire game design.&quot;<br /> <br /> To my mind this is the big reason why WoD5 rubs a lot of people wrong way because they have tried to mix up the approach of oWoD (heavy ambiguous metaplot) with nWoD (metaplot agnostic) and ultimately they made both groups of fans unhappy. YMMV of course. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T05:29:00-07:00","id":1560974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560973#post1560973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So that is the issue with metaplot, RPGs are not novels. When you are reading Lord of the Rings you are following the story that the writer put his merry gang of hobbits, humans and assorted miscreants in. But in RPGs you are creating your own stories and you're using as much or as little of what the writers conceived of the world. And hence metaplot is a &quot;damned if you do, damned if you don't&quot; kinda thing. If you make the metaplot too rigid some people will be annoyed that it's hamstringing their play (kinda what happened with WoD5 what with blowing up Sabbat, making them a bunch of homicidal hobos or making a nazi cult out of Get of Fenris). On the other hand if you make the story to vague and open-ended you risk of angering players like you, that prefer to have the answers spelled out. Ultimately the vagueness is understandable when you consider one of Rein-Hagen's answers about the concept for Caine and VtM as a whole<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>According to Demon, Hell was a place reserved exclusively for the rebellious angels, and humans were never actually tossed in there. Also, the arch angels cursed humanity to forget the knowledge of how to return from the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Then the Kuei Jin claims that humans actually were tossed into Hell, but they found a way to escape and became &quot;kindred of the east.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then Wraith presents the afterlife as a place of infinite depression, where the only escape is to either succumb to Oblivion, or to resolve whatever Fetters tether you to this existence.<br /> <br /> Then Mage claims that people keep reincarnating into multiple lives over and over, thus allowing them to continue the path of Ascension if they failed to get it right the previous time.<br /> <br /> And Werewolf presents the idea that powerful individuals may become ancestral spirits upon their deaths and continue to guide their descendants.<br /> <br /> Then Mummy claims that Duat exists, and the judges there can just make you immortal if they decide to accept you as a servant.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness afterlife is a cluster fuck of contradictions, and I do not enjoy it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T06:27:57-07:00","id":1560975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560974#post1560974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to Demon, Hell was a place reserved exclusively for the rebellious angels, and humans were never actually tossed in there. Also, the arch angels cursed humanity to forget the knowledge of how to return from the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Then the Kuei Jin claims that humans actually were tossed into Hell, but they found a way to escape and became &quot;kindred of the east.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then Wraith presents the afterlife as a place of infinite depression, where the only escape is to either succumb to Oblivion, or to resolve whatever Fetters tether you to this existence.<br /> <br /> Then Mage claims that people keep reincarnating into multiple lives over and over, thus allowing them to continue the path of Ascension if they failed to get it right the previous time.<br /> <br /> And Werewolf presents the idea that powerful individuals may become ancestral spirits upon their deaths and continue to guide their descendants.<br /> <br /> Then Mummy claims that Duat exists, and the judges there can just make you immortal if they decide to accept you as a servant.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness afterlife is a cluster fuck of contradictions, and I do not enjoy it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah there's more than one place a soul can go when they die in the world of darkness.<br /> <br /> Made a list for this once, something like<br /> <br /> You might go to Oblivion and cease to exist.<br /> Become a wraith (including spectre or drone)<br /> Be reincarnated<br /> Go to a pocket realm in the deep umbra matching an after life (not verified if this is your soul or just a spirit that looks like it)<br /> Disappear (maybe you go to one of the above or reach some true afterlife).<br /> <br /> What soul goes where is a bit who they are, a bit random chance, a bit fate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T07:10:19-07:00","id":1560976,"title":"","content":"The World of Darkness is not known for its consistency, and the afterlife is no exception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T13:04:32-07:00","id":1560987,"title":"","content":"That\u2019s what happens when you smush several separate Worlds of Darkness together and pretend they were meant to fit together all along.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T13:51:22-07:00","id":1560993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560974#post1560974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to Demon, Hell was a place reserved exclusively for the rebellious angels, and humans were never actually tossed in there. Also, the arch angels cursed humanity to forget the knowledge of how to return from the Shadowlands.<br /> <br /> Then the Kuei Jin claims that humans actually were tossed into Hell, but they found a way to escape and became &quot;kindred of the east.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then Wraith presents the afterlife as a place of infinite depression, where the only escape is to either succumb to Oblivion, or to resolve whatever Fetters tether you to this existence.<br /> <br /> Then Mage claims that people keep reincarnating into multiple lives over and over, thus allowing them to continue the path of Ascension if they failed to get it right the previous time.<br /> <br /> And Werewolf presents the idea that powerful individuals may become ancestral spirits upon their deaths and continue to guide their descendants.<br /> <br /> Then Mummy claims that Duat exists, and the judges there can just make you immortal if they decide to accept you as a servant.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness afterlife is a cluster fuck of contradictions, and I do not enjoy it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I take it you haven't heard of the Fractured Cosmos model, then? Go read it and things will suddenly make a lot more sense: <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Fractured_Cosmos\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Fractured_Cosmos</a><br /> <br /> Basically, they're not the same World of Darkness. They're just overlapping alternate realities.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T13:55:01-07:00","id":1560994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560971#post1560971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like, if it's not confirmed one way or the other, then why even bring up the subject in the first place? It sounds like they want me to write my own story, while also trying to present their own narrative at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>The games need to speak to a wide audience. The &quot;stuff happening in the background,&quot; is a fun element of the game for people that don't have the inclination to do it themselves, but still want the game to feel &quot;alive.&quot; Again, it's a tool the devs are giving you, even if it's a tool you don't personally use over a different one in the package.<br /> <br /> And yes, they are both desiring you to write your own story (though ideally the goal is for a story to come out of you playing the game with other people, not just write fiction set in the WoD even if that's also something to do it's just not the focus of the tools provided), and trying to present a premade narrative at the same time. Some people want more freedom, and some people want more tools. Having room to create your own narrative and the tools to use a premade one can coexist just fine as long as you remember that they're not meant to be so tightly linked that you have to use both together or neither.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The two settings can not coexist within the same space, due to a conflict of creative differences. </div> </div> </div>And since VtM 1e, the WoD has consistently stressed you and your group's setting overrides the canon material because you can tailor the setting to your groups specific tastes, while the game needs to work for a lot of people that have different creative preferences from you and your group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560974#post1560974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The World of Darkness afterlife is a cluster fuck of contradictions, and I do not enjoy it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Um, oddly I'm going to disagree with Amethyst on this and point out that the WoD is not at all a clusterfuck. It's not perfectly coherent by any means, but it's much more coherent than you've presented. It doesn't help that you've presented the game-lines in an order that seems to be based purely on personal inclination. How about we start with the release order?<br /> <br /> VtM: Ghosts are real, there's an underworld, human mediums exist, most vampires no jack-shit about the underworld and ghosts, but there's those creepy necromancer vampires. Later after Wraith is out we get that vampires that suffer Final Death don't become ghosts, but vampires can become underworld entities through other means (and those vampires get up to some weird shit)<br /> <br /> WtA: Ghosts are real, there's an underworld - or the &quot;Dark Umbra&quot; - and the Garou have some general knowledge of it but avoid it for the most part. Normal humans go to the underworld, while non-human living things (including the Garou and other shifters) end up in other spiritual realms when they die (though just like ghosts, most are just minor spiritual wisps, not full thinking acting spirits). The concept of spiritual reflections that aren't inherently the same entity as a dead person are also introduced. Garou can travel to the Battleground Realm and literally meet spirits of dead humans, or even themselves, by joining in battles... but those spirits aren't the real originals even if they might know things the real originals would have. Has an Abyss Realm and Malfeas, but neither aligns with human ideas of afterlives.<br /> <br /> MtA: Ghost are real, there's an underworld, many mages study it but few risk going there regularly. The underworld is for normal humans (if this is getting repetitive... yeah, that's kinda the point, this isn't actually drowning in contradictions), and fully Awakening mages don't seem to go specific places when they die. Awakened mages imprint on their Avatars, and those Avatars can carry those personalities to their next mage, resulting in high rates of a form of reincarnation (and a reasonable explanation of why mages don't seem to persist as dead spirits). Though, like vampires, mages can become spirits of realms if they spend too much time there and the underworld counts. Mages are aware of even more Realms that contain spirits that seem to be dead people, but generally feel it's a spiritual reflection phenomenon over some humans dying and ending up in the High Umbra.<br /> <br /> WtO: The game about ghosts goes into lots of details about ghosts, the underworld, and so on in the WoD. Unsurpringling the residents of the underworld know a lot more about it than the rest of the supernaturals up until this point. Largely though, Wraith provides details and nuance instead of overriding things in the earlier games. A vastly important cosmological feature of the underworld gets defined here that is vital context for further entries. The WoD underworld is altered by human belief. Stygia is the European and Western cultural underworld, and it's rules - both its societies rules and metaphysical rules - are not universal. The other Kingdoms of the dead work differently. Charon, the First Emperor, Osiris and his Judges, and so on are not cultural takes on some underlying entity. They are all distinct products of the humans that died there and who's memories of life shaped the world of the dead.<br /> <br /> CtD: Pretty much C&amp;P from Mage, but the changelings have fae souls that jump from human to human instead of Avatars, and the changelings are generally even more adverse to going to the underworld since they're not as skilled as navigating other realms as mages and the Garou are.\u200b<br /> <br /> KotE: Combines the umbra cosmology of the previous games with the established cultural flexibility of the underworld to introduce a large number of hell realms (aka the Yomi Realms). It is explicitly the case that these hells are not natural aspects of the WoD, but artificial realms created by the Yama Kings after they gave up of their original purpose and opted to turn the souls of dead humans into chi batteries. While getting trapped in one of their hells is an afterlife of sorts, they have the capture the dead before they get to the Kingdom of Jade (or in theory try to grab people from there too) rather than it being the normal flow of life and death in the metaphysics of the setting.<br /> <br /> HtR: Shockingly, ghosts are real. The Imbued know extremely little about the underworld and are more concerned about getting ghosts to go back there.<br /> <br /> MtR: While I admit I'm skipping the earlier mummy books, they're not really separate games like the third iteration is. Duat is just the Egyptian Kingdom of the Dead, like Stygia and the Jade Kingdom, and so on. Though there's some explaining of how it's persisted so long as culturally ancient despite it being so long (mostly Osiris using a lot of power to hold it that way, and the Web of Faith adding a bit of oomph). Like all the Dark Kingdoms, Duat has it's own special rules but it's still a place normal humans go when they die.<br /> <br /> DtF: Ghost and the underworld continue to exist as a culturally depended set of islands in the Tempest. Adds another Abyss Realm (weeee reuse of names doesn't help even if they're not the same things according to the text) that's joined to the underworld and is negatively impacted by Maelstroms in the Tempest in it's function as a prison for the demons. While the Abyss/Hell/the Pit is called those things, it's only for demons and is distinct from established horrific realms. Demons think they're the creators of everything in the WoD and have their own story about how the underworld came to be, but it doesn't really change anything about how ghosts and the underworld work. <br /> <br /> Orpheus: Basically an extension of Wraith.. so much so that WtO20 managed to include it as an appendix. We get some more information on the Malfeans (who are not entities from the WtA Malfeas...), but metaphysically and cosmologically, no really changes happen to how dying in the WoD works for normal folks.<br /> <br /> So... while complicated, this is something the WoD managed to keep pretty coherent between the game lines.<br /> <hr /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560972#post1560972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I said that Caine is the First Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also said he's the First Murderer, which is a separate claim towards Noddist myth. The VtM creators might not have come up with the idea on their own, but Caine from the Eden story is not intrinsically linked to him becoming a vampire. The thing that connects the first vampire and the first murderer in VtM is Noddism. By including both you're affirming both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rest is your projection. </div> </div> </div>Projection is a specific thing, what am I projecting and how?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't even know what 100% true means. </div> </div> </div>Fortunately I didn't use that specific phrase?<br /> <br /> Though it's really not that hard: &quot;The sky is blue,&quot; can be treated as true statement even though it is not the 100% full truth as to the color of the Earth's sky because it varies in color based on the angle of the sun and the observer, as well as being colorless when there's insufficient external light coming in (aka night). In common use, most people understand the concept of generalized truths that don't capture all nuance and details, partial truths, metaphoric truths, and so on. Not every phrase that uses &quot;true&quot; is speaking in a strictly binary true/false context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> All I said was that as how the world was conceptualised by Hagen and different line developers over the years Caine was always considered the First Vampire. </div> </div> </div>And yet there's a plethora of evidence against this statement. There are multiple alternative vampire creation myths in the game. It's some fans, not the creators and developers, that consider Caine to be factually the first vampire in the WoD. You cited one line from one book that isn't a definitive as you're claiming, and have now cited a different quote from MR*H that doesn't support your claim either. That whole story about reading a comic with Caine as a vampire didn't end with, &quot;and thus we made the setting about how Caine, the first murderer in Eden, was also the first vampire.&quot; It ends with talking about the themes and conflicts of the WoD. Themes and conflicts that are much better supported by the Noddist story not being canonically true. I'm guessing you don't see the oddity in citing the themes about what makes people belief so strongly in something, while trying to defend a stance where we are supposed to ignore a text that says &quot;probably&quot; and interpret it as a statement of &quot;definitely.&quot; You believe the books are so clearly in that direction you're refusing the text you pointed to's own wording.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gehenna does not say that Caine is possibly a First Vampire. You read the quote, right? </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the quote that literally has the world &quot;probably&quot; in it. If it's possible that vampires can exist without Caine, than it's not definite that Caine is the first vampire.<br /> <br /> You also might want to read me a bit more closely. I didn't say &quot;you quoted X, but that just proves you wrong!&quot; I said your quote is bad evidence for your claim. There is, in fact, better evidence for your claim in the books... but I also consider there even more evidence contrary to your claim on top of that if you want to keep doing this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oh no, I thought we were supposed to refrain from discussing religion because it does not end up well? </div> </div> </div>Discussing the origin of the common usage of the word &quot;canon&quot; in modern English is not discussing religion just because the usage started with theology. Etymology is interesting and all, but going back to the original Greek kanon has no bearing on how we use the word now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And comparing Bible to VtM is silly in reference to canon anyway. </div> </div> </div>And yet, I made a perfectly coherent and easily fact checked claim on what &quot;canon&quot; means in this context and how it derives from theological discussions of what books do and don't count for a bible (and not the Bible, whichever specific one you might mean, there's a bunch of them). I'm not comparing bibles as documents to TTRPGs as documents, I'm comparing how the word canon is used to describe compilations of documents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Despite to what some crazy VtM fans might think, vampires are not real, and VtM was created as an entertainment. </div> </div> </div>Not that it's a particularly helpful comment to make.... but my atheist friends are going to get a real kick out of that line considering how they feel about what's &quot;real&quot; in any bible.<br /> <br /> Did you bother reading me saying, &quot;Canon literally comes from the result of a process by which some texts are considered official and some aren't; not the specifics of the contents within them.&quot; Vampires not being real has nothing to do what we mean when we call something canon or not. Canon isn't about fiction vs. reality. It's about authority to organize things into an official group.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mark Rein-Hagen and most of it's writers are still alive and we can talk with them about their ideas. </div> </div> </div>Have you tried since they stopped going to Dragoncon regularly? The OG founders of WW are not big on chatting online with the fans. They might do a podcast or interview, but that's not really the same thing. I've talked to plenty of late 2e, Revised, and later WoD devs over the years, but they are unsurprisingly more online interaction positive. Even then, most of them have moved on and justifiably want to talk about what they care about now instead of what they worked on years ago.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So there you go, not wrong just in minority. Metaplot is/was an important part of the setting for many players and as I said, a big part of the reason Vampire became so popular in the 90s. </div> </div> </div>How, exactly, does &quot;many fans love this part of the WoD,&quot; demonstrate those of use that don't like that part of the game a minority exactly? I was there in the 90s. Metaplot was not what made VtM popular. Metaplot was a side bonus for people that love deep setttings to dig into. VtM was popular because it managed the best balance of accessibility and pop-culture relevance of many of the 90s TTRPGs appealing for market share by not competing in the standard fantasy or sci-fi genres. Dark broody night creatures in leather were in. VtM delivered that in a package that wasn't to mechanically experimental for people to get, or too metaphysically dense to try to capture concepts more thoroughly. Other games like Kult, Unknown Armies, In Nomine, Witchcraft, and more just didn't hit the right balance despite it being similar in style and subject matter.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Computers and consoles started to be more popular and TTRPGs started to falter so the higher-ups at White Wolf decided to make a shake up that is going to bring them more money. It worked only for the initial Requiem corebook. </div> </div> </div>Besides the somewhat silly idea of there being a major distinction of &quot;higher-ups&quot; in a company the size of WW at the time, the decision they made is something that was openly acknowledged as the more financially risky one. Lots of early 00s WW folks pointed out they could have easily done a 4th edition and coasted on selling another round of core books and supplements treading on the same exact ground as 1/e2e and Rev had already done twice if not three times before. If they just cared about bringing in more money, that would have been the smart move. The hard reset in the form of the CofD was a risk that knew it would piss off a significant number of fans - and their cash would not be coming in - in the hopes of long term gains if people came around to the benefits of starting over.<br /> <br /> And the history is largely: having to choose wasn't as true as they though since CofD and WoD20 coexisted for quite some time and it was probably the best period for WoD fans in the last 20 years, combined with the TTRPG industry imploded in the mid 00s and nothing was going to keep WW independent regardless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T14:13:55-07:00","id":1560999,"title":"","content":"Just ignore Demon and Orpheus and WoD is largely, but haphazardly, consistent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T14:26:06-07:00","id":1561001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560967#post1560967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As of the time of me writing this, my belief is that the metaplot attempts to join all the different splats together under one unified cosmology. </div> </div> </div> </div>No, that's not what the metaplot does.<br /> <br /> It's purpose is a set of optional events you can add into your chronicle if you think it'd be fun.<br /> <br /> It let's you run a chronicle were the PCs affect major changes to the world by changing a part (or many parts) of the metaplot.<br /> <br /> Or you can just run a normal chronicle, but have an adventure relate to some metaplot event for fun.<br /> <br /> It's not there to join different splats into a unified cosmology.<br /> <br /> It's a lot easier to run crossovers between splats than the internet may let on so it's not really needed for that. Metaplot is a good excuse for a team up though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28924-tjalei","name":"Tjalei","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T14:43:51-07:00","id":1561004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560993#post1560993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically, they're not the same World of Darkness. They're just overlapping alternate realities.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is what I'm beginning to suspect the metaplot might actually be. The phrase <i>&quot;THE Metaplot&quot;</i> got me confused into thinking there was only a single joint narrative, instead of multiple versions.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-25T15:27:27-07:00","id":1561005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560955#post1560955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I still don't like it. Given my neurological condition, I don't like when things are left up to interpretation, or surrounded by nuance. My brain always comes away with a radically different conclusion than what the original creator was going for, and then it makes me feel lesser for not understanding it.<br /> <br /> I need things to be spelled out, clear cut, no room for misinterpretation. When the story fails to provide that, it leaves me confused and frustrated.<br /> <br /> I do love the World of Darkness franchise, don't get me wrong. But the metaplot was a mistake, and getting rid of it was the right call.</div> </div> </div> </div>I understand this frustration, and it is valid.<br /> <br /> That said, let's unpack some things:<br /> <br /> 1. Let's judge a work on its proposal. There are things we don't like because they're bad at what they try, and there are things we don't like because we personally don't enjoy what they try, but they're meant for people who do.<br /> <br /> This distinction matters.<br /> <br /> 2. You're mistaking ambiguity as obfuscation with ambiguity as goal. The unreliable narrator in VtM isn't there to make finding the truth hard and frustrating for people like us, they're there to say the ST decides how much they're correct.<br /> <br /> The author isn't waiting that you understand the answer, they're giving you an open question to answer as you see fit, exactly like CofD does, if not the same style of delivery.<br /> <br /> 3. The game did spelled it out, several times. Not as clearly, not nearly clear enough, but did. There are several reasons why it is easy to miss, but when you know what to pay attention to, it's all over the place.<br /> <br /> 4. The Metaplot was... A thing. An artifact of its time and place, and a mixed bag. A lot of things could have been done better. Some are a result of their literary purpose. Some are the reason why the game went so far.<br /> <br /> You're right in the end for their execution, and other gamelines show that many authors agree and learned from it. V5 is also there to show that some of the things you find awful are the actual selling point for others.<br /> <br /> 5. At the end of the day we're discussing old books and lore. Whatever we think of them won't change the past. That's relevant for analysis: you can get rid of ambiguity at your table or headcanon, but not at lore discussion.<br /> <br /> Instead, give it time. Learn the ins and outs of its nuance. As something past and done, VtM from the 90s is now a fixed thing, so as big and hard as the problem is, you can take it with time.<br /> <br /> This will help exercise the understanding of nuance and stuff within your condition, which is satisfying in the long run and useful. It will not make you normal, but you'll understand why people do certain things better than them by acquiring as knowledge and analytical training the abilities they take for granted.<br /> <br /> VtM is what it is, what we can do is appreciate it's reality even if not what we would have preferred.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560958#post1560958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For hatever reasom Quote function does not work for me so here we go:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar5826_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"5826\" data-vbnamecard=\"5826\">monteparnas</a> No, I didn't.<br /> <br /> And there is also fourth part, about Caine which the quote comes from. And it states pretty clearly that Caine is/was a First Vampire even if it presents other options. Again, the possibility of different options does not mean that there is not one that is considered &quot;canon&quot; FWIW.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the Quote, it sometimes do that. It also has a lot of little bugs overall.<br /> <br /> Part four presents a standard, not a canon. A canon (in this context) is what the author say to be undeniably true. Anything short of that is not canon.<br /> <br /> You can also define it as the information that future materials will assume as true in a way that matters. Not possible, true. Not &quot;the story works if this is reality&quot;, but &quot;the story don't work without adjustments if it isn't&quot;.<br /> <br /> And I'm adamant about this because as an author myself I know the difference in intention and how frustrating it is when people try to force you to resolve ambiguity, or attribute ambiguity resolution to you.<br /> <br /> When openness is the point, no matter how much the author has preferences among the options, it is the damn fucking point.<br /> <br /> If you did or not:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560885#post1560885\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the truth about vampire mythos in-world I agree that treating it as a legend that might or might not be based in historical facts is the best approach. That's when on the subreddits people ask about Caine, Second Generation or Antes I say that most of this stuff is debatable. Because what sources we have for Caine existence? Book of Nod, Erciyes Fragments, Book of Grave War or Revelations of the Dark Mother? Those are all books of religious mythology that are surely coloured by religious and political bias of their authors.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rest my case.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560960#post1560960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I understand that, but I try to remain true to established lore and canon as much as possible.<br /> <br /> It's my way of showing my passion for the franchise, and respect for the creator's vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>The point of an open-ended interpretation is to get people to think, this is the creator's vision. I say this as an author that uses this kind of device regularly today.<br /> <br /> I want to see what readers or players will come up with, be surprised by their creativity. I want people to reflect on the doubt and the significance of taking sides without knowing. I want to explore belief and curiosity, how people are affected by the story instead of the truth of its contents.<br /> <br /> Frequently I want to be free to explore options myself, to try different scenarios. And to not few constrained to decide on a path when I'm not certain of which I want.<br /> <br /> VtM makes thematic use of the ambiguity. The setting doesn't work if things are clear and cut, because it's about factions fighting for things they can't prove to be real, but do have plausible evidence. It matters that they all might be right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560963#post1560963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With that said, is it perhaps worth bringing it back to the topic of the Sabbat so we don't get too off-track? For instance, I think that subjective dimension is also why the Sabbat is relatively popular both IC and OOC. It also has that element of &quot;people see what they want to see&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely the case.<br /> <br /> Even with unreliable narrators, as the game's default the Camarilla gets constant depictions and that means we see more or less how the pieces work. It has Traditions, institutions, Conclave and whatnot, but we see the nightly life and how those pieces can fit and interact in practice.<br /> <br /> But the Sabbat is The Other\u2122 more than any other faction. Camarilla vampires receive the independent clans in their Domains and see them, deal with them.<br /> <br /> Sabbat information is always fractured. Even their books don't change one thing: you don't see much of their regular nights. We get good descriptions of several important pieces, but very little on how they fit together, how they vary, how they clash \u2013 and this is extremely important.<br /> <br /> Add to this how much their books change from each other due to a combination of factors. Revisions from player backlash, clash between artistic conceptions, need/benefit of fitting DA developments to clans and Paths. With fewer and more controversial books, the Sabbat gets heavier revisions that result in more diverse information with less fleshed out connecting tissue.<br /> <br /> What comes from the other side is something far less clear between striking main pieces, and each player gets to fill those gaps as they see fit, sometimes not noticing how much the gaps matter to the end result.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560967#post1560967\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But from the way people are talking about it on these forums, it sounds like each of the different splats has their own version of a metaplot, which applies specifically to their gameline?</div> </div> </div> </div>Long story short, yes.<br /> <br /> The lines are independent and ultimately irreconcilable, and their individual metaplots are meant to resolve their individual questions.<br /> <br /> How much they align is a matter for infinite debate, as both individual authors and company policy had inconsistent approaches to it, but in the end all similarities are more Easter Eggs (even if huge ones) than anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560971#post1560971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like, if it's not confirmed one way or the other, then why even bring up the subject in the first place? It sounds like they want me to write my own story, while also trying to present their own narrative at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Two reasons:<br /> <br /> 1. Show how rumors work in the setting. If the ST decides those things aren't true, the rumors still exist, there's still people that believe them.<br /> <br /> 2. Give starting ideas. For many STs this helps a lot, even to change or reverse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560972#post1560972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> He is fine with having whatever preference about the way VtM/WoD are written but he is in minority. So there you go, not wrong just in minority. Metaplot is/was an important part of the setting for many players and as I said, a big part of the reason Vampire became so popular in the 90s.<br /> <br /> Agreed about the Time of Judgment, the reasons were many. Computers and consoles started to be more popular and TTRPGs started to falter so the higher-ups at White Wolf decided to make a shake up that is going to bring them more money. It worked only for the initial Requiem corebook. And the rest is history.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Actually I think the initial Requiem Corebook was by and large the worst they got.<br /> <br /> If you don't like CofD, that's a you thing. Not same setting, not exactly same fan base, but it thrived quite well.<br /> <br /> The Metaplot was definitely not a consensus back them, lots of players hated it.<br /> <br /> And TTRPGs didn't start to falter as they hadn't raised yet. They'd be marginally relevant as a market only in the 2000s.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560974#post1560974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to Demon, Hell...</div> </div> </div> </div>Those words don't have hard definitions, so they're used irregularly. It goes like that:<br /> <br /> 1. Dead humans go to the Underworld by default.<br /> <br /> 2. Things not human have their own destination, Mages too for other reasons.<br /> <br /> 3. You can mess up with where dead people go. The Yama Kings do that, Osiris started to do that, some Mages do that, Demons may have done that in the past.<br /> <br /> 4. Demons have a prison realm custom-built for them and for them only.<br /> <br /> 5. Since the Umbra is an infinite copy machine, it has spirits that are copies of any person or entity, and realms that are copies of concepts of afterlives, but this is mostly the Umbra being itself and you can safely ignore. It's not completely guaranteed the real thing isn't actually one of those copies, but mostly.<br /> <br /> From this, the problem is words. Each splat or explorer meets different things and use the name they want for it. Just don't assume they're talking about the same place just because they used the same name.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> - Werewolves know a Realm in the Middle Umbra that's a big chasm that spills depression. They call it the Abyss.<br /> <br /> - the Discipline of Obtenebration uses solid shadows the Lasombra claim to come from another realm that's partially confirmed by Abyss Mystics. As their name suggest, they call the place the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Wraith and Demon also have their own places they each call the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The thing is: they're not talking about the same thing. Each just has experience with a place they thought make sense to call Abyss. Those places may be linked, even aspects of the same realm, but that's not the reason they get the same name.<br /> <br /> It's just 4 different otherworldly experiences, by different groups that don't know what the others use the word Abyss for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T01:37:31-07:00","id":1561024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1560994#post1560994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> LONG TEXT</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, it's silly to discuss with you the matter because you are so bad faith that you quibble about the fact that Wiecks and Hagen were higher-ups. Fuck, Stewart Wieck was a freaking CEO.<br /> <br /> I will gladly ignore your further posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","user":"sathriel","date":". 06-26-2026, 04:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude0e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T01:48:58-07:00","id":1561025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561005#post1561005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually I think the initial Requiem Corebook was by and large the worst they got.<br /> <br /> If you don't like CofD, that's a you thing. Not same setting, not exactly same fan base, but it thrived quite well.<br /> <br /> The Metaplot was definitely not a consensus back them, lots of players hated it.<br /> <br /> And TTRPGs didn't start to falter as they hadn't raised yet. They'd be marginally relevant as a market only in the 2000s.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't talking about quality but financial success. Because that is quantifiable, quality is in the eye of the beholder. <br /> <br /> I don't care about CofD because it was never something that did interest me. I have nothing against it and I wish it was still published for people that love the systems. Though I understand the decision from financial perspective it does not mean I have to like it. <br /> <br /> Sure, there is little consensus on anything as we can well see from this thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T06:41:36-07:00","id":1561028,"title":"","content":"<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561005#post1561005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I understand this frustration, and it is valid.<br /> <br /> That said, let's unpack some things:<br /> <br /> 1. Let's judge a work on its proposal. There are things we don't like because they're bad at what they try, and there are things we don't like because we personally don't enjoy what they try, but they're meant for people who do.<br /> <br /> This distinction matters.<br /> <br /> 2. You're mistaking ambiguity as obfuscation with ambiguity as goal. The unreliable narrator in VtM isn't there to make finding the truth hard and frustrating for people like us, they're there to say the ST decides how much they're correct.<br /> <br /> The author isn't waiting that you understand the answer, they're giving you an open question to answer as you see fit, exactly like CofD does, if not the same style of delivery.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I know it's my personal hang up. I just wanted to voice my frustration on the matter.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, though, I did originally enjoy the ongoing metaplot, until I started digging deeper and found out how muddled it gets.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561005#post1561005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From this, the problem is words. Each splat or explorer meets different things and use the name they want for it. Just don't assume they're talking about the same place just because they used the same name.<br /> <br /> Example:<br /> <br /> - Werewolves know a Realm in the Middle Umbra that's a big chasm that spills depression. They call it the Abyss.<br /> <br /> - the Discipline of Obtenebration uses solid shadows the Lasombra claim to come from another realm that's partially confirmed by Abyss Mystics. As their name suggest, they call the place the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Wraith and Demon also have their own places they each call the Abyss.<br /> <br /> The thing is: they're not talking about the same thing. Each just has experience with a place they thought make sense to call Abyss. Those places may be linked, even aspects of the same realm, but that's not the reason they get the same name.<br /> <br /> It's just 4 different otherworldly experiences, by different groups that don't know what the others use the word Abyss for.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, great, that makes things much less confusing! (sarcasm) <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T06:53:14-07:00","id":1561029,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2357\" data-vbnamecard=\"2357\">sathriel</a> Did they officially confirm that Chronicles was being abandoned after releasing Deviant?<br /> <br /> I don't think I've heard any other news come out of the franchise since then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T07:08:23-07:00","id":1561030,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29009_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29009\" data-vbnamecard=\"29009\">DarkKing</a> People seem to agree that Chronicles failed to meet expectations. Plus the *cough* 'issues' that arose regarding the lead developer for Beast, I don't think they're very keen on investing further resources into the reboot.<br /> <br /> Deviant was probably the last book on the assembly line, before they decided to finally close up shop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29027-greathornedratkin","name":"GreatHornedRatkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29027_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2026"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"413"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T11:43:04-07:00","id":1561034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561029#post1561029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2357\" data-vbnamecard=\"2357\">sathriel</a> Did they officially confirm that Chronicles was being abandoned after releasing Deviant?<br /> <br /> I don't think I've heard any other news come out of the franchise since then.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox have never come out and said they've abandoned Chronicles, but... they stopped approving Onyx Path's proposals a good while back, and haven't licensed it to any other publisher, so to all intents and purposes they've let it go dormant.<br /> <br /> I'd disagree with GHR's assessment of why - it wasn't anything to do with Chronicles itself, it was that they didn't want to be putting out something competing with the original WOD (as they saw it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T14:20:38-07:00","id":1561039,"title":"","content":"That's exactly correct. Having both WoD and CofD has already made a remarkable, permanent, split between the tabletop side of the omni-fanbase. There is no reason why Paradox would want CofD to continue. <br /> <br /> This is also the reason why V5 (and thereafter, concerning the other &quot;5th&quot; gamelines for the other splats) is so (blatantly) similar to CofD, opposed to cWoD; the lead developer at the time (who I will not name) wanted to continue CofD, but Paradox told him no. So, he went ahead and jarringly emplaced VtR mechanics into VtM without no care or reasoning. <br /> <br /> I wonder how they're going to develop V6 now. I also wonder if the rest of the gamelines that didn't get a 5th will skip to the 6th.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T15:39:50-07:00","id":1561041,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561039#post1561039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's exactly correct. Having both WoD and CofD has already made a remarkable, permanent, split between the tabletop side of the omni-fanbase. There is no reason why Paradox would want CofD to continue.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh? The worst divide for the &quot;omin-fanbase&quot; was in the late 00s and early 10s when it was just the CofD. When V20 revived the WoD fan division reduced drastically and there was increased sales on both sides. The WoD20/CofD 2e era showed &quot;both&quot; was objectively better for fan sentiment and profit. Having both at the same time was clearly better than when WW cut one for the other.<br /> <br /> Also... there's a whole &quot;money&quot; thing. Paradox could have easily let Onyx Path continue to make CofD books like they do with Exalted. Paradox gets money for doing absolutely nothing. And if Paradox is worried about Onyx Path having a wider audience reach that it would hurt WoD5 (and now 5.5 and 6) sales, that's an indictment of Paradox's capabilities as a company given the disparities in operating budgets alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T16:12:19-07:00","id":1561044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561039#post1561039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder how they're going to develop V6 now. I also wonder if the rest of the gamelines that didn't get a 5th will skip to the 6th.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's hope that 6th edition moves away from the whole 'street level' power scaling, or else Mage and Changeling are screwed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-26T23:57:16-07:00","id":1561049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561039#post1561039\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, he went ahead and jarringly emplaced VtR mechanics into VtM without no care or reasoning.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, good, I wasn't the only one who noticed that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T10:31:24-07:00","id":1561054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561044#post1561044\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let's hope that 6th edition moves away from the whole 'street level' power scaling, or else Mage and Changeling are screwed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Assumption being that there will be Changeling or even Mage. Which is not impossible but I'd think rather unlikely at the moment. And that is even considering Outstar saying that there are people pushing for Changeling at WW. At the end of the day it doesn't matter because it's Paradox who is calling the shots and the whole WoD5 has been a big disappointment financially. I would not be surprised if they let go of everything but Vampire going forward because it seems to be the main thing that sells. That makes Mage iffy and Changeling very unlikely as the least popular oWoD system next to Wraith.<br /> <br /> And that is even before we consider how &quot;ethnic&quot; the Traditions are between kung-fu monks and hindu necromancers and African shamans. Even if WW wanted to touch that I am afraid another W5 fiasco where new fans will not come in satisfying numbers (for Paradox) and the old fans will stick to superior, to their wit, Revised and M20 editions.<br /> <br /> Also, they have been moving away from their initial street level play with the introduction of rules for creating older vampires the Methuselahs in Gehenna War and so on. Hell, even Baali returned although Paradox said &quot;no demons in our WoD&quot;.<br /> <br /> But only time will tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2357,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","user":"sathriel","date":". 06-27-2026, 01:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T10:47:45-07:00","id":1561056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561054#post1561054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Assumption being that there will be Changeling or even Mage. Which is not impossible but I'd think rather unlikely at the moment. And that is even considering Outstar saying that there are people pushing for Changeling at WW. At the end of the day it doesn't matter because it's Paradox who is calling the shots and the whole WoD5 has been a big disappointment financially. I would not be surprised if they let go of everything but Vampire going forward because it seems to be the main thing that sells. That makes Mage iffy and Changeling very unlikely as the least popular oWoD system next to Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>Gee, what a surprise that an IP featured around goth-punk from the 90's wouldn't resonate with today's audience.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561054#post1561054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And that is even before we consider how &quot;ethnic&quot; the Traditions are between kung-fu monks and hindu necromancers and African shamans. Even if WW wanted to touch that I am afraid another W5 fiasco where new fans will not come in satisfying numbers (for Paradox) and the old fans will stick to superior, to their wit, Revised and M20 editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the ethnic stuff is what prevents me from getting more engrossed into Mage, Werewolf, and the like.<br /> <br /> I want to, because these games look awesome, but I also don't want to have to sit through an entire culture seminar for each of the playable tribes / traditions.<br /> <br /> Chronicles fixed this problem for me, by making the Tribes / Watchtowers / Clans / and Courts into archetypes, as opposed to regional variants. Much easier to dive into by comparison.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561054#post1561054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Also, they have been moving away from their initial street level play with the introduction of rules for creating older vampires the Methuselahs in Gehenna War and so on. Hell, even Baali returned although Paradox said &quot;no demons in our WoD&quot;.<br /> <br /> But only time will tell.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have absolutely zero interest in playing any game that takes place in the middle east.<br /> <br /> Especially with how V5 is trying to claim that my Sabbat has decided to team up with mortal terrorist organizations.<br /> <br /> I mean, come on. That couldn't be any more on the nose, if it was written by Pinnochio!\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-27T12:16:20-07:00","id":1561061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561025#post1561025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't talking about quality but financial success. Because that is quantifiable, quality is in the eye of the beholder.<br /> <br /> I don't care about CofD because it was never something that did interest me. I have nothing against it and I wish it was still published for people that love the systems. Though I understand the decision from financial perspective it does not mean I have to like it.<br /> <br /> Sure, there is little consensus on anything as we can well see from this thread <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, me too. Because while quantifiable, it isn't a simple analysis.<br /> <br /> VtR1st was the big sale for obvious reasons. It was also a big let down. That matters more than its total sales, because it set up the market reaction to everything that came after.<br /> <br /> Following books suffered from the challenge of walking out of the financial pit. Requiem's error was to be too little itself while not nearly enough Masquerade. That left a bad taste and led to evasion.<br /> <br /> But those books did as well as you could expect. All things considered and the market at the time, they did a very good recovery. The whole nWoD managed to be stable through rough times for the TTRPG market. It's not by any metric a small thing or bad sales.<br /> <br /> Under Onyx Path we got the Second Edition and then it wasn't just stable, it thrived.<br /> <br /> As for the reason it doesn't got new books, is strictly because Paradox stopped greenlighting projects they have no cost with, as they think it would compete with WoD5. It's the opposite of doing bad.<br /> <br /> CofD showed continued resilience and stable profits. That's way more valuable in the long run than a one - off of dubious reception.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T12:06:23-07:00","id":1561082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561061#post1561061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Indeed, me too. Because while quantifiable, it isn't a simple analysis.<br /> <br /> VtR1st was the big sale for obvious reasons. It was also a big let down. That matters more than its total sales, because it set up the market reaction to everything that came after.<br /> <br /> Following books suffered from the challenge of walking out of the financial pit. Requiem's error was to be too little itself while not nearly enough Masquerade. That left a bad taste and led to evasion.<br /> <br /> But those books did as well as you could expect. All things considered and the market at the time, they did a very good recovery. The whole nWoD managed to be stable through rough times for the TTRPG market. It's not by any metric a small thing or bad sales.<br /> <br /> Under Onyx Path we got the Second Edition and then it wasn't just stable, it thrived.<br /> <br /> As for the reason it doesn't got new books, is strictly because Paradox stopped greenlighting projects they have no cost with, as they think it would compete with WoD5. It's the opposite of doing bad.<br /> <br /> CofD showed continued resilience and stable profits. That's way more valuable in the long run than a one - off of dubious reception.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, we are in agreement on most of those things. <br /> <br /> It's funny that Ericsson as, apparently, a fan of CofD, made V5 similar to it in that respect you mention: not enough like the old thing to satisfy old fans and too similar to it for the new fans. <br /> <br /> As I previously stated, I understand the reasoning Paradox followed to end support for CofD (not wanting it to compete with WoD5) but it is no comfort for people who genuinely loved the system. <br /> <br /> All we can do now is to inhale the copium and hope that concentrating on one universe will allow them to make a better product... but it has not worked that well so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-28T13:36:00-07:00","id":1561087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>sathriel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561082#post1561082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's funny that Ericsson as, apparently, a fan of CofD, made V5 similar to it in that respect you mention: not enough like the old thing to satisfy old fans and too similar to it for the new fans.<br /> <br /> As I previously stated, I understand the reasoning Paradox followed to end support for CofD (not wanting it to compete with WoD5) but it is no comfort for people who genuinely loved the system.<br /> <br /> All we can do now is to inhale the copium and hope that concentrating on one universe will allow them to make a better product... but it has not worked that well so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unfortunately I can't say any of this surprise me, because Ericsson was from start too easy to profile. And all those things are wrong, not from your part, but his.<br /> <br /> V5 is not intended to be a depart in any sense, but a return, a pure 1st edition experience.<br /> <br /> If you don't get this vibe from the game, it's a testament to how misguided this idea is from the start.<br /> <br /> As many fans, he's a romantic that want return to a game that never existed but in his head, a curious trick our memory can play with us. This is not new or surprising, but is telling, because this kind of person is always chasing an ideal past that can't exist.<br /> <br /> Hence why you get this impression: it is made to be a slightly improved 1st Edition, which isn't a new game by any standard, but it is made out of a fantasy full of things that weren't there.<br /> <br /> For the reason of stopping CofD, it's equally misguided. Understandable, but utterly incorrect. The best time for both games was when V20 and VtR2nd were both actively releasing and reinforcing each other. Onyx Path had a lot of success doing just that. Paradox had zero to actually gain doing what they did, it was a plain bad decision.<br /> <br /> But it was intuitive for someone with his mindset, because this kind of person despise what doesn't confirm to their vision and see as an obstacle regardless. He hated CofD on principle, as in his heart it is a thorn in the way of a truly masterful game.<br /> <br /> The result was exactly to be expected:<br /> - the company has no know-how in the area,<br /> - this is the pet project of a person with this profile,<br /> - the cost, at the time, was mostly beneath notice for them. Not irrelevant, but low enough that it was worth a shot without engagement.<br /> <br /> We got a game with lots of good things, because it does have a lot of them, but riddled with serious, na\u00efve problems a serious publisher would have caught. They went through instead and we got the result.<br /> <br /> We also had at the time a company (or a public stance for the company) that was more or less openly hostile to other views about the game and the people that held them. A company that wanted anyone who disagreed to go away. Who wasn't just not hearing fans of Revised or 2nd edition or CofD, but actively tried to make those fans feel bad and either convert them or drive them away.<br /> <br /> Other things compounded. Early he did what, again, was expected, and amassed a team of both like minded writers and Yesmen. One of his early acquisitions was Rein-Hagen himself, which is NOT good: Rein-Hagen is a prolific but problem writer, White Wolf did well because they had people that could temper him, but Ericsson instead gave him sycophants.<br /> <br /> What I can say after all those years is that the writing was on the wall the whole time inside Paradox. Time just made clear, and this is not just a WoD thing, that they have a severely bad management.<br /> <br /> V5 abandoned most of its initial stances and is backpedaling, but this is all overall slow. Paradox burned bridges, pissed people, broke things they could use, and blundered around until investors had to intervene. Now they have to play chill, and WoD simply isn't a focus, as they had to admit they just don't know what they're doing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T09:47:05-07:00","id":1561100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561087#post1561087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> V5 abandoned most of its initial stances and is backpedaling, but this is all overall slow. Paradox burned bridges, pissed people, broke things they could use, and blundered around until investors had to intervene. Now they have to play chill, and WoD simply isn't a focus, as they had to admit they just don't know what they're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amen to that, considering that WoD had 2 revisions in the 12 years life span (Second Edition was released less than 2 years after the first) and it took Paradox 7-8 years and the failure that is Bloodlines 2 to realize that something is not working is a bit jawdropping. But as you have said, it's clear that people in charge have no idea what they are doing. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T10:04:01-07:00","id":1561101,"title":"","content":"It also probably doesn't help that after shutting down production of Chronicles, they decide to start production of yet another personal horror game in the form of Curseborne.<br /> <br /> Like, seriously, just go ahead and sell the IP already. There are fans of the game who have proven to be deeply passionate about it, and can write better material than what Paradox has been releasing.<br /> <br /> Just take a look at <b>The Book of Hungry Names</b>, for example. Described as being <i>&quot;3x the length of the Lord of the Rings trilogy.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T11:14:13-07:00","id":1561103,"title":"","content":"The delay to notice problems comes from the problems themselves.<br /> <br /> You had a passionate leader that wouldn't admit his errors because they're also his whole point.<br /> <br /> A company without know-how, and so without the tools to see what's wrong and what's expected, much less diagnose the cause.<br /> <br /> More pressing matters elsewhere as this was a low budget - low return thing.<br /> <br /> From this other Paradox problems compounded, but mainly they have a tendency to finish things for the sake of it without course correction. And now they're under pressure to stop wasting money in things they know shit about and keep to their particular brand of Real Time Strategy games.<br /> <br /> If anything can shake up things back into movement is their colab with D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar29009_1.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"29009\" data-vbnamecard=\"29009\">DarkKing</a> Curseborn is not theirs.<br /> <br /> Since Onyx Path couldn't get any more books approved by Paradox (because it was Onyx Path making all the CofD and WoD20 books under authorization), they made Curseborn as a thing they can work on without depending on Paradox developing Common Sense.<br /> <br /> It is actually a good thing, and our best shot at a decently supported horror game going forward. It's that, accepting what WoD 20 already released as the end of it, or V5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T13:34:45-07:00","id":1561105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561103#post1561103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Curseborn is not theirs.<br /> <br /> Since Onyx Path couldn't get any more books approved by Paradox (because it was Onyx Path making all the CofD and WoD20 books under authorization), they made Curseborn as a thing they can work on without depending on Paradox developing Common Sense.<br /> <br /> It is actually a good thing, and our best shot at a decently supported horror game going forward. It's that, accepting what WoD 20 already released as the end of it, or V5.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, the Curseborne forums seem to be a ghost town. I was the first person to reply to any old topics in several months, and Basic was the first to start any new ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-29T14:58:21-07:00","id":1561114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561105#post1561105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know, the Curseborne forums seem to be a ghost town. I was the first person to reply to any old topics in several months, and Basic was the first to start any new ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't take these forums as a metric for anything, even my generation mostly left to Reddit and Discord.<br /> <br /> Curseborne is doing well. It's still new, a lot to grow yet, but the pipeline is full of released for the time being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T01:50:51-07:00","id":1561118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561087#post1561087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Unfortunately I can't say any of this surprise me, because Ericsson was from start too easy to profile. And all those things are wrong, not from your part, but his.<br /> <br /> V5 is not intended to be a depart in any sense, but a return, a pure 1st edition experience.<br /> <br /> If you don't get this vibe from the game, it's a testament to how misguided this idea is from the start.<br /> <br /> As many fans, he's a romantic that want return to a game that never existed but in his head, a curious trick our memory can play with us. This is not new or surprising, but is telling, because this kind of person is always chasing an ideal past that can't exist.<br /> <br /> Hence why you get this impression: it is made to be a slightly improved 1st Edition, which isn't a new game by any standard, but it is made out of a fantasy full of things that weren't there.<br /> <br /> For the reason of stopping CofD, it's equally misguided. Understandable, but utterly incorrect. The best time for both games was when V20 and VtR2nd were both actively releasing and reinforcing each other. Onyx Path had a lot of success doing just that. Paradox had zero to actually gain doing what they did, it was a plain bad decision.<br /> <br /> But it was intuitive for someone with his mindset, because this kind of person despise what doesn't confirm to their vision and see as an obstacle regardless. He hated CofD on principle, as in his heart it is a thorn in the way of a truly masterful game.</div> </div> </div> </div>AIUI, Ericsson has said he actually wanted to do VTR3e instead of V5. He was told to stick to WoD as the more recognisable brand of the two, but this explains why the system borrows so liberally from CofD.<br /> <br /> But it's also worth remembering that Ericsson wasn't the only person involved in writing V5. Don't forget, Paradox specifically wanted Ken Hite to do <i>Nights Black Agents</i> from the vampire's perspective.<br /> <br /> As you mentioned, they also had MRH, who has always had strong views about his games, but they also had Justin Achilli, who also has traditionally had strong views about the game. They were also told to include certain elements from the version of <i>Bloodlines 2</i> that never was, such as Blood Resonance and You Are What You Eat l.<br /> <br /> As such, V5 has similarities to both V1 and Revised, but also tries to do a bunch of new things all at once. While it aims to capture a version of the game that never really existed, it also often adopts (and exaggerates) Revised's approach to &quot;rectifying&quot; things (literally blowing stuff up for being &quot;tonally inconsistent&quot; without any hint of irony), being vague about things (intentionally excluding concrete dates and prioritising &quot;mystery&quot; over clarity), and ST/player guidance (wagging its finger at badwrongfun, etc).<br /> <br /> After release, the books were also developed by a range of licensees, so tonally and quality-wise, they were all over the place. This is presumably why they're bringing the whole thing back in-house for the entire run of V6. Many people who stuck with V20 rules would've still bought V5 books just for the lore and any new ideas they could crib. But if you don't know whether the next V5 book is going to be another <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> or another <i>Camarilla</i>, you're less likely to take the risk and buy a copy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561087#post1561087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The result was exactly to be expected:<br /> - the company has no know-how in the area,<br /> - this is the pet project of a person with this profile,<br /> - the cost, at the time, was mostly beneath notice for them. Not irrelevant, but low enough that it was worth a shot without engagement.<br /> <br /> We got a game with lots of good things, because it does have a lot of them, but riddled with serious, na\u00efve problems a serious publisher would have caught. They went through instead and we got the result.<br /> <br /> [...]<br /> <br /> What I can say after all those years is that the writing was on the wall the whole time inside Paradox. Time just made clear, and this is not just a WoD thing, that they have a severely bad management.<br /> <br /> V5 abandoned most of its initial stances and is backpedaling, but this is all overall slow. Paradox burned bridges, pissed people, broke things they could use, and blundered around until investors had to intervene. Now they have to play chill, and WoD simply isn't a focus, as they had to admit they just don't know what they're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious to see how they handle distribution going forward. Renegade seems to have slowed down distribution of V5 books (at least here in the UK). The most recent books are getting harder to obtain and there's often big time lags even when they can get stuff to you.<br /> <br /> From my experience in publishing (having worked on ~300 titles in one form or another since 2007), distribution is becoming a riskier business, with storage costs going up, margins becoming tighter, and bookselling becoming much more fragmented as time goes on. On the publisher side, this is aggravated by rising paper costs, greater reliance on overseas shipping, and disruptions to the supply chain caused by tariffs and politics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T06:15:01-07:00","id":1561130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561118#post1561118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> After release, the books were also developed by a range of licensees, so tonally and quality-wise, they were all over the place. This is presumably why they're bringing the whole thing back in-house for the entire run of V6. Many people who stuck with V20 rules would've still bought V5 books just for the lore and any new ideas they could crib. But if you don't know whether the next V5 book is going to be another <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i> or another <i>Camarilla</i>, you're less likely to take the risk and buy a copy.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the lore that they either disregarded from the previous editions, or retconned so heavily as to be almost unrecognizeable?<br /> <br /> Yeah, no, V5 is not my gothic horror vampire game!<br /> <br /> Blood Resonances were a stupid addition, because your discipline affinity is supposed to be linked to your clan, not the kind of people you eat. And predator types were also a bad move, because the Beast is a mindless animal that runs on pure instinct. It does not give a crap where and how you feed, so long as you continue to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T06:23:33-07:00","id":1561131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561118#post1561118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> AIUI, Ericsson has said he actually wanted to do VTR3e instead of V5. He was told to stick to WoD as the more recognisable brand of the two, but this explains why the system borrows so liberally from CofD.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>That doesn't line up with what I heard, but also I didn't got it from the best sources, it wasn't important enough for me at the time.<br /> <br /> Yet the overall gist persist, one or more people in decision positions had this profile that's very close to MRH already.<br /> <br /> And the biggest source of problems in the end was Paradox take on markets they don't know about, which is something that plagued them for 10 years and affected a lot of projects, BL2 being only the latest and biggest money sink.<br /> <br /> On distribution, the reality is that on top of everything else the whole model is dated. We can't keep the idea that centralized mass printing and storage is the way to go.<br /> <br /> We need to pulverize printing, localize it near the places that will actually sell and time it rather than store it.<br /> <br /> Not saying that this is easy or feasible today. But we must aim for that goal as at least the technology to pull it off already exists and has enough penetration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-30T06:38:38-07:00","id":1561132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561130#post1561130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You mean the lore that they either disregarded from the previous editions, or retconned so heavily as to be almost unrecognizeable?<br /> <br /> Yeah, no, V5 is not my gothic horror vampire game!<br /> <br /> Blood Resonances were a stupid addition, because your discipline affinity is supposed to be linked to your clan, not the kind of people you eat. And predator types were also a bad move, because the Beast is a mindless animal that runs on pure instinct. It does not give a crap where and how you feed, so long as you continue to do so.</div> </div> </div> </div>I heavily disagree.<br /> <br /> Treating V5 as universally bad isn't any better than doing what they did at first. And there are definitely good ideas in there.<br /> <br /> Blood Resonance, by the way, is a decidedly good rule, if not ideal in execution. The notion has existed in the lore since the very beginning, with tropes of preference and dark research on the benefits of selective feeding.<br /> <br /> Discipline affinity is still from clan. The game was never about saying everything related to them must be from clan, though. I don't think it in any way detracts from the game by being tied to Disciplines.<br /> <br /> And even if you do, just move the benefits around. The important part isn't the Discipline link, it's adding selective feeding as a mechanic with enough weight for players to consider it.<br /> <br /> Predator types are a shorthand for the old Bonus Points system and honestly better than them, it isn't as if they impacted anything really important besides allocation of a few dots.<br /> <br /> Loresheets are another good idea, if in need of polishing. I don't think bloodlines should be there, but overall they're a very good way of presenting lore and making it relevant in game without the need to dive in deeper than you want or can, or messing much with actual plot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T14:08:14-07:00","id":1561169,"title":"","content":"I found blood resonance uneeded bloat.<br /> <br /> Predator types i could take or leave.<br /> <br /> Loresheets were neat however","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T14:30:16-07:00","id":1561170,"title":"","content":"As usual when it comes ot V5 mechanics... implementation is usually the far bigger problem than concept. Blood Resonance - as monteparnas keeps noting - has been a concept in VtM from the beginning... so finally putting some mechanics to it isn't a bad thing. But I'd agree they made it too complicated in base rules (what they went with could have been find as an expanded optional rule for groups that want finer mechanical details, but the core rule should have been simpler IMO). Predator types are fine conceptually... they're just a bundle of starting points based on your character's approach to things; however they are horribly balanced in terms of XP value and the Discipline assignments are fairly meh and prone to incentivizing mechanical favor over character. Loresheets skipped an important part of the game they were copied from: a bonus to your character's knowledge, exposure, or access of/to the topic so regardless of which specific perk you invest towards. Your Loresheet rating should replace or supplement relevant skill dots when dealing with your topic even when individual perks don't apply. What dot levels get you what was also not well curated in terms of a semblance of balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T14:37:19-07:00","id":1561171,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561169#post1561169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I found blood resonance uneeded bloat.<br /> <br /> Predator types i could take or leave.<br /> <br /> Loresheets were neat however</div> </div> </div> </div>Seen arguments claiming that one's choice of Predator Type is a way for them to exercise a bit more control over the Beast and retain their humanity.<br /> <br /> Don't know if they're aware of this, but humans aren't in the habit of eating each other. Regardless of how civilized they choose to go about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T14:50:28-07:00","id":1561173,"title":"","content":"Given some Predator types mean starting with reduced Humanity... not sure why people are saying that. V5 is pretty clear: predator type is just your character's preferred eating habits. Whatever else you want to attach to that for your character is up to you. &quot;Seen arguments claiming...&quot; is always an inferior source to the actual text. While some Predator Types are clearly geared towards vampires that want to try to maintain their Humanity as much as possible... that's all it is a hunting strategy that tries to be as ethical as possible regarding an inherently unethical activity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T16:49:29-07:00","id":1561177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561170#post1561170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As usual when it comes ot V5 mechanics... implementation is usually the far bigger problem than concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's for sure.<br /> <br /> Resonance could have been more focused on how to hunt for them rather than randomizing people. And be more freeform on the benefits rather than lock so tightly to humour theory.<br /> <br /> I'd like a rule that gives me ideas on what I can get by looking for 'blood flavor' and then abstract the process of getting it if I want to.<br /> <br /> Predator Types have a roughly stable scheme: 1 choice of Discipline, 1 choice of Specialization, 1 dot of Advantage. The bigger problem is with the ones that mix Disadvantages to give bigger bonuses. In theory this is simple to correct by homebrew or free dot placement.<br /> <br /> Loresheets need an overhaul of the rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561171#post1561171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seen arguments claiming that one's choice of Predator Type is a way for them to exercise a bit more control over the Beast and retain their humanity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>How you interpret your Predator Type is up to you.<br /> <br /> What it really is is a package of starting dots and nothing else. Everything else that uses them are just ST helpers for feeding scenes where you follow a given Type. They don't even have to follow the one you chose, even if the assumption is that.<br /> <br /> How it reflects character ethics is up to the player. Humans don't <i>usually </i>eat each other, except when they do, but that has nothing to do with the human capacity to reflect upon the ethics of personal activities and needs and try to approach them in a less harmful way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T02:26:13-07:00","id":1561285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561177#post1561177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's for sure.<br /> <br /> Resonance could have been more focused on how to hunt for them rather than randomizing people. And be more freeform on the benefits rather than lock so tightly to humour theory.<br /> <br /> I'd like a rule that gives me ideas on what I can get by looking for 'blood flavor' and then abstract the process of getting it if I want to.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should be an optional rule in a sidebar somewhere. As it is, it's a rule that's both underdeveloped <i>and</i> clunky, so it fails on two counts. Dyscrasias are yet another thing layered on top that should probably die by fire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561177#post1561177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Predator Types have a roughly stable scheme: 1 choice of Discipline, 1 choice of Specialization, 1 dot of Advantage. The bigger problem is with the ones that mix Disadvantages to give bigger bonuses. In theory this is simple to correct by homebrew or free dot placement.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem is that they finely balanced XP with the available chargen picks, but then completely blew it all again with Predator Types. The first dot in a Discipline is obviously not worth the same as the third dot in a Discipline, so just saying &quot;add a dot of x&quot; is sloppy and undoes their own hard work.<br /> <br /> IMO, they should have gone with flat XP costs as a much saner option (perhaps with the fifth dot costing double, as in CofD), because then it doesn't matter. You can just let people allocate dots however they want. But even keeping the system they had, all they had to do was limit the bonus to the first dot in a choice of Disciplines. (This doesn't even have to be tied to Predator Type, though. You could just give people 2/1/1 dots to allocate at chargen, stipulating that the first three have to go into clan Disciplines.)<br /> <br /> Personally, I would also give an optional sidebar that just lets you spend the equivalent points however you want. Going from V1 to V20, where you're relatively free to assign points, to V5, where everything is allocated for you, just feels so antithetical to the simplicity and freedom of the original system. Giving people a choice for freeform chargen is much better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561177#post1561177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Loresheets need an overhaul of the rule.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I like them, but I like Heavy Arms' suggestion of them counting as &quot;lore&quot; skills as well. One thing I think we do need is to move away from the 1\u20135 dot progression and let them be whatever makes the most sense. It cuts out on the boring stuff added in just to get five distinct Advantages out of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561177#post1561177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How you interpret your Predator Type is up to you.<br /> <br /> What it really is is a package of starting dots and nothing else. Everything else that uses them are just ST helpers for feeding scenes where you follow a given Type. They don't even have to follow the one you chose, even if the assumption is that.<br /> <br /> How it reflects character ethics is up to the player. Humans don't <i>usually </i>eat each other, except when they do, but that has nothing to do with the human capacity to reflect upon the ethics of personal activities and needs and try to approach them in a less harmful way.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's perhaps useful the first time you make a character, but it never gets reinforced in play. Because you can't allocate the points where you want to, it just ends up being something you pick to get the traits you wanted all along. Which means a freeform approach would actually be better most of the time. To avoid the optimisation trap, you could just say, &quot;Now pick some traits based on how your character approaches feeding. Pick one Discipline you regularly use, one specialty that helps you...&quot; etc. Discuss it with your ST and you're golden.<br /> <br /> Ultimately, though, it's still a meaningless pick that doesn't really reflect how people tend to feed in play. They work best as optional templates to guide character builds. If you want Predator Type to have more fangs (pun intended) it should have more ongoing mechanical weight. E.g., you heal one level of Willpower damage when you feed according to type. Maybe even let it heal aggravated Willpower! That'll certainly make people use it. This makes it more like the old Archetypes and fixes a problem with aggravated Willpower damage to boot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T03:03:36-07:00","id":1561286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561285#post1561285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The problem is that they finely balanced XP with the available chargen picks, but then completely blew it all again with Predator Types. The first dot in a Discipline is obviously not worth the same as the third dot in a Discipline, so just saying &quot;add a dot of x&quot; is sloppy and undoes their own hard work.<br /> <br /> IMO, they should have gone with flat XP costs as a much saner option (perhaps with the fifth dot costing double, as in CofD), because then it doesn't matter. You can just let people allocate dots however they want. But even keeping the system they had, all they had to do was limit the bonus to the first dot in a choice of Disciplines. (This doesn't even have to be tied to Predator Type, though. You could just give people 2/1/1 dots to allocate at chargen, stipulating that the first three have to go into clan Disciplines.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Two of the Predator Types are also useless in the long term, as your appetite increases with your Blood Potency.<br /> <br /> Bagger and Farmer try to limit themselves to only feeding on blood bags and animals. But they will inevitably have to move on to live humans at some point.<br /> <br /> Then there's the Organovore, who has to consume the victim's flesh as well as their blood. Good luck not leaving a trail of missing persons with that kind of shit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T03:35:44-07:00","id":1561287,"title":"","content":"Just to be clear, I wasn't really making a suggestion as much as translating something that got lost when the V5 creators ported Loresheets from Weapons of the Gods to V5: that the individual perks you can buy from a Loresheet were coupled with extensive knowledge of the broader subject the perk is involved in. WotG was also far more narrative over mechanical for the perks which made the pricing of them easier: how big was the narrative impact going to be? Putting the minimum into, &quot;Former member of a criminal organization&quot; means you get a small perk that will help out in probably once every five or six game sessions. Putting in for a max perk makes that organization a major part of the story and whatever perk you have means they're going to be around - a lot - for possibly good and ill for the group.<br /> <br /> That said, it still had significant problems with balancing perks (even if you get away from a progression) simply because you were putting character resources to ensure narrative-significant results that might have been easier to achieve by just buying character traits instead. You could use a Loresheet to ensure your character finds their one true love... or just buy good social stats and romance a NPC your character develops rapport with.<br /> <br /> My actual suggestion for making Loresheets better would be to import the Lore rules from Exalted 3e, with Loresheets being areas you can introduce facts from, and investment in the loresheet increases how major the facts you can introduce are. This means instead of paying resources for good knowing of things and some perks that may or may not be worth it in the long run, you get something that you can always try to use with some creativity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T16:02:45-07:00","id":1561322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561285#post1561285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It should be an optional rule in a sidebar somewhere. As it is, it's a rule that's both underdeveloped <i>and</i> clunky, so it fails on two counts. Dyscrasias are yet another thing layered on top that should probably die by fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think Dyscrasias are a bad thing, I think the random frequency is badly done and the sample bonuses are badly designed.<br /> <br /> As it is now, Resonance and everything about it is a game of repeated dice throwing for the sake of it. It boggles down play and don't distinguish when it is needed and when it isn't.<br /> <br /> But I'd say it couldn't be a sidebar for another reason: it's a primary rule for Thin Blood Alchemy, and they were really into making this thing.<br /> <br /> Resonance is also a valuable information. Any way you find out about someone's Resonance, you just also found out an incomplete but broad information on their personality's makeup.<br /> <br /> Overall I think the rule as is could use tinkering, and should just be ignored sometimes, but is otherwise ok. A little cumbersome, but useful enough.<br /> <br /> For Predator Type I know exactly what you mean, but that has a simple solution: rather than a dot, it gives you a level 1 power. Comes with the dot if you don't have the Discipline, not if you don't.<br /> <br /> Still don't think the freeform building is necessary. Acceptable, sure, not necessary. And flat XP is the way to go, why they went back with growing costs is beyond me.<br /> <br /> Even as an experienced player I liked the Types in practice as a fast way to think about this in context with a good list of ideas. It's not a tool you need, but is one you'll find use for. And I don't think they should get any rules, just maybe Ambition/Desire get a better write up.<br /> <br /> My idea for loresheets is that they should be a list of 5 1-dot Advantages and the sum of what you bought is a score for lore rolls and some other things. I'm not sufficiently familiar with Exalted to know the rule cited by <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> <br /> <br /> Bagger, Farmer and Organovore aren't intrinsic bad options. They're legit strategies and there are Advantages/Flaws to follow them, putting them in the list is just staying in tune with the tool box. I'd say drinking from Vampires is way worse as a starting plan.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T19:47:32-07:00","id":1561330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561322#post1561322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bagger, Farmer and Organovore aren't intrinsic bad options. They're legit strategies and there are Advantages/Flaws to follow them, putting them in the list is just staying in tune with the tool box. I'd say drinking from Vampires is way worse as a starting plan.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's easier than you'd think. Since you can just lock a couple childer up in your basement / dungeon and avoid telling anybody about their existence.<br /> <br /> Pose as a Bagger in public, while secretly feeding those blood bags to your prisoners, before you siphon it back out of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T20:20:24-07:00","id":1561333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561330#post1561330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's easier than you'd think. Since you can just lock a couple childer up in your basement / dungeon and avoid telling anybody about their existence.<br /> <br /> Pose as a Bagger in public, while secretly feeding those blood bags to your prisoners, before you siphon it back out of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's definitely harder than I think. There are plenty of easier ways to do it.<br /> <br /> Also that demands an extremely narrow character concept even after we get rid of problems like Humanity and Blood Bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T21:18:16-07:00","id":1561335,"title":"","content":"That sounds like way to much hard work DarkKing when it comes to hunting and feeding.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T21:22:20-07:00","id":1561336,"title":"","content":"I personally like the lore sheets myself as it adds more options to character creation and gives more satisfying game play.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T22:24:46-07:00","id":1561339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561335#post1561335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like way to much hard work DarkKing when it comes to hunting and feeding.</div> </div> </div> </div>How? Unless you're a worthless, piece of shit Thinblood, you can embrace literally any human you can get your hands on. There's no criteria involved, just grab the first victim who comes within arm's reach.<br /> <br /> Then it's a simple matter of plunging a wooden stake into their chest and pouring a couple blood bags into their mouth every few days.<br /> <br /> I fail to see the complications here?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T07:54:42-07:00","id":1561344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561322#post1561322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think Dyscrasias are a bad thing, I think the random frequency is badly done and the sample bonuses are badly designed.<br /> <br /> As it is now, Resonance and everything about it is a game of repeated dice throwing for the sake of it. It boggles down play and don't distinguish when it is needed and when it isn't.<br /> <br /> But I'd say it couldn't be a sidebar for another reason: it's a primary rule for Thin Blood Alchemy, and they were really into making this thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thin Blood Alchemy is pretty niche, though. You can always have TBA function off a Blood Resonance-like system without making it a core mechanic for everyone else as well. The sidebar can be an option to use Blood Resonance for everyone, instead of only using it for TBA.<br /> <br /> But most of this stuff doesn't really need hard and fast rules. &quot;Eat some type-A personalities hopped up on coffee and it might give you a Celerity bonus&quot; is probably enough for me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561322#post1561322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resonance is also a valuable information. Any way you find out about someone's Resonance, you just also found out an incomplete but broad information on their personality's makeup.<br /> <br /> Overall I think the rule as is could use tinkering, and should just be ignored sometimes, but is otherwise ok. A little cumbersome, but useful enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like the definition of an optional rule to me. Something that's &quot;should just be ignored sometimes, but is otherwise ok&quot; doesn't strike me as an essential rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561322#post1561322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Predator Type I know exactly what you mean, but that has a simple solution: rather than a dot, it gives you a level 1 power. Comes with the dot if you don't have the Discipline, not if you don't.<br /> <br /> Still don't think the freeform building is necessary. Acceptable, sure, not necessary. And flat XP is the way to go, why they went back with growing costs is beyond me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it just gives a level one power, you first need to fix the (IMO stupid) limitation on one power per dot. As for freeform building, it's only as necessary as Blood Resonance. I.e., they are both fine as optional rules. But most rules are fine when they're only optional.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T00:43:34-07:00","id":1561374,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561339#post1561339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How? Unless you're a worthless, piece of shit Thinblood, you can embrace literally any human you can get your hands on. There's no criteria involved, just grab the first victim who comes within arm's reach.<br /> <br /> Then it's a simple matter of plunging a wooden stake into their chest and pouring a couple blood bags into their mouth every few days.<br /> <br /> I fail to see the complications here?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The new Vampire is instantly in Frenzy, you have no guarantee of managing to stake them.<br /> <br /> 2. Staking someone is hard to begin with. The rules state 5 extra successes in the attack just because they're generous, but even working with it you're trying to stake a frenzied vampire.<br /> <br /> 3. That's kidnapping, which is way harder to do than say. Doable, sure, not necessarily hard, but not such an automatic success. Especially if you have no criteria.<br /> <br /> 4. It's up in the air if the staked vampire can process blood. The ST would be completely justified in saying you have to unstake them.<br /> <br /> 5. You'd be Blood Bonded in no time, and under the Bond you'd find it extremely hard to keep this arrangement indefinitely.<br /> <br /> 6. That would easy cause you problems with Humanity regularly, and I mean at leas once a week. Unless the ST handwave the persistent situation as encompassed by the first rolls/stains, you'd see your Humanity plummeting.<br /> <br /> 7. After all that, pay special attention to this: you have to get them blood through another method. You solved exactly nothing, because you have to hunt for blood for your hunt.<br /> <br /> You just got another hunting style and added a lot of convoluted steps to feed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561344#post1561344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for freeform building, it's only as necessary as Blood Resonance. I.e., they are both fine as optional rules. But most rules are fine when they're only optional.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is a fair comparison and I wouldn't say ignoring sometimes is the same as being an optional rule. Optional rules are alternatives to how the system works, a rule that doesn't need to be enforced every time is context dependant.<br /> <br /> On the other side, freeform with scaling costs would generally cause problems, and in my experience for no meaningful gain. Freeform is the source of a lot of decision paralysis in my group, and until now I've seen no character concept that couldn't be built in it as is.<br /> <br /> With flat XP, which should have been standard, then freeform would have more benefits.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T03:11:35-07:00","id":1561378,"title":"","content":"Thanks for explaining way better than I ci.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T05:13:41-07:00","id":1561379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561374#post1561374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5. You'd be Blood Bonded in no time, and under the Bond you'd find it extremely hard to keep this arrangement indefinitely.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, right, I completely forgot about that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561374#post1561374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">6. That would easy cause you problems with Humanity regularly, and I mean at leas once a week. Unless the ST handwave the persistent situation as encompassed by the first rolls/stains, you'd see your Humanity plummeting.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>&quot;Vampires aren't people, so it's okay to imprison, torture, experiment on, and kill them.&quot;</i> - Hue Mann, probably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T11:47:07-07:00","id":1561393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561374#post1561374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this is a fair comparison and I wouldn't say ignoring sometimes is the same as being an optional rule. Optional rules are alternatives to how the system works, a rule that doesn't need to be enforced every time is context dependant.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a rule can be safely ignored most of the time, it's not really necessary. That's not the same as saying that if the circumstances the rule comes up are rare, then it should be optional.<br /> <br /> E.g., Humanity rolls don't occur every session (or don't have to), but they're still a core rule. If you can handwave Humanity rules because you don't feel like engaging with the system any more, then it's an optional system.<br /> <br /> I think Blood Resonance is more akin to the latter than the former.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561374#post1561374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other side, freeform with scaling costs would generally cause problems, and in my experience for no meaningful gain. Freeform is the source of a lot of decision paralysis in my group, and until now I've seen no character concept that couldn't be built in it as is.<br /> <br /> With flat XP, which should have been standard, then freeform would have more benefits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I think we're in agreement. That's why I suggested flat XP costs, too.<br /> <br /> Freeform with scaling costs is a mess. But also, the system with scaling costs is already a mess because of Predator Types\u2014RAW, they ignore the scaling costs. They can be fixed, as we've discussed, but it's just easier to use flat XP because then the base system can be used with greater flexibility.*<br /> <br /> Personally, I use the old Freebie Points costs, with a few tweaks: Clan Disciplines cost 5 per dot, others cost 7 per dot, secondary blood magic paths cost 4 per dot, Merits cost their rating, and alternate/combo-powers (I just call them Devotions) cost the same as in VTR2e: [sum of all dots/2], rounded down (min. 1). Dots 5+ cost twice as much. Most traits can only be increased once per story except with ST permission.<br /> <br /> &quot;XP&quot; gain is 1\u20133 points per session. If you want to make XP awards more granular (e.g., 1\u20135 per session), you can just double the XP cost relative to the freebie cost. So Attributes are 10 points per dot, Disciplines are 10/14, etc. So long as you keep the conversion strictly equal at all times (i.e., 1 freebie = 2 XP or whatever), it works fine. The problem comes in when 1 freebie equals a variable amount of XP.<br /> <br /> *I quite liked the option in the <i>Guide to the Camarilla</i> to build your character with 184 freebie points back in the day. Not for every character, and definitely not for new players, but if you want to make a niche concept. You just have to put limits in certain areas (the main two are: no more than 100 points in Attributes or 35 points in Disciplines).<br /> <br /> With these caps, characters have flexibility to invest in fewer Attributes and Disciplines to bump up their Abilities, or to go all in on Backgrounds, etc., but they can't go over the top on Attributes and powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":5291,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","user":"adambeyoncelowe","date":".  Typo, spacing 07-06-2026, 02:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T12:01:56-07:00","id":1561396,"title":"","content":"You also forgot that a newly embraced kindred is the throes of frenzy until they feed and kill which mortal is infront of them. There's a reason why sires keep a distance in the early minutes of a freshly embraced neonate as they don't want to get needless injuries and have to use more blood to fuel the healing and restrain a frenzied kindred.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T12:54:35-07:00","id":1561397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561396#post1561396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You also forgot that a newly embraced kindred is the throes of frenzy until they feed and kill which mortal is infront of them. There's a reason why sires keep a distance in the early minutes of a freshly embraced neonate as they don't want to get needless injuries and have to use more blood to fuel the healing and restrain a frenzied kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like plunging a stake into them the moment they start twitching might remedy that problem.<br /> <br /> Unless they just fly off the table in an explosive lunge?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T14:55:22-07:00","id":1561399,"title":"","content":"Easier said than done DarkKing as the heart is well protected by the rib cage and newly embraced neonates moving at incredible speed isn't uncommon as a freshly embraced Augustus Giovanni proved it in Clan Book Cappadocian when they mentioned the inclusion of his family.<br /> <br /> Battles are not won in seconds, and the odds of of a sire being able to put a frenzied newly embraced kindred are not very good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T22:06:28-07:00","id":1561409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561379#post1561379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>&quot;Vampires aren't people, so it's okay to imprison, torture, experiment on, and kill them.&quot;</i> - Hue Mann, probably.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but not how the books have depicted it and your ST's call anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561397#post1561397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I feel like plunging a stake into them the moment they start twitching might remedy that problem.<br /> <br /> Unless they just fly off the table in an explosive lunge?</div> </div> </div> </div>Explosive lunge is definitely on the table, yes.<br /> <br /> More importantly, to stake:<br /> <br /> By the rules you have to win the contested roll against their attack with 5 extra successes, if we assume V5 rules. Previous rules you have also to win initiative, and still get 5 successes.<br /> <br /> Not reliable on an initial character, and requires a particular build to even try. Not easy by any means.<br /> <br /> In a serious note, this Type was probably thought for a character that trades on blood or something rather than hunting, but is still full of problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T08:00:39-07:00","id":1561467,"title":"","content":"As the Embrace involves feeding vitae to a warm corpse, and the process itself is a bit vague, it depends on how long the conversion takes and whether you're instantly awake once it does, or whether it's more gradual. Could you stake someone in the moment between the Embrace working and then regaining consciousness? Possibly. But it probably requires a lot of trial and error, which is fairly difficult given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> Mind you, you could cut off the person's arms and legs, and pull out their teeth, and <i>then</i> Embrace them. But that's not so good on the old Morality front...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T11:26:42-07:00","id":1561475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561467#post1561467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you stake someone in the moment between the Embrace working and then regaining consciousness? Possibly. But it probably requires a lot of trial and error, which is fairly difficult given the circumstances..</div> </div> </div> </div>That gave me a funny mental image of a vampire just repeatedly stabbing someone in the chest with a stake, trying to find the heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T13:58:52-07:00","id":1561479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561467#post1561467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the Embrace involves feeding vitae to a warm corpse, and the process itself is a bit vague, it depends on how long the conversion takes and whether you're instantly awake once it does, or whether it's more gradual. Could you stake someone in the moment between the Embrace working and then regaining consciousness? Possibly. But it probably requires a lot of trial and error, which is fairly difficult given the circumstances.<br /> <br /> Mind you, you could cut off the person's arms and legs, and pull out their teeth, and <i>then</i> Embrace them. But that's not so good on the old Morality front...</div> </div> </div> </div>Just my headcanon, but I'd be inclined to make it like Claudia's rebirth in Interview, where it takes about 15 seconds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T14:35:37-07:00","id":1561481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561479#post1561479\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just my headcanon, but I'd be inclined to make it like Claudia's rebirth in Interview, where it takes about 15 seconds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Same. Only Thin Bloods seem to take a long time. The rest seem to happen pretty quickly. So that's long enough if you know exactly where to stab and how hard to do it. But as RuPaul says, &quot;And don't fuck it up.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T19:34:14-07:00","id":1561498,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561481#post1561481\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Same. Only Thin Bloods seem to take a long time. The rest seem to happen pretty quickly. So that's long enough if you know exactly where to stab and how hard to do it. But as RuPaul says, &quot;And don't fuck it up.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>From a RL perspective, wouldn't be enough time for a Vampire without Potence. Even a very strong man needs a hammer and time to break through the ribcage with a wooden stake. 15 seconds I'd say either isn't enough time, or would be even harder for being rushed.<br /> <br /> And the question remains: does the stake interfere with the Embrace? At which point in this process is it really safe to pierce the heart?<br /> <br /> In game terms it's still an attack demanding 5 extra successes. And if you're using the Advanced combat rules it's actually 7 or more, depending on how the ST defines the targeted hit.<br /> <br /> This is a tall order for a starting character, much less to a starting character that isn't built specifically for this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T20:23:13-07:00","id":1561500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561498#post1561498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From a RL perspective, wouldn't be enough time for a Vampire without Potence. Even a very strong man needs a hammer and time to break through the ribcage with a wooden stake. 15 seconds I'd say either isn't enough time, or would be even harder for being rushed.<br /> <br /> And the question remains: does the stake interfere with the Embrace? At which point in this process is it really safe to pierce the heart?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, I figured it out!<br /> <br /> Just use the automatic stake jacket from True Blood!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T00:27:44-07:00","id":1561507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561498#post1561498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From a RL perspective, wouldn't be enough time for a Vampire without Potence. Even a very strong man needs a hammer and time to break through the ribcage with a wooden stake. 15 seconds I'd say either isn't enough time, or would be even harder for being rushed.<br /> <br /> And the question remains: does the stake interfere with the Embrace? At which point in this process is it really safe to pierce the heart?<br /> <br /> In game terms it's still an attack demanding 5 extra successes. And if you're using the Advanced combat rules it's actually 7 or more, depending on how the ST defines the targeted hit.<br /> <br /> This is a tall order for a starting character, much less to a starting character that isn't built specifically for this.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's Celerity, too. 15 seconds = up to 5 rounds of combat, so it's possible even without it, since your target isn't resisting for the most part. But the reason I said you'd have to time it for the point after the Embrace has taken hold but before they wake up is precisely so it doesn't interfere with the Embrace.<br /> <br /> It's all hypotheticals at this stage, in any case, since there's no official ruling either way. But the point still stands that this is no way to (un)live. Who would want to entrust their survival to a process that's so easily derailed, even if you could do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T07:56:39-07:00","id":1561519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561507#post1561507\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But the point still stands that this is no way to (un)live. Who would want to entrust their survival to a process that's so easily derailed, even if you could do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>As main strategy for a Predator Type is just ludicrous, but as a long term strategy it has a point.<br /> <br /> You can have an old enough vampire that think of this as an insurance, especially if they're old enough to require Vampire blood. If it isn't your current main method, it's doable with prepare.<br /> <br /> But is still quite problematic. For starters you'd probably have to be under old Humanity rules to stay afloat, since you need a Hierarchy that'll eventually let you proceed without further loss.<br /> <br /> And all the problems would remain, just you'd be expecting them. That must include finding out lots of answers that may complicate things and preparing for escapes, no matter how you thoroughly removed risks","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T16:37:11-07:00","id":1561539,"title":"","content":"1. Take human.<br /> 2. Chain/bind/incarcerate human so that they can't move.<br /> 3. Feed on human till they nearly die.<br /> 4. Feed human blood so they turn.<br /> <br /> Waw. Vampire trapped for staking.<br /> <br /> Bonus tip: Condition human and newly formed fledgling with Dominate and Presence until they have 0 Willpower to resist you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T17:37:36-07:00","id":1561541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561539#post1561539\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Take human.<br /> 2. Chain/bind/incarcerate human so that they can't move.<br /> 3. Feed on human till they nearly die.<br /> 4. Feed human blood so they turn.<br /> <br /> Waw. Vampire trapped for staking.<br /> <br /> Bonus tip: Condition human and newly formed fledgling with Dominate and Presence until they have 0 Willpower to resist you.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Fledgling can still burn Blood to get to Strength 6 through the scene.<br /> <br /> No bonus, either: the exercise assume generic vampire, you can't rely on any particular build.<br /> <br /> We all know how to do this if you build a char to do this, even more if you research a target that's suitable.<br /> <br /> But the proposal is an easy strategy to make Blood Leech a feasible general use Predator Type. If it requires any particular trait, then it is not easy or feasible as general strategy.<br /> <br /> So I'd say that this must be viable with at most 2 in any relevant Attribute, 1 in Skill, no defined Clan or Discipline, maybe 2 dots in Merits, but no more than that. I'd extend those by 1 for the traits reinforced by Blood Leech: 3 in Strength or Dexterity, 2 in Brawl or Stealth, any common effect of Blood Potency 2. You also suffer the penalty of Prey Exclusion.<br /> <br /> My Reasoning: if you need anything beyond that, the strategy is not versatile enough to make this a viable Predator Type to as many characters as any other Type let you do. You can't even rely on the traits of it open to choice, because the choice must remain open.<br /> <br /> Overall I keep my original statement: Blood Leech is the worse Predator Type, because it really requires you to feed on Vampires and this is not as simple for a starting character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T17:42:58-07:00","id":1561542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561541#post1561541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A Fledgling can still burn Blood to get to Strength 6 through the scene.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strength 6 is not breaking out of a heavy set of iron / steel chains.<br /> <br /> If keeping a vampire restrained or locked up is so difficult, then how have the Second Inquisition managed to pull it off?<br /> <br /> Because I'm pretty sure the facility shown in Swansong had a whole damn prison wing full of starving vampires, who weren't even chained up!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T19:02:36-07:00","id":1561544,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be shocked if the Second Inquisition had other methods of keeping Kindred restrained. Perhaps items overflowing with true faith and arcane methods that didn't violate there belief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T19:11:50-07:00","id":1561547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561542#post1561542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength 6 is not breaking out of a heavy set of iron / steel chains.<br /> <br /> If keeping a vampire restrained or locked up is so difficult, then how have the Second Inquisition managed to pull it off?<br /> <br /> Because I'm pretty sure the facility shown in Swansong had a whole damn prison wing full of starving vampires, who weren't even chained up!</div> </div> </div> </div>By the book Strength 5 in V5: Break open a metal door or tear open a chain-link fence. (Deadlift 250kg in V5, 300Kg in V20). This is without a roll.<br /> <br /> You can roll to increase this for one feat, but is not necessary: Strength 6 is definitely enough to break chains if we keep the progression (it is enough to switch from throwing daggers to throwing motorcycles).<br /> <br /> Well, maybe not if they're well tied, but our char has to do with 3 dice tops, so I wouldn't expect the best technique. And yes, it is technique, the difficulty depends a lot on knowing how to distribute compression and avoid that it overpower the weakest spot.<br /> <br /> On the rest, read what I actually said. If you think the Second Inquisition is made up of untrained civilians that only work alone, that's a you problem.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T20:51:06-07:00","id":1561550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561547#post1561547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strength 6 is definitely enough to break chains if we keep the progression (it is enough to switch from throwing daggers to throwing motorcycles).</div> </div> </div> </div>How the fuck?<br /> <br /> I thought 5 dots was supposed to be the peak of normal human capabilities?<br /> <br /> You're telling me that just 1 dot above that is enough to make you Hulk out?<br /> <br /> Suddenly, those stories about methuselahs racing around the planet at super sonic speeds, generating shockwaves with their punches makes a lot more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T21:43:14-07:00","id":1561552,"title":"","content":"Under the old system Kindred who were 7th generation or lower could have 6+ dots in physical, mental and social attributes as well as Disciplines DarkKing.<br /> <br /> It could make for uneven game play if you were playing as a 9th or 10th generation kindred and you had a 6th generation elder coming after you. By raw power alone you couldn't compete.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T22:44:55-07:00","id":1561553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561550#post1561550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How the fuck?<br /> <br /> I thought 5 dots was supposed to be the peak of normal human capabilities?<br /> <br /> You're telling me that just 1 dot above that is enough to make you Hulk out?<br /> <br /> Suddenly, those stories about methuselahs racing around the planet at super sonic speeds, generating shockwaves with their punches makes a lot more sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>V5 Blood Surge is a flat bonus, even then +2 can get you far. But previous editions it was a direct physical attribute increase for the rest of the scene.<br /> <br /> Your limit with this is Generation cap +1, so any Kindred could reach Strength 6 for a whole scene given a few turns. You can go up to 10 for a single action, so breaking chains is well within what a Child of the Night can do.<br /> <br /> This is before a Willpower roll for the Feat of Strength. This roll was hard Diff 9, which for V5 would be kind of a 5 or 6, but the margin count as extra Strength dots for that action.<br /> <br /> So let's say you capture a random human with Str 2 and Willpower 4: in the 3rd turn they would have Strength 5 and a single success in Willpower (4 dice, one of them has to be 9+) is already enough to break the chains. If they get no success, next turn they have Strength 6 and just break them.<br /> <br /> They can make such rolls every turn while still buffing up, so a lucky Willpower roll will get them freedom earlier. And as Lysander said, with 7th Gen or less they'd have an even higher cap. A 5th Gen Methuselah could have natural attributes as high as 8, and buff up to 9.<br /> <br /> We still didn't reach the part where Disciplines were overall double the power. For most of them, the two V5 core powers were together the effect of that level, sometimes stronger.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T22:55:00-07:00","id":1561554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561552#post1561552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could make for uneven game play if you were playing as a 9th or 10th generation kindred and you had a 6th generation elder coming after you. By raw power alone you couldn't compete.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was greatly exaggerated.<br /> <br /> Everyone starts with the same points distribution and a veto on traits above 5. The low Gen still had to buy every dot.<br /> <br /> And Above Human traits had double the cost on top of the usual multiplier, so the 6th dot of an Attribute would cost 60 XP alone.<br /> <br /> If the only difference is Generation and they're close to initial character, the low Gen char would have only a marginal advantage. Greater Blood Pool and greater Blood/Turn are nice, but the logistics of getting the Blood for a Neonate would effectively limit that. It simply isn't wise for a new vamp to be killing 3, 4 mortals every night through exanguination, that would call bad attention and get them killed to stop being dumb.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T02:23:04-07:00","id":1561562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561552#post1561552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Under the old system Kindred who were 7th generation or lower could have 6+ dots in physical, mental and social attributes as well as Disciplines DarkKing.<br /> <br /> It could make for uneven game play if you were playing as a 9th or 10th generation kindred and you had a 6th generation elder coming after you. By raw power alone you couldn't compete.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, I'm aware. That's not what I was asking.<br /> <br /> I was surprised that we go from Olympic athlete, to hurling vehicles in the span of a single dot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T02:30:06-07:00","id":1561563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561553#post1561553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your limit with this is Generation cap +1, so any Kindred could reach Strength 6 for a whole scene given a few turns. You can go up to 10 for a single action, so breaking chains is well within what a Child of the Night can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you play a Nosferatu in Nightroad, you can lower yourself to 7th generation by diablerizing Reremouse and figuring out how to use the blood serum to enhance yourself.<br /> <br /> You have to be a Nosferatu specifically, because they're the only clan who starts as 9th generation, while everyone else starts as 11th.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T04:33:56-07:00","id":1561566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561562#post1561562\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, I'm aware. That's not what I was asking.<br /> <br /> I was surprised that we go from Olympic athlete, to hurling vehicles in the span of a single dot.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a motorcycle, but yeah.<br /> <br /> To be fair, the 300Kg of Strength 5 is already an average motorcycle, so you're going from dead lifting to throwing, it's not as big of a stretch as it seems.<br /> <br /> But is a stretch. The table is wonky and weird, it isn't consistent even in what the reference is. There are levels that only state dead lift, others go to breaking things only, and badly defined at that, the whole thing was eyeballed by people who weren't experts on nothing.<br /> <br /> Yet, in better systems it would still make sense because the growth is usually exponential, not arithmetic, what's called a logarithmic scale. So a common expression in many games is that each point doubles or quadruples the one before it.<br /> <br /> And again, how well you put the chains matter. A bad arrangement only requires you to break the lock, which would be the weakest spot, and Strength 5 already says you can break the lock of a metal gate.<br /> <br /> While I'm mostly liking the overall rules of V5, I must say I miss damage in 3 categories, with Lethal between Superficial and Aggravated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T07:29:38-07:00","id":1561569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561566#post1561566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a motorcycle, but yeah.<br /> <br /> To be fair, the 300Kg of Strength 5 is already an average motorcycle, so you're going from dead lifting to throwing, it's not as big of a stretch as it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't aware that motorcycles were so light (relatively speaking).<br /> <br /> That's only about 660 lbs. (I use freedom units of measurement).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561566#post1561566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I'm mostly liking the overall rules of V5, I must say I miss damage in 3 categories, with Lethal between Superficial and Aggravated.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the reason why Aggravated damage became rarer in 5th edition, is because the SI is supposed to be presented as intimidating.<br /> <br /> However, mortals only heal <b>1 point </b>of aggravated damage <b>per month</b> at their natural healing rate.<br /> <br /> That means it only takes 1 clean hit from an Aggravated damage source (such as Protean Claws), and that elite hunter will be out of commission for most of the year, as they take time to recover.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T11:48:16-07:00","id":1561573,"title":"","content":"The thing is, there really are three damage types in V5: normal damage that vampires half, supernatural but not aggravated damage they don't half, and then aggravated damage. VtM 1e had the same setup and they realized it was easier to move it to the classic B/L/A scheme that was introduced in WtA 1e and stayed the default until V5.<br /> <br /> WoD 2e and Rev definitely bloated sources of Agg out the whazoo, but that's fixed by cutting back on things that do Agg, not by recreating system clunk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T19:12:30-07:00","id":1561580,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561569#post1561569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wasn't aware that motorcycles were so light (relatively speaking).<br /> <br /> That's only about 660 lbs. (I use freedom units of measurement).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I think the reason why Aggravated damage became rarer in 5th edition, is because the SI is supposed to be presented as intimidating.<br /> <br /> However, mortals only heal <b>1 point </b>of aggravated damage <b>per month</b> at their natural healing rate.<br /> <br /> That means it only takes 1 clean hit from an Aggravated damage source (such as Protean Claws), and that elite hunter will be out of commission for most of the year, as they take time to recover.</div> </div> </div> </div>On motorcycles, yeah, I found out a few days ago. Lighter models are barely above 100Kg, I remember seeing a heavy one a little above 400Kg. So almost 900lb was the top of the heap, but as low as 250lb is feasible.<br /> <br /> Lethal wasn't a matter of making Agg rarer, the opposite, actually. With it you have a clearer distinction on what it takes to heal it - or kill you - without looking back on the source.<br /> <br /> Superficial is mostly the same as the old Bashing damage. Mortals take it from punches and Vampires from most things, and Vampires also halve it. Everyone heals it easy, in fact the Kindred healed at twice the rate they heal in V5, 2B per Blood Point, which is very close to a Rouse Check.<br /> <br /> Lethal was the damage of things that can &quot;kill&quot; you directly, but not take prohibitive amounts of time to do so. In current terms a mortal would be out of commission for days to weeks, and for Supernatural splats their healing methods were calibrated against Lethal. Mortals would die if full with Lethal, and most supernaturals would be OoC, though still alive, Kindred included.<br /> <br /> Aggravated was when things were dire. Only fire and arguably radiation were regular natural sources of Aggravated (you could also go for an exquisite wound like smashing bones, lots of healing time and likely crippling, without big danger to life). Otherwise Agg came with Supernatural sources, originally rare ones.<br /> <br /> IME CoD did it right: kept the three types but rebalanced Agg to be really rare. And I agree that Hunters in general should be dangerous among other things through the ability to bring a reliable source of Agg to the fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T20:12:36-07:00","id":1561582,"title":"","content":"Speaking of damage types. One thing I always thought was dumb, was the rules for heat. There's mention that high heat of 200+F having the same effect as fire. Water boils at around 212F. Sooo a pot of boiling water does Agg damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T21:39:07-07:00","id":1561584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561582#post1561582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of damage types. One thing I always thought was dumb, was the rules for heat. There's mention that high heat of 200+F having the same effect as fire. Water boils at around 212F. Sooo a pot of boiling water does Agg damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally houserule that heat causes no damage until it's enough to actually ignite your clothes. It's the fire itself what harms Vampires and not mere heat. Same with cold or radiation too. A mystical immortal corpse animated by one of the most powerful curses in existence is not easy to harm by things that merely kills due to metabolic constraints.<br /> <br /> Sometimes they just got carried by the idea of being &quot;realist&quot;, a common design theory at the time, or by fear of PCs being &quot;too overpower&quot;. That's ridiculous, they basically slowly backed in most human limitations a Magic Dead Body should bypass.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T21:45:03-07:00","id":1561585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561582#post1561582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of damage types. One thing I always thought was dumb, was the rules for heat. There's mention that high heat of 200+F having the same effect as fire. Water boils at around 212F. Sooo a pot of boiling water does Agg damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>By all means, dip your hand in one and see what happens!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T21:47:54-07:00","id":1561586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561584#post1561584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I personally houserule that heat causes no damage until it's enough to actually ignite your clothes. It's the fire itself what harms Vampires and not mere heat. Same with cold or radiation too. A mystical immortal corpse animated by one of the most powerful curses in existence is not easy to harm by things that merely kills due to metabolic constraints.<br /> <br /> Sometimes they just got carried by the idea of being &quot;realist&quot;, a common design theory at the time, or by fear of PCs being &quot;too overpower&quot;. That's ridiculous, they basically slowly backed in most human limitations a Magic Dead Body should bypass.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think radiation would be very effective against a vampire, due to their ability to reconstitute their bodies.<br /> <br /> Radiation is deadly because it causes the cells and DNA strands to break down and decay.<br /> <br /> But vampires are constantly regenerating back to the state they were in at the time of their embrace. So any damage the radiation causes will ultimately be reversed.<br /> <br /> Now, as for anybody who happens to be standing in close proximity to them... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-10T23:35:47-07:00","id":1561589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561585#post1561585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By all means, dip your hand in one and see what happens!</div> </div> </div> </div>They're not a Magical Dead Body.<br /> <br /> Vampires don't take damage from fire because it is hot, but because it is fire specifically. It is a sacred element, a ritual cleanser. It's not by the physics of fire that this damage comes, but the symbolism, the metaphysics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DarkKing</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561586#post1561586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Radiation is deadly because it causes the cells and DNA strands to break down and decay.<br /> <br /> Now, as for anybody who happens to be standing in close proximity to them... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not cells, only DNA.<br /> <br /> Radiation damage is too tiny and spread, very few cells get any meaningful damage even at very high doses.<br /> <br /> Otherwise we would see immediate damage in tissue hit when exposed to high doses, there's none. Instead we observe Radiation Sickness setting in with a significant delay. This is DNA damage.<br /> <br /> Burnings only happen when the radiation heats material or irradiate a lot of energy in specific wavelengths, which isn't that common.<br /> <br /> As for anyone near them... If at the moment, sure. Later, depends on the type of radiation, exposure and cleaning. &quot;Radiation infection&quot; is really just radioactive dust. Nothing becomes radioactive from exposure, but can be covered in radioactive particles.<br /> <br /> The Vampire just needs to clean themselves. It isn't terribly hard. Thorough, careful, but is easy enough to be standard procedure several times a day in facilities that deal with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T01:15:41-07:00","id":1561593,"title":"","content":"I always ignore heat, radiation, etc., for vamps. Ever since <i>Requiem</i> 2e, I've also lessened damage by having a flat rule: vamps downgrade all damage one step relative to humans. Only the three banes (sunlight, fire, and True Faith) cause aggravated damage. Other sources of aggravated get downgraded to lethal, lethal gets downgraded to (unhalved) bashing, and bashing is downgraded to half bashing. One blood point heals 1L or 2B. Ignore all other special rules.<br /> <br /> So, teeth and claws (including Protean 2: Feral Claws) do aggravated to mortals but lethal to vampires. This makes vamp-on-vamp (or vamp-on-lupe) combat less all-or-nothing, and Fortitude less obligatory. Swords and bullets do (unhalved) bashing damage. Fists and blunt instruments do (halved) bashing damage.<br /> <br /> Under this system, bullets work out a little bit more damaging upfront, but it's made up for with swords being less damaging and teeth and claws being much more tolerable. The 2B for one blood point rule also makes vamps very hardy. This removes the incentive for <i>Blade</i>-style trenchcoats and katanas\u2014American vamps can still use their WalMart assault rifles like normal (if bought before 2015), and everyone else can just fight like snarling beasts with their fangs.<br /> <br /> I've toyed with giving all vamps claws, since we use VTR2e Disciplines in most cases anyway (so Protean 2 is more diverse), but I ultimately ruled against it out of tradition. But it would be cool for making vamps feel more visceral.<br /> <br /> I also like vamps having Kindred Senses (&quot;Predator Senses&quot;, I call them, since Sabbat vamps wouldn't use &quot;Kindred&quot;), allowing them to see in low-light and easily detect blood nearby. I'm basically running <i>Requiem</i> at this point, but with a lower target number and <i>Masquerade</i> lore. <i>Requiem</i> just gets the <i>feel</i> of vampires better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-11T09:18:09-07:00","id":1561607,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560488-how-did-the-sabbat-exist?p=1561593#post1561593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm basically running <i>Requiem</i> at this point, but with a lower target number and <i>Masquerade</i> lore. <i>Requiem</i> just gets the <i>feel</i> of vampires better.</div> </div> </div> </div>It does. I'm having fun with V5, but Requiem did got it far better. I'm starting to read Curseborne to see how it goes, but for a WoD style Vampire I think Requiem is the way to go.<br /> <br /> And seriously, so many unique Disciplines would have been so better as Devotions...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}